// Generated by docs/manual/build_manual.py from the manual - do not edit.
export const HELP = {"en":[{"id":"s1","ch":"What the LWK Viewer is","h":"What the LWK Viewer is","lv":2,"html":"<p>The LWK Viewer shows a project's Revit sheets and 3D model in a web browser, so anyone on the team can review, measure, mark up and raise issues without Revit. It runs on desktop, iPad and iPhone, and every issue raised is shared live with the whole team and can be picked up back in Revit.</p><p>Around the drawings and the model it also holds the team's work: a list of projects, task lists (in place of Lark Tasks), whiteboards and a messenger, all linked to the same sheets, 3D views and issues, with one search across all of them.</p><p><b>Who it is for</b></p><table><tr><th>Who</th><th>Typical use</th></tr><tr><td>Architects and designers</td><td>Check drawings and the 3D model, raise design and coordination issues, answer issues assigned to them</td></tr><tr><td>Project leads and directors</td><td>Review progress on a tablet, follow open and overdue issues on the Dashboard</td></tr><tr><td>BIM coordinators</td><td>Publish models and sheets from Revit, run nightly exports, manage issues from inside Revit</td></tr><tr><td>Consultants and site staff (Viewer role)</td><td>Look and read only, on any device</td></tr><tr><td>Team leads</td><td>Plan the team's task lists, follow who does what by when, discuss in project channels</td></tr><tr><td>Project and site admins</td><td>Add people, set roles, manage projects</td></tr></table><p><b>What you can do</b></p><ul><li><b>Sheets (2D):</b> open every published sheet as a sharp PDF, search the words on all drawings, mark up with 20+ tools, compare with earlier versions, and export PDFs with markups.</li><li><b>3D:</b> orbit, pan and walk through the model and its links, cut floor plans and sections, measure with snapping, check element properties, and save views.</li><li><b>Issues:</b> raise an issue on a sheet or in 3D with a snapshot, assign it, set a due date, comment with @mentions, and track it to closure. Issues exchange with Revit, Navisworks and BIMcollab through BCF.</li><li><b>2D + 3D side by side:</b> click a plan on a sheet and the 3D view goes there; walk in 3D and see where you are on the plan.</li><li><b>Revit link:</b> the LWK Issues window in Revit lists the same issues, zooms to them and sends replies back.</li><li><b>Projects:</b> every job with its people, drawings, model, tasks, issues, files and chat on one page.</li><li><b>Tasks:</b> team task lists with List, Kanban, Gantt and Dashboard views, imported from Lark and linked to issues, sheets and 3D views.</li><li><b>Board:</b> a shared whiteboard per project for notes, mind maps and sketches.</li><li><b>Messenger:</b> project channels, group chats and direct messages, with task and issue updates posted in, links to tasks, issues, sheets and 3D, and messages to and from WhatsApp.</li><li><b>Issues and tasks together:</b> make a task from an issue; finishing one offers to close the other.</li><li><b>Revit elements:</b> a 3D issue keeps its Revit ElementId, ready for Select by ID, BCF and the LWK add-in.</li><li><b>Search:</b> one box (Ctrl+K) for tasks, issues, sheets, 3D views, messages and file links.</li><li><b>Offline:</b> download a project to a tablet and keep working on site with no signal.</li></ul>"},{"id":"s2","ch":"Before you start","h":"Before you start","lv":2,"html":"<p>You need an account, a supported browser and the viewer's web address; nothing is installed on your computer.</p><p><b>The pictures:</b> each page's chapter starts with a screenshot in which every panel, button and choice has a red number; the list under it says what each number does. Most come from a demo project and a few from a live one, so your names and drawings will differ. In Help, click a picture to see it full size.</p><p><b>Your account</b></p><ul><li>An admin creates your account and sends you an invitation with a <b>temporary password</b>.</li><li>Open the viewer address, sign in with your <b>Email</b> and the temporary password, then choose your own password (at least 8 characters) on the <b>My account</b> page that opens.</li><li>You stay signed in for 30 days on each browser. After 10 wrong passwords in 15 minutes the sign-in pauses for 15 minutes.</li><li>Your role is set per project: <b>Project admin</b>, <b>Publisher</b>, <b>Member</b> or <b>Viewer</b> (see For admins). Only a Publisher or project admin can publish from Revit. A Viewer sees a banner saying they can look and read but not change anything.</li></ul><p><b>Viewer address:</b> [paste the viewer address here before sending]</p><p><b>Browsers and devices</b></p><table><tr><th>Device</th><th>Browser</th><th>Notes</th></tr><tr><td>Windows or Mac</td><td>Chrome or Edge (recommended), Safari, Firefox</td><td>A mouse with a middle button (wheel) makes 3D much easier</td></tr><tr><td>iPad</td><td>Safari</td><td>Apple Pencil works for markup; landscape recommended</td></tr><tr><td>iPhone</td><td>Safari</td><td>Best for looking and reading; 3D loads a lighter copy of the model</td></tr></table><p><b>Confidentiality</b></p><ul><li>Treat the viewer like the project folder: only people on the project team should be added.</li><li>Do not share your password, forward invitation emails, or post links outside the team.</li><li>Screenshots and exported PDFs follow the same rules as any other project document.</li></ul>"},{"id":"s3","ch":"How it fits together","h":"How it fits together","lv":2,"html":"<p>A BIM coordinator publishes sheets and 3D from Revit; the team reviews in the browser; issues go back to the modeller inside Revit.</p><p>LWK Viewer workflow · publish, review, answer in Revit</p><ol><li><b>Publish.</b> In Revit, <b>Publish to Viewer</b> exports the chosen sheets as PDF and the model (with its links) in a fast 3D format, then uploads only the files that changed. It can repeat every night.</li><li><b>Prepare.</b> The server makes a lighter copy of each 3D model for phones and tablets, and reads the text on every sheet so it can be searched. This takes a few minutes after each upload.</li><li><b>Review.</b> The team opens Sheets, 3D or the Dashboard in any browser. Markups and issues save automatically and appear for everyone.</li><li><b>Answer.</b> The person assigned sees the issue in the viewer, and also in Revit through the <b>LWK Issues</b> window, which zooms to it and sends replies and status changes back.</li><li><b>Close.</b> The author or a project admin marks the issue Resolved and then Closed. The Dashboard tracks what is open, overdue and who holds it.</li></ol><p>Around this loop, the work itself is planned in <b>Tasks</b> (a task can be made from an issue and closes it when done), discussed in <b>Messenger</b> (each project has a channel where task and issue updates appear) and found again with <b>Search</b>. The <b>Projects</b> page ties each job together.</p>"},{"id":"s4","ch":"Quick start: your first ten minutes","h":"Quick start: your first ten minutes","lv":2,"html":"<figure class=\"shot\"><img src=\"help-img/header.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><ol><li>The project you are in - click to switch project (the same place on every page)</li><li>The pages: Projects, Dashboard, Sheets, 3D, Board, Tasks, Chat (number: unread), Calendar, Folders</li><li>Search everything (Ctrl+K)</li><li>Notifications</li><li>Help - this manual, searchable</li><li>Your profile: name, password, dark mode, sign out</li></ol></figure><p>Sign in, open a sheet, look at the same place in 3D, and raise one test issue.</p><ol><li><b>Sign in.</b> Open the viewer address, enter your email and password, and change the temporary password when asked.</li><li><b>Pick the project.</b> Use the project name at the top (a drop-down appears when you are on more than one project), or pick it on the <b>Dashboard</b>.</li><li><b>Open a sheet.</b> On <b>Sheets</b>, click a sheet in the left list, or type a room name, grid or note in <b>Search all sheets</b>. Scroll to zoom, hold the middle mouse button to pan, press <b>Fit</b> to see the whole sheet.</li><li><b>Go to 3D.</b> Click <b>3D</b> at the top left. Hold the right mouse button to orbit, the middle button to pan, and scroll to zoom. Double-click a surface to zoom in on it.</li><li><b>Look at a floor.</b> Choose a level in the <b>Floor plan</b> drop-down: the model is cut 1.2 m above that floor and seen from the top. <b>Page Up / Page Down</b> step between floors; <b>Whole building</b> goes back to 3D.</li><li><b>Click an element</b> to see its properties in the <b>Selection</b> panel on the right.</li><li><b>Raise a test issue.</b> Click <b>Add issue</b>, click a surface, type a title such as \"TEST - please ignore\", then <b>Save issue</b>. It appears in <b>Issues in 3D</b> for everyone.</li><li><b>Try 2D + 3D.</b> Back on Sheets, open a plan and press <b>2D + 3D</b>; click on the plan and the 3D view moves there.</li><li><b>Make a task from it.</b> Open the test issue, press <b>+ New task from this issue</b>, check the list, owner and due date, then <b>Make the task</b>.</li><li><b>Say hello in Chat.</b> Open <b>Chat</b>, pick the project's channel, type <b>#</b> and pick your test task, then press <b>Send</b>.</li><li><b>Search.</b> Press <b>Ctrl+K</b> (or the magnifier at the top) and type a word from your issue title: the issue, the task and your message are all found.</li><li><b>Delete your test issue and task</b> when you are done: the issue from its detail window (<b>Delete</b>), the task from its window (the bin button).</li></ol>"},{"id":"s5","ch":"Dashboard and projects","h":"Dashboard and projects","lv":2,"html":"<figure class=\"shot\"><img src=\"help-img/dashboard.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><ol><li>Filters as chips: resolved within, type, assigned to, discipline</li><li>Only mine</li><li>More filters: office, team, dismissed issues</li><li>Export: report, CSV, BCF, weekly summary</li><li>The project's tasks</li><li>Open, overdue, resolved in the period, average days to resolve</li><li>This week: raised, resolved, open, overdue</li><li>Raised and resolved by week</li><li>Open issues by person and discipline</li></ol></figure><p>The Dashboard is the project's issue scoreboard: how many are open, overdue, who holds them and what changed this week.</p><p><b>Getting around</b></p><ul><li>The header is the same on every page: the logo, then <b>the project you are in</b> (top left, its initials, name and code - click it to switch project), then the pages <b>Projects</b>, <b>Dashboard</b>, <b>Sheets</b>, <b>3D</b>, <b>Board</b>, <b>Tasks</b>, <b>Chat</b> (with the number of unread messages), <b>Calendar</b> and <b>Folders</b>. At the right: <b>Search</b> (Ctrl K), the bell, <b>Help</b> and <b>your profile button</b> (your initials, with a green dot when online). Click it for <b>Work offline ...</b>, <b>Admin</b> (admins only), <b>Account</b> (your password), <b>Theme</b> (Light, Dark, Auto) and <b>Sign out</b>. On a phone the pages scroll sideways.</li><li>The <b>project picker</b> lists the project names from the Projects page, e.g. \"SKW · HKA-P-01681-ARC\". A project made of several models, such as MOS Site 1 and Site 2, shows its parts under it. <b>All projects →</b> at the bottom opens the Projects page.</li><li><b>A whole project on one dashboard:</b> a project made of several models or sheet sets (e.g. TKO with its CAL and LAY files) opens on one dashboard of all its parts together: the counts and charts add them up, the <b>Part</b> filter and <b>Open issues by part</b> tell them apart, <b>Where</b> names the part (CAL · A102 ...), and <b>How this project is published</b> has a table per part. Under the title, <b>All parts</b> / <b>CAL</b> / <b>LAY</b> switch to one part and back. In the project picker on the Dashboard, the project's name opens all its parts, a part opens that part.</li><li><b>My dashboards - several projects together:</b> <b>+ Combine projects …</b> (under the title, or in the project picker) makes your own dashboard: give it a name and tick projects (all their parts, also ones added later) or single parts. It is kept for you and listed under <b>My dashboards</b> on any device; <b>Edit</b> and <b>Delete</b> are beside it when it is open. The printable report is per part: choose a part in the Part filter first (the spreadsheet takes them all, with a Part column).</li><li>The connection chip appears only when there is something to say: <b>N waiting to save</b> (the connection dropped; your changes are queued and sent when it returns), or <b>offline</b>. Do not reload the page while changes are waiting: the queue is kept only until you leave the page.</li></ul><p><b>What the Dashboard shows</b></p><table><tr><th>Part</th><th>What it tells you</th></tr><tr><td>Filters</td><td>One row of chips: <b>Resolved within</b> (Any time to Last 12 months), <b>Type</b>, <b>Assigned to</b>, <b>Discipline</b>, <b>Only mine</b>; <b>More filters</b> adds <b>Office</b>, <b>Team</b> and <b>Show dismissed issues</b></td></tr><tr><td>Key numbers</td><td><b>Open issues</b>, <b>Overdue</b> (with how late the oldest is), <b>Resolved</b> in the period (of how many raised) and <b>Average time to resolve</b>; under them In progress, Due in 7 days, Unassigned, Resolved awaiting sign-off and Closed (zeros dimmed)</td></tr><tr><td>This week</td><td>Issues raised, resolved, open and overdue this week, and open issues by person; <b>Send to Teams</b> posts it to the project channel</td></tr><tr><td>Charts</td><td>Raised and resolved by week (last 12 weeks), open issues by person and by discipline, by status, type, priority, where raised (sheet or 3D) and office</td></tr><tr><td>Responsibility table</td><td>Each assignee's open, in progress, overdue and due-soon counts, oldest open issue and last activity; click a row to filter</td></tr><tr><td>Lists</td><td><b>Overdue</b>, <b>Due in the next 14 days</b>, <b>Recently changed</b>, <b>Going quiet</b> (untouched for 14 days or more)</td></tr></table><ul><li><b>Export ▾</b> takes the issues the filters show: <b>Report</b> (a printable report with pictures - save it as PDF), <b>Spreadsheet (CSV)</b> for Excel, or <b>BCF</b> for Revit, Navisworks or Solibri.</li><li>The page refreshes itself every 2 minutes; <b>Updated ... ago</b> says how fresh it is. \"Resolved\" counts issues that became Resolved or Closed (Closed is a resolved issue the raiser has signed off).</li><li><b>Tasks of this project:</b> when the project is on the Projects page, the Dashboard also shows its tasks from every team's list: open, overdue and sub-tasks done.</li><li><b>Opens from your device:</b> what the Dashboard showed last time is kept on this device and shown at once; the server is then asked only for the issues changed since. If the server does not answer, the last copy stays on screen and the page says so.</li></ul><p><b>Notifications</b></p><ul><li><b>Email</b> (when the server's mail is set up): you are emailed when you are made owner of a task, when someone @mentions you in a task or a chat, and when a task you follow gets a comment or is completed; once a day you also get your tasks due tomorrow and overdue.</li><li><b>Teams:</b> if an admin has connected the project's Teams channel, it posts there when an issue is raised, assigned, changes status or due date, or gets a comment. @mentions in comments become Teams mentions.</li><li>A weekly summary can be posted to the same Teams channel (Monday by default). The same week's report is kept as a PDF in the project's Folders, under <b>00 BIM &gt; Weekly dashboard</b>, every week at that time (Teams or not); <b>Dashboard &gt; Export &gt; Weekly report to Folders</b> keeps one now.</li><li><b>Messenger:</b> the project's channel shows new tasks, assignments, completions and comments, and new or changed issues, as cards.</li></ul>"},{"id":"s6","ch":"Projects","h":"Projects","lv":2,"html":"<figure class=\"shot\"><img src=\"help-img/projects.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><ol><li>Search projects or people</li><li>Status: Active, On hold, Completed, Archived</li><li>Sort (or click a heading)</li><li>Manage projects (admins)</li><li>A project: click its name for its page</li><li>Open its Sheets, 3D, Chat, Dashboard, Folders</li></ol></figure><p><b>Order:</b> projects are listed by status - <b>Active</b> first, then <b>On hold</b>, <b>Completed</b> and <b>Archived</b> - and by name within each. The Projects page and the project picker in the header use this order. On the Projects page, click a column heading (Project, Status, Tasks, Completion, Overdue, Issues) or use <b>Sort</b> to order the list another way; click again to reverse it. Your choice is remembered.</p><p>The project picker at the top left of every page lists each <b>project</b> (name · code) with <b>its parts</b> under it (for example Site 1 / Site 2). On Sheets, <b>Set:</b> at the top of the sheet list chooses \"Revit sheets\" or an uploaded PDF set.</p><p>In a project's panel, <b>Project information</b> keeps the project no., client, address, building type, site area, GFA, storeys, stage, start and completion dates and a description (<b>Edit</b>, for the project's owners and admins). Click or drop a picture at the top of the panel to give the project a <b>picture</b>; it also shows in the list.</p><p>The <b>Projects</b> page lists the team's jobs, each with its people, drawings, model, tasks, issues, files and chat in one place. It is for reading; admins set projects up on <b>Admin &gt; Projects and members</b> (the <b>Manage</b> button takes you there).</p><p><b>The list</b></p><table><tr><th>Column</th><th>Shows</th></tr><tr><td>Project</td><td>Its short name and code, e.g. SKW · HKA-P-01681-ARC</td></tr><tr><td>Open</td><td><b>Sheets</b>, <b>3D</b> and <b>Dashboard</b> buttons. A project made of several models (MOS Site 1, Site 2) shows a small menu of its parts on each button</td></tr><tr><td>Tasks</td><td>Progress (done of all), overdue tasks and the open tasks, from every team's list that has a group for this project</td></tr><tr><td>Issues</td><td>A bar of the issues by status, with open / total; overdue in red. Added up over all the project's models</td></tr><tr><td>Folders</td><td>Its OneDrive, SharePoint or ACC folders</td></tr><tr><td>Chat</td><td>The project's channel in the Messenger, with unread messages</td></tr></table><ul><li>Search projects or people, and filter by status, at the top.</li><li>Click a row for the <b>details</b>: members by team, issues by status (click a figure to open the Dashboard), the tasks with their sub-tasks, and <b>Models and sheets</b>: each part with its own Sheets, 3D and Dashboard links.</li><li><b>One project, several models.</b> A job exported as several Revit models and sheet sets stays one project with several parts. Its members are everyone on any part, its issue counts add up all the parts, and the project picker shows it with its parts under it.</li></ul>"},{"id":"s7","ch":"Tasks","h":"Tasks","lv":2,"html":"<p><b>Tasks</b> are the team's task lists, in place of Lark Tasks, linked to the drawings, the model and the issues.</p><p>A list you opened before shows at once from this device, then only what changed since comes from the server. A long group shows its first 150 tasks; the next ones appear as you scroll down (or click <b>Show more</b>). Search and filters always look at every task.</p>"},{"id":"s8","ch":"Tasks","h":"Lists, groups and views","lv":3,"html":"<figure class=\"shot\"><img src=\"help-img/tasks.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><ol><li>Owned, Subscribed, Activities: your tasks</li><li>Quick access: all, created, assigned, completed</li><li>The task lists (+ makes one)</li><li>People: everyone's tasks</li><li>List, Kanban, Gantt, Dashboard, Activities</li><li>Members of the list</li><li>+ New task (▾: import)</li><li>Search tasks</li><li>Filter: status, owner, priority, sort, group by</li><li>Customize the columns</li><li>Click a heading to sort (▲ ▼)</li><li>A group (a project): fold it, open its sheets and dashboard</li><li>Tick to complete</li><li>The title - click to open the task</li><li>Edit any cell where it stands</li></ol></figure><ul><li><b>Task lists</b> belong to a team (for example LWK-MANILA). Inside a list the <b>groups</b> are usually the jobs (SKW, Kai Tak 2A3 ...). A group linked to a project shows <b>Project</b>, <b>Sheets</b> and <b>Dashboard</b> buttons; link them in <b>...</b> &gt; <b>Groups and projects</b>.</li><li><b>Quick access</b> on the left: <b>Owned</b> (open tasks that are yours), <b>Subscribed</b>, <b>All</b>, <b>Created</b>, <b>Assigned</b> (by you to others) and <b>Completed</b>, across every list you can see. <b>People</b> shows the organisation by team, office or company, with each person's open and overdue tasks.</li><li><b>List:</b> a grouped table. Edit in place, open sub-tasks with ▸, drag rows to reorder or move them to another group. A task with linked issues shows <b>#2 open</b> until they are all resolved, then <b>#✓</b>.</li><li><b>Sort by a heading:</b> click any column heading (Task title, Priority, Owner, Start, Due ...) - ▲ ascending, again ▼ descending, again the list's own order; empty cells go last, sub-tasks are sorted too, and your choice is remembered. Drag the edge of the side bar or of the task panel to make it wider or narrower (double-click the edge: usual width); the task panel's buttons (Delete among them) always stay in view.</li><li><b>Kanban:</b> cards in columns; drag a card to another column. The board fills the window, so the sideways scroll bar is always at the bottom of the screen; <b>Shift + mouse wheel</b>, dragging an empty part of the board, or the <b>‹ ›</b> buttons at its edges also scroll it.</li><li><b>Gantt:</b> bars on a timeline; drag a bar, or drag its ends to change the dates. Each change asks <b>Change the dates?</b> first: <b>Save</b> keeps it, <b>Cancel</b> puts the bar back (tick <b>Don't ask again today</b> to skip the question on this device). The legend explains the colours; milestones are gold.</li><li><b>Dashboard:</b> total, completed, incomplete and overdue, by owner, by project, average duration and due soon. <b>Activities:</b> everything that changed, by whom.</li><li><b>Filter ▾</b> (beside the search) holds which tasks (all, not done, done, overdue, mine), owner and priority, and the order (<b>Sort</b>, <b>Group by</b>); it says how many filters are set (\"Filter · 2\"), and <b>Clear filters</b> resets them. <b>Customize</b> which columns show. Lists can have their own columns (person, select, text, date, number), for example Modelers and Project Manager.</li></ul><figure class=\"shot\"><img src=\"help-img/tasks-kanban.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><ol><li>Kanban: the tasks as cards, a column per group</li><li>A group, with its Sheets and Dashboard</li><li>A card: tick, dates, owner, sub-tasks, issues, comments, priority - click to open; drag to another column</li><li>+ New task in this column</li></ol></figure><figure class=\"shot\"><img src=\"help-img/tasks-gantt.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><ol><li>Gantt: the tasks on a timeline</li><li>Zoom: Day, Week, Month</li><li>Today: back to today</li><li>What the bars and marks mean</li><li>A task, its owner - click to open</li><li>A bar: drag it to move the dates, drag an end to change one</li><li>Today</li></ol></figure><figure class=\"shot\"><img src=\"help-img/tasks-dashboard.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><ol><li>Dashboard: the list in numbers</li><li>Group and period; count sub-tasks or not</li><li>Total, completed, incomplete, overdue</li><li>By completion status</li><li>By overdue status</li><li>By assignee - click a name for their tasks</li><li>Average time from start to completion</li><li>Completed per week</li></ol></figure>"},{"id":"s9","ch":"Tasks","h":"A task","lv":3,"html":"<figure class=\"shot\"><img src=\"help-img/task-detail.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><ol><li>Mark complete</li><li>Previous / next task (K / J)</li><li>Follow: e-mails when it changes</li><li>Share to a chat</li><li>Copy a link to the task</li><li>Delete (Ctrl+Z brings it back)</li><li>The title</li><li>Owners, dates, group, priority and the list's own fields</li><li>Description</li><li>Sub-tasks</li><li>Linked issues, sheets, 3D views and files</li></ol></figure><ul><li><b>Owners</b> (and the list's person columns) list the <b>task list's members</b>; <b>Show everyone</b> at the bottom of the list adds anyone else. Add people to the list with <b>Members</b> (top right).</li><li>Click a task to open its window: title, <b>Owners</b>, start and due <b>Dates</b>, <b>Group</b>, <b>Priority</b> and the list's own columns. <b>Mark complete</b> finishes it.</li><li><b>Completion method:</b> <b>OR</b> = done when any owner completes it; <b>AND</b> = every owner completes their own part.</li><li><b>Sub-tasks:</b> type in <b>+ Add sub-task</b> and press Enter. A sub-task can have sub-tasks of its own, as in Lark, up to 5 levels: open the sub-task and add them there, or use the <b>+</b> that shows on a row in the List. Drop a task on the right half of another task's title to make it its sub-task. Deleting a task deletes everything under it (<b>Ctrl+Z</b> brings it all back). <b>Copy and paste tasks:</b> Ctrl-click rows to choose several (Shift-click: a range), then <b>Ctrl+C</b> or right-click &gt; <b>Copy</b> (or the copy button in a task's panel). Right-click another task &gt; <b>Paste as sub-tasks of ...</b> or <b>Paste below ...</b>, or right-click a group's heading &gt; <b>Paste into ...</b> (<b>Ctrl+V</b> pastes under the one task chosen). Each copy brings its sub-tasks, title, description, owners, dates, priority, fields and links, and starts fresh: not done, no percent, no comments. It pastes into another list too; one <b>Ctrl+Z</b> takes the whole paste back.</li><li><b>Arranging sub-tasks by dragging:</b> in the List, drag a sub-task above another sub-task to put it there - in the same task (a new order) or under another task. Drop it on a task's <b>+ Add sub-task</b> line to make it that task's last sub-task; drop it above a top-level row (or on the group) to make it a task of its own. In a task's panel, drag the sub-tasks (⋮⋮) into another order. A task cannot go under its own sub-task. When the List is sorted by a column, the order is kept but shown once you go back to your own order.</li><li><b>Linked issues</b> show their status now (Open, In progress, Resolved). <b>+ Link an issue</b> picks one of the project's issues.</li><li><b>Files, sheets and 3D views:</b> paste a OneDrive, SharePoint or ACC address, or use <b>+ Task</b> on the Sheets or 3D page to keep the sheet or view you are looking at. Revit elements kept on a task show as <b>Elements to change</b>.</li><li><b>Comments:</b> @name tells someone; paste a screenshot or attach files (up to 50 MB each). Your own comments have <b>edit</b> and <b>delete</b>.</li><li><b>Follow</b> emails you when the task changes; <b>Share</b> sends it to a chat; the link button copies its address.</li><li>The ▲ ▼ buttons, or <b>K</b> / <b>J</b>, go to the previous / next task. On a phone, <b>Back</b> returns to the list.</li></ul>"},{"id":"s10","ch":"Tasks","h":"Members of a list","lv":3,"html":"<ul><li><b>Owner</b> (changes the list's settings and members), <b>Editor</b> (adds and changes tasks) and <b>Viewer</b> (reads only). Site admins see every list.</li></ul>"},{"id":"s11","ch":"Tasks","h":"Importing from Lark","lv":3,"html":"<ol><li>In Lark, open the task list and choose <b>...</b> &gt; <b>Export</b> (Excel).</li><li>In Tasks, use <b>+</b> &gt; <b>Import a Lark task list (.xlsx)</b> to make a new list, or <b>...</b> &gt; <b>Import from Lark (.xlsx) / CSV</b> to bring it into the open list.</li><li>Groups, sub-tasks, owners, followers, dates, done status, priority, completion method, milestones, Modelers and Project Manager all come in, with a link back to each task in Lark.</li><li>Importing the same export again updates the tasks instead of adding them twice. Names with no account yet are kept as names; once the accounts exist, use <b>...</b> &gt; <b>Match names to accounts</b>.</li></ol>"},{"id":"s12","ch":"Tasks","h":"Queries","lv":3,"html":"<p><b>Queries</b> (the blue button at the top of the Tasks side bar) is a register of questions for each project on the Projects page, numbered <b>Q-001</b>, <b>Q-002</b> ... - for example a missing dimension, an unclear detail or a clash to be decided. It is separate from the issues: a query asks the team, inside the viewer, and keeps their answer. The number beside <b>Queries</b> is how many open queries are to you (and answered ones you raised, to close); a red <b>N overdue</b> shows when some of yours are past their due date.</p><ul><li><b>Raise a query:</b> pick the project at the top, then <b>+ New query</b>: the subject, the question, <b>To</b> (the project's people who should answer; Ctrl-click for several), <b>Due</b> (a week from today unless you change it) and <b>Priority</b>. The people it is to get a notice in the bell and an email, and a card goes to the project's chat channel.</li><li><b>Pictures of the exact view:</b> on a sheet or in the 3D model, click <b>+ Query</b> in the header (next to + Task; in 3D in the <b>⋯</b> menu). A small menu asks where the picture goes: type a subject and <b>Create</b> for a new query, or click one of the project's open queries (the one you used last is on top: <b>Add another to Q-...</b>). <b>After adding:</b> <b>Stay here</b> (a note confirms it, and you move to the next sheet or 3D view and click <b>+ Query</b> again - so one query can hold several 2D and 3D views) or <b>Open the query</b> (opens it in Tasks). Your choice is remembered. Anyone on the project can add pictures to a query.</li><li><b>Opening a picture:</b> on the query, a click on a sheet picture opens the same sheet zoomed to the same area; a 3D picture opens the model with the same camera, section box and plane. Remove a picture with its ✕ (who raised it, who it is to, or a project admin).</li><li><b>Pictures of your own:</b> under <b>Pictures &amp; views</b>, <b>+ Add picture</b> adds image files (site photos, a consultant's markup, a screenshot saved before); or paste a screenshot (<b>Ctrl+V</b>) or drop pictures anywhere on the query panel. The <b>New query</b> form takes them the same way. A click shows a picture full size; <b>‹ ›</b> or the arrow keys go through the query's pictures, <b>Esc</b> closes. They are in the report too.</li><li><b>Marking up a picture:</b> the ✎ on any picture of a query - a sheet or 3D view, or a picture of your own - opens the same markup tools as an issue's snapshot: cloud, rectangle, circle, arrow, line, pen, text, text box, callout, with colour, weight and text size. <b>Done</b> keeps the drawing on the picture; the ✎ shows how many marks it has, and opening it again brings the drawing back to change (the picture as taken is kept underneath). In the <b>+ Query</b> menu on a sheet or in 3D, tick <b>Mark up the picture first</b> to draw on the view before it is added.</li><li><b>+ Sheet view / + 3D view:</b> in a query (and in the <b>New query</b> form, which raises the query first) these open the project's sheets or 3D model with a bar saying which query you are adding to; go to the view and click <b>+ Query</b> (or right-click &gt; <b>Add to query here</b>) - that query is offered first. <b>Back to the query</b> returns. A project of several parts asks which part.</li><li><b>Answer, follow-ups and close:</b> the people it is to write the <b>Answer</b> and click <b>Mark answered</b>. Under <b>Answer &amp; follow-ups</b>, anyone on the project can then click <b>+ Follow-up question</b> - the query is open again - and the people it is to answer it with <b>+ Answer</b>, as often as needed; the conversation shows as bubbles (questions on the left, answers on the right), and each step tells the people concerned and posts a card in the project's chat. When it is settled, the one who raised it (or a project admin) clicks <b>Close the query</b>. The <b>Discussion</b> below is for comments and files. <b>Reopen</b> brings a closed query back. <b>History</b> lists every step.</li><li><b>Queries on the sheets and in 3D:</b> each sheet or 3D picture of a query shows where it was taken - on the sheet, a badge (<b>Q12</b>, in the status colour: orange open, blue answered, green closed, red overdue) with the area it showed in a dashed outline; in 3D, a pin. Right-click on a sheet or the model &gt; <b>Add to query here</b> captures the view with its marker on the point you clicked (then the same menu as <b>+ Query</b>). Click a badge or pin for its card: the query, its status and due date, the picture, <b>Open query</b> and <b>Delete marker</b>.</li><li><b>The list and hiding them:</b> on Sheets, the right-hand column has a <b>Queries</b> tab (and <b>All</b> lists them first); in 3D, <b>Queries in 3D</b> heads the issue list. A click goes to the sheet area or the 3D view and opens its card. The Status filter and Search apply. <b>? Queries</b> (Sheets) / <b>Hide queries</b> (3D) hide the markers; <b>Hide closed</b> also hides closed queries.</li><li><b>Deleting:</b> <b>Delete marker</b> (on its card, or right-click the badge) removes that picture from the query - the query stays, with its other pictures. Deleting a query removes all its markers. A marker can be deleted by who raised the query, who it is to, a project admin, or who added that picture.</li><li><b>Tasks:</b> <b>+ New task from this query</b> makes a task in one of your lists (its owners are the people the query is to, its due date the query's, with a link back to the query and its pictures); <b>Link a task</b> links one you have. The tasks show with their done state.</li><li><b>List:</b> filter by status (Open and answered, Open, Overdue, Answered - to close, Closed, All) and by <b>To me</b> / <b>Raised by me</b>, or search. An overdue query shows red.</li><li><b>Calendar:</b> the due dates of the open queries that are to you or raised by you show in the Calendar (<b>My queries</b>); click one to open it.</li><li><b>Chat:</b> in a message type <b>?</b> and a few letters to link a query (or use the link button &gt; <b>? Query</b>); <b>+</b> &gt; <b>Query</b> raises a new query in the chat's project and posts its card. <b>Send to chat</b> on a query posts its card to the project's channel again.</li><li><b>Dashboard</b> tab: open, overdue, due in 7 days, answered - to close, closed this month and the average days to answer; queries by status, open queries per person (red: overdue) and raised against answered per week. Click a tile to see those queries in the list.</li><li><b>Report (PDF):</b> the register (number, subject, raised by, to, due, status, answered) and then each query with its question, pictures and answer - of the queries in the list as filtered. <b>Print / Save as PDF</b>, or <b>Save to Folders</b> (a PDF in Folders &gt; Queries).</li></ul>"},{"id":"s13","ch":"Board","h":"Board","lv":2,"html":"<figure class=\"shot\"><img src=\"help-img/board.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><ol><li>Boards: all the project's boards, new board, templates</li><li>The board's name</li><li>Who is on the board now</li><li>Find text on the board</li><li>A countdown for everyone</li><li>Present: frame by frame</li><li>Export: picture, PDF, backup</li><li>Select and move; move the board</li><li>Sticky note, text, shape, connector, mind map, pen</li><li>Frame, picture, card linked to an issue or a sheet</li><li>Undo / redo</li><li>The board: double-click to write</li><li>Overview map, zoom, Fit</li></ol></figure><p><b>Board</b> is a shared whiteboard for each project, in the manner of Miro: sticky notes, text, shapes, connectors, mind maps, pictures and frames, with templates to start from. Everyone on the project sees changes as they are made. Pick the project at the top; use the board list to make, rename, copy or delete boards.</p><p>A board you opened before shows at once from this device; changes made since then by others arrive within a few seconds. Signing out clears the copies kept on the device (Board, Tasks, Dashboard).</p><p><b>The LWK BIM Workflow board</b></p><p>Every project starts with a board called <b>LWK BIM Workflow</b>: the company's BIM workflow as the project's own copy, to change to suit the project. It is made the first time someone who can edit opens the project's Board page.</p><ul><li><b>What is on it:</b> 0 Project card (number, name, stage, software, CDE location - fill in at kick-off) · 1 How to use this board · 2 Team &amp; roles (responsibilities, knowledge, a column for the names) · 3 Work stages (who leads and what comes out, from Inception to Completion) · 4.0-4.6 the workflow charts: Project setup (1.0), Modelling (2.0), Model review / design changes (2.1), Model development using SAM (2.3), clash detection in ACC (3.0), GBP submission with BD's Area Tool (4.0 / 4.1) · 5 CDE folder states (ISO 19650) · 6 QA/QC checks · 7 BIM audit checklist · 8 Meetings · 9 How the viewer supports each step · 10 Project notes · 11 Reference diagrams.</li><li><b>Colours:</b> each role has one colour in every chart (BIM Manager, HK Coordinator, Manila Senior Coordinator, Task Team Lead, BIM Authors, Project Team, Design Team, CAD Team); the key is under each chart.</li><li><b>The audit checklist:</b> the board shows all the items as a guide. The record of an audit is still the Excel: a blank <b>LWK BIM Audit Checklist.xlsx</b> is put in the project's <b>Folders</b> under <b>BIM QA</b> when the board is made (if one of that name is not there already).</li><li><b>A project that already had boards</b> is not given one by itself. Add it with <b>New board</b> &gt; <b>LWK BIM Workflow</b>; the same adds another copy to any project.</li><li>Everything on it is ordinary board content: move, recolour, add or delete anything. Deleting the board does not bring it back by itself.</li></ul>"},{"id":"s14","ch":"Messenger","h":"Messenger","lv":2,"html":"<figure class=\"shot\"><img src=\"help-img/chat.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><ol><li>Search chats (Enter: search the messages)</li><li>New chat: a message to someone, or a group</li><li>Project channels - one per project</li><li>Groups and direct messages</li><li>Task discussions</li><li>Open the project, its sheets or 3D</li><li>Files sent in the chat</li><li>Members</li><li>Topics: sub-channels for one subject</li><li>The messages</li><li>Write: @ person, # task, ! issue, $ sheet, % 3D view</li><li>Bold, lists, quote, link, code</li><li>Emoji, mention, link, files, poll / event / task</li><li>Send (Enter)</li></ol></figure><p><b>Chat</b> opens the Messenger: the team's conversations, next to the work they are about.</p><p>Drag the edge of the chat list or of the details panel to size it; the small tab on the list's edge pins it, or - unpinned - folds it away for a wider conversation (as on the Sheets and 3D pages).</p><p><b>Kinds of chat</b></p><table><tr><th>Chat</th><th>What it is</th></tr><tr><td>Project channel</td><td>One per project, with its own colour and initials (its topics take the same colour). Everyone on the project is in it. New tasks, assignments, completions, task comments, progress (when a task passes 25, 50 or 75 %) and new or changed issues are posted into it as cards. A task card shows its progress bar and how many of its sub-tasks are done; a sub-task's card also says which task it is under and how far that task is</td></tr><tr><td>Topic</td><td>A sub-channel of a project channel for one subject (Facade, MEP coordination, Site visits). Listed under its channel, and as tabs under the channel's name: <b># General</b> is the channel itself</td></tr><tr><td>Group</td><td>Any group of people, named by whoever starts it</td></tr><tr><td>Direct message</td><td>Two people</td></tr><tr><td>Task discussion</td><td>The comments of the tasks you follow, answered from here</td></tr></table><ul><li>The pencil at the top starts a new chat. Right-click a chat (or hold it on a phone) for <b>Details</b>, <b>Mark as read</b>, <b>New topic</b> (project channels), <b>Leave</b>, <b>Import WhatsApp chat ...</b>, <b>Send chat link to WhatsApp</b> and <b>Delete chat</b>, for those who may delete it.</li><li><b>Opening a topic:</b> anyone in the project channel presses <b>+ Topic</b> on the tabs under its name (or <b>New topic</b> in its menu, or the pencil &gt; <b>Topic in a project channel</b>). Everyone in the channel is added.</li><li><b>Who can delete a chat:</b> a direct message, either of the two people (it goes for both); a group, its admins (who started it) or a site admin; a project channel or topic, the project's admins or a site admin. Deleting a channel deletes its topics too.</li><li><b>Chat info</b> (the people button): the description, the members (add, remove, message), <b>Pictures and files</b>, <b>Leave this chat</b> and <b>Delete this chat</b>.</li><li>The number on <b>Chat</b> in the header of every page shows unread messages; <b>@</b> means you were mentioned.</li></ul><p><b>Writing</b></p><ul><li><b>Enter</b> makes a new line; the <b>Send</b> button sends (on a keyboard, <b>Ctrl+Enter</b> sends too).</li><li>Paste or drop screenshots, or use the paper clip for pictures and files up to 50 MB each. OneDrive, SharePoint and ACC links show as cards; a video link shows a play card, and a pasted OneDrive or SharePoint <b>Embed</b> code plays right in the chat.</li><li><b>@</b> a person. <b>#</b> a task, <b>!</b> an issue, <b>$</b> a sheet, <b>%</b> the 3D model or a saved view: a list opens as you type. <b>Choose the project first</b> in the row of projects at the top of the list (in a project channel its own project is chosen). The <b>#</b> button beside the paper clip opens the same lists with tabs.</li><li>The picked item shows in the message as a named link that opens it.</li><li>🙂 adds emoji.</li><li><b>Formatting (Aa):</b> the box shows the words as they will be sent, as in Lark. <b>Aa</b> shows the format buttons: <b>B</b>, <b>S</b>, <b>I</b>, <b>U</b>, numbered and bulleted lists, quote, link, code and block of code; <b>Ctrl+B</b>, <b>Ctrl+I</b>, <b>Ctrl+U</b> and <b>Ctrl+Shift+X</b> work on the selection. On a phone they appear in their own row after <b>Aa</b>. Forwarded to WhatsApp, a message keeps its bold, italic and strikethrough.</li><li><b>The buttons under the box:</b> <b>Aa</b>, 🙂 emoji, <b>@</b> a person, <b>#</b> a task, issue, sheet or 3D view (it shows in the box as a chip), the paper clip, <b>+</b> and <b>Send</b>, which is always on screen, on a phone too.</li><li><b>The + button:</b> <b>Poll</b>, <b>Event / meeting</b>, <b>Task</b>, or a link to a task, issue, sheet or 3D view.</li></ul><p><b>Polls, events and tasks</b></p><ul><li><b>Poll:</b> a question with 2 to 10 choices; tick <b>Allow more than one answer</b>, <b>Anonymous</b> or a closing date if you like. Tap a choice to vote, again to take it back. The writer can <b>Close poll</b> (and reopen it).</li><li><b>Event:</b> title, date, time (or <b>All day</b>), where and the Teams link. Everyone in the chat is invited (by email too when mail is set up) and answers <b>Going</b>, <b>Maybe</b> or <b>Can't go</b>. <b>Add to calendar (.ics)</b> puts it in Outlook, Google or the phone. The writer can <b>Change</b> or <b>Cancel event</b>; the chat is told.</li><li><b>Task:</b> choose the task list and group (this project's first), owners (the chosen list's members; <b>Show everyone</b> for the rest), due date and priority. The task goes into the list and its card into the chat. ⋯ More &gt; <b>Make a task</b> on any message does the same, with the message as the description, the people @mentioned as owners and a link back to it.</li></ul><p><b>A message</b></p><ul><li>Hover a message (tap it on a phone): 🙂 <b>React</b>, ↩ <b>Reply</b>, ✏ <b>Edit</b> (your own) and ⋯ <b>More</b>: <b>Copy</b>, <b>Pin</b>, <b>Make a task</b>, <b>Forward to another chat</b>, <b>Send to WhatsApp</b>, <b>Copy link to this message</b> and <b>Delete</b> (your own).</li><li><b>Edit</b> changes the message in place: <b>Ctrl+Enter</b> saves, <b>Esc</b> cancels; others see \"(edited)\". <b>Edit</b> and <b>Delete</b> are only for the person who sent the message (not the chat's admin, not a site admin); others see \"message deleted\".</li><li><b>Pinned messages:</b> anyone in the chat can pin a message, up to 100 a chat. The bar under the chat's name shows the latest one; click it to see the message and move on to the next; <b>All</b> lists them, with <b>unpin</b>.</li><li><b>Reactions</b> show under the message with a count; tap one to add or take away yours.</li><li>A message that could not be sent stays with <b>send again</b>.</li></ul><p><b>WhatsApp</b></p><ul><li><b>Out:</b> <b>Send to WhatsApp</b> on a message sends its words, links and files. On a phone, pictures go as themselves through the share sheet; on a computer it opens WhatsApp Desktop or WhatsApp Web.</li><li><b>Copied messages:</b> messages copied in WhatsApp and pasted into the box are offered as one \"From WhatsApp\" quote.</li><li><b>Exported chat:</b> in WhatsApp, the chat &gt; <b>More</b> &gt; <b>Export chat</b>, and send yourself the .zip (with media) or .txt. Then in a chat's menu choose <b>Import WhatsApp chat ...</b>: the messages arrive as one quote with the pictures in place.</li><li><b>Android:</b> with the viewer installed as an app, use WhatsApp's <b>Share</b> &gt; <b>LWK Viewer</b> and choose the chat. (iPhone does not offer this: copy and paste, or export.)</li><li>There is no automatic two-way link with WhatsApp.</li></ul>"},{"id":"s15","ch":"Calendar","h":"Calendar","lv":2,"html":"<figure class=\"shot\"><img src=\"help-img/calendar.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><ol><li>Previous / Today / Next</li><li>The month (or week) shown</li><li>Groups: see a team's leave</li><li>Month, Week or List</li><li>Sync to Outlook: this calendar in Outlook, kept up to date</li><li>+ New: an event, a meeting, a task or leave</li><li>Show: click a kind to hide or show it; Holidays ▾ chooses HK / PH</li><li>Your tasks on their due dates - click to open</li></ol></figure><p><b>Right-click a day</b> (hold it on a phone) to add on that day an <b>event</b> (all day), a <b>meeting</b> (from 10:00, choose the chat to invite) or a <b>task</b> due that day.</p><p><b>Calendar</b> shows what is coming up for you, by date: <b>meetings</b> sent in the Messenger (with your reply), <b>your tasks</b> on their due dates - with the <b>sub-tasks</b> (at any level) of the tasks you own, which say <b>Sub-task of ...</b>, and the tasks whose sub-tasks are yours (their own due date beside the sub-tasks') - and <b>issues assigned to you</b> on their due dates.</p><ul><li>A month on a computer, a list on a phone (<b>Month</b> / <b>Week</b> / <b>List</b>). The <b>Show</b> row is the legend and the switches: click <b>Issue due dates</b>, <b>Tasks</b>, <b>Holidays</b>, <b>Team leave</b> or <b>Meetings</b> to hide or show them. <b>Filter ▾</b> also sets <b>Week starts on: Monday / Sunday</b> (remembered for you). <b>‹ ›</b> and <b>Today</b> move through the months (or weeks); on a phone, swipe.</li><li>Click an entry for its details, then open the chat, the task or the issue. Replies to a meeting are made in its chat.</li><li><b>+ New ▾:</b> an <b>Event</b> or <b>Meeting</b> (choose a chat; the form opens there, so everyone in it is invited), a <b>Task</b>, or <b>Leave</b>.</li><li><b>Sync to Outlook:</b> <b>Open in Outlook on this PC</b> subscribes Outlook to your calendar (choose <b>Yes</b>), or copy the address and use Outlook's <b>Add calendar &gt; From Internet</b>. Outlook then shows the entries beside your own calendar and updates them by itself. Outlook on the web and on phones can only reach it when the viewer is reachable from the internet.</li><li>The address is yours alone: <b>Make a new address</b> if it was shared by mistake (the old one stops working).</li></ul>"},{"id":"s16","ch":"Calendar","h":"Public holidays","lv":3,"html":"<ul><li>The <b>Holidays</b> chip (its <b>▾</b>) shows the public holidays of <b>Hong Kong</b> and / or <b>the Philippines</b> on the calendar (tick either or both; remembered for you). The 2026 and 2027 lists are built in (Hong Kong: Government Gazette; Philippines: Proclamations No. 1006 and 1427, regular holidays and special non-working days).</li><li>A site admin adds later years and dates proclaimed late (the Philippine Eid'l Fitr and Eid'l Adha): <b>Holidays ▾ &gt; Edit the list</b>, one a line, e.g. <i>2028-01-01 New Year's Day</i>.</li></ul>"},{"id":"s17","ch":"Calendar","h":"Annual leave and calendar groups","lv":3,"html":"<ul><li><b>+ New ▾ &gt; Leave</b>, <b>right-click a day &gt; Add leave</b>, or <b>drag across days</b> in the month: from and to, the type (annual, sick, other), a half day (AM / PM, for one day) and a note. The form counts the working days (weekends and the ticked holidays left out; Hong Kong when none is ticked).</li><li>Your leave shows on your calendar and on the calendars of the people who share a <b>calendar group</b> with you; theirs shows on yours. Click a leave for its details; <b>Remove this leave</b> takes your own away.</li><li><b>Groups:</b> <b>+ New group</b>, a name and its people (anyone can make one; you are in it). The person who made a group (or a site admin) edits or deletes it; the others can <b>Leave group</b>. <b>Filter ▾ &gt; Leave of</b> shows the leave of one group only.</li><li>Outlook (Sync to Outlook) gets your own leave, not your colleagues'.</li></ul>"},{"id":"s18","ch":"Notifications and the app","h":"Notifications and the app","lv":2,"html":"<figure class=\"shot\"><img src=\"help-img/bell.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><ol><li>For you: tasks given to you, @mentions, issues assigned to you - tick to mark read</li><li>Mark all read</li><li>Chat notifications in this browser</li><li>Tell me about: every message, @mentions only, or nothing</li><li>Push when no page is open; Send a test</li><li>The app: install it for its own window and badge</li><li>Look: Light, Dark, Auto</li><li>What's new in the viewer</li></ol></figure><p>New chat messages reach you without reloading any page, and the viewer can be installed as an app.</p><ul><li><b>While a viewer page is open</b> (any page, a tab in the background, or the app): new messages show as notifications on Windows, Mac and Android; a click opens the chat at the message. The chat you are looking at stays quiet. The tab title shows the unread count, e.g. <b>(3) LWK Viewer</b>, and so does the app's icon.</li><li><b>The bell</b> in the header: <b>Turn on notifications</b> (the browser asks once), then choose <b>Every message</b>, <b>@mentions and direct messages</b> or <b>Nothing</b>.</li><li><b>Mute a chat:</b> Chat info &gt; <b>Mute notifications</b>. A muted chat still tells you when you are @mentioned.</li><li><b>Not only messages:</b> you are also told when a task is made yours, when you are @mentioned on a task or an issue, when an issue is assigned to you or your query is answered, and when tasks you own are due. The bell's <b>For you</b> list keeps the latest ones (a red number shows how many are new); click one to open it, <b>Mark all read</b> clears the number. The <b>box beside each one</b> marks it read (ticked) or unread again (unticked) without opening it.</li><li><b>Install the app:</b> the bell &gt; <b>Install the app</b> (Edge, Chrome), or the install icon at the right of the address bar. On Android: menu &gt; <b>Add to Home screen</b>. On iPhone and iPad: Safari &gt; Share &gt; <b>Add to Home Screen</b>. The app opens in its own window, with shortcuts to Chat, Tasks, Calendar, Folders and Projects (right-click the icon).</li><li><b>When no page is open (push):</b> the bell &gt; <b>Turn on for this device</b>. This works when the viewer is opened by its <b>https</b> address; ask your admin. Messages then arrive on that phone or computer even with the app closed.</li><li><b>iPhone and iPad:</b> first add the viewer to the Home Screen (Safari &gt; Share &gt; <b>Add to Home Screen</b>) and open it from there; then in the bell turn on notifications and <b>Turn on for this device</b>, and press <b>Send a test</b>. If it does not arrive, the message says why (for example the server cannot reach Apple). After a server update, turn push off and on again once.</li></ul>"},{"id":"s19","ch":"Look, links and what's new","h":"Look, links and what's new","lv":2,"html":"<figure class=\"shot\"><img src=\"help-img/profile-menu.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><ol><li>Your picture: opens this menu</li><li>Work offline: keep this project on the device</li><li>Admin: people and project members</li><li>Account: your password</li><li>Help (F1)</li><li>Theme: Light, Dark, Auto</li><li>Sign out</li></ol></figure><p>Small things that make the viewer easier to find your way around and to share.</p><ul><li><b>Dark mode:</b> the bell &gt; <b>Look</b> &gt; <b>Dark</b>. <b>Auto</b> follows your computer or phone (dark at night if it is set so); <b>Light</b> is the usual look. It is kept on each computer or phone. Drawings, PDFs, document previews and the whiteboard stay white, as paper; the 3D background turns dark grey unless you picked a colour in Display.</li><li><b>What's new:</b> after each update a small card lists what changed, once. <b>Got it</b> closes it; the bell &gt; <b>What's new in the viewer</b> shows the whole list at any time.</li><li><b>Copy link</b> (the 🔗 buttons) copies an address to paste into a chat or an email. Only people in the project can open it.</li><li><b>A sheet:</b> the 🔗 in the sheet toolbar. <b>An issue:</b> the 🔗 at the top of the issue (2D or 3D). <b>A project:</b> the 🔗 on the project's panel (Projects page). <b>A 3D view:</b> the 🔗 next to <b>BCF</b> in the 3D header copies the exact view - camera, section box or plane, floor, display mode and hidden elements - and whoever opens it sees the same.</li><li><b>Sections fold:</b> click a heading on a project's panel (Projects page), on the Admin page or in the 3D left panel to fold or open it. The viewer remembers which ones you folded.</li><li><b>Lists keep your place:</b> Folders reopens the folders you had open in the tree, and the sheet list and the chat list keep the one you are on in view.</li><li><b>While a list loads</b> grey placeholder rows show where it will be.</li></ul>"},{"id":"s20","ch":"Undo","h":"Undo","lv":2,"html":"<ul><li><b>Ctrl+Z</b> (Cmd+Z on a Mac) undoes the last change; <b>Ctrl+Y</b> (or Ctrl+Shift+Z) redoes it. A note at the bottom says what was undone, with <b>Redo</b>.</li><li><b>Tasks:</b> changed fields, Kanban moves, list drags, Gantt moves, a new task and a deleted task (with its sub-tasks).</li><li><b>Messenger:</b> a deleted message (your own, within a day), an edit, a pin and a reaction.</li><li><b>Folders:</b> delete, rename, move, upload and a new folder.</li><li>While you type in a box, Ctrl+Z undoes the typing as usual. The Sheets and 3D pages keep their own undo for markups.</li></ul>"},{"id":"s21","ch":"Folders","h":"Folders","lv":2,"html":"<figure class=\"shot\"><img src=\"help-img/folders.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><ol><li>Pinned, Starred, Recent, Recently deleted</li><li>The folders (drag files here to move them)</li><li>Hide or show the folders</li><li>Where you are</li><li>Search this project's files</li><li>+ Folder</li><li>Upload</li><li>Drop files here to upload into this folder (or click)</li><li>Click a heading to sort</li><li>The locked 00 BIM folder: the sheets and models from Revit</li><li>More: rename, move, versions, pin, star, delete</li></ol></figure><p>Right-click a folder in the tree on the left (or use ⋯ on a folder) for <b>New folder here</b>, <b>Rename</b>, <b>Move to ...</b>, <b>Star</b>, <b>Pin</b>, <b>Copy link</b> and <b>Delete</b>.</p><p><b>Reading documents without downloading:</b> click a PDF, picture, video, text file, or a <b>Word, Excel or PowerPoint</b> file and it opens beside the list. Office files look exactly as in Office when LibreOffice is installed on the server (ask your admin); without it, Word and Excel are shown in a simpler way and PowerPoint has to be downloaded.</p><ul><li><b>More room for the document:</b> <b>☰</b> (top left of the list) hides or shows the folder column, and is remembered. <b>⤢</b> in the preview hides the folders and the file list too, so the document gets the whole width; press it again, or <b>Esc</b>, to bring them back. Drag the preview's left edge to make it wider.</li><li><b>Whole page:</b> Word and Excel files shown in the page start at <b>Fit</b>: the widest page, landscape pages too, fits the width of the preview, on a computer and on a phone. <b>−</b> and <b>+</b> zoom; <b>Fit</b> goes back. PDFs open at the page width.</li><li><b>On a phone or tablet</b> (upright or on its side) a document opens full screen: PDFs and converted Office files show every page, one under the other, to scroll through; pinch with two fingers or use <b>−</b> / <b>+</b> to zoom. <b>☰</b> opens the folders; tap beside them to close.</li><li><b>For the admin - installing LibreOffice</b> on the server (Ubuntu): `sudo apt-get install -y --no-install-recommends libreoffice-writer libreoffice-calc libreoffice-impress fonts-noto-cjk fonts-liberation fonts-crosextra-carlito fonts-crosextra-caladea`, then restart the viewer service. All three of Writer, Calc and Impress are needed: with only libreoffice-core the page says \"cannot read this kind of file\". A big document takes a while the first time; it is kept, so it opens at once after that.</li></ul><p><b>Folders</b> holds each project's files in a folder on the server, like ACC Docs or a shared drive. Pick the project at the top left.</p><p><b>00 BIM</b> (🔒, always first) holds what the viewer has for the project, always up to date: <b>2D Sheets</b> (the sheets exported from Revit, named by number and name, and the PDF sets uploaded on the Sheets page) and <b>3D Models</b> (opened on the 3D page; IFC files - IFC projects and consultant models - can be downloaded). Everyone in the project can open and download there; nobody can add, rename, move or delete. A project with several parts has a folder per part.</p><p><b>Exports kept in Folders:</b> after any export downloads (a clash or headroom spreadsheet, the Dashboard spreadsheet, BCF, a marked-up PDF, a board picture or backup) a bar at the bottom offers <b>Save to Folders</b>; reports (clash, headroom, the issue report) have <b>Save to Folders (PDF)</b> beside Print - the server makes the PDF. They are kept in <b>00 BIM &gt; Exports &gt; Clash / Headroom / Issues / BCF / Markups / Board</b>, and the weekly report in <b>00 BIM &gt; Weekly dashboard</b>, with who kept them. Like the rest of 00 BIM they cannot be renamed or deleted there (download a copy to change it). A name already there gets \"(2)\".</p><ul><li><b>Browse:</b> the folder tree on the left, the path at the top, or <b>Search this project's files</b>. Double-click a folder to open it; click a PDF, picture or video to preview it.</li><li><b>Upload:</b> drop files, or whole folders, onto the page (or onto a folder in the list), or press <b>Upload</b>. <b>+ Folder</b> makes a folder.</li><li><b>⋯ on a file</b> (or right-click): Preview, Download, <b>Add to the Sheets page</b> (PDFs), <b>Star</b>, <b>Pin for everyone</b> (project admins), Copy link, Rename, <b>Move to ...</b> and Delete. <b>Delete</b> and <b>F2</b> work on the selected file.</li><li><b>Drag and drop, as in OneDrive:</b> drag files or folders from the list - or a folder in the tree on the left - onto any folder in the list, the tree or the path at the top. Hold the pointer on a closed folder in the tree for a moment and it opens, so you can drop deep inside; near the top or bottom of the tree it scrolls. A note by the pointer says what will happen. Hold <b>Ctrl</b> as you drop to <b>copy</b> instead of move. <b>Ctrl+Z</b> undoes it.</li><li><b>Versions:</b> upload a file whose name is already in the folder and the page asks: <b>New version</b> (the same name and place; the one there is kept as the version before) or <b>Keep both</b> (\"name (2)\"). You can say what changed (for example <i>Rev B - layout revised</i>). A file with versions shows <b>v2</b>, <b>v3</b> ... beside its name. <b>⋯ &gt; Versions</b> (or <b>Versions</b> in the preview) lists them all - who, when, what changed - with <b>Open</b> (shown in the preview, marked as an earlier version), <b>⬇</b> download and <b>Make current</b>, which brings an earlier one back as the newest version (nothing is lost). A project admin can remove an old version with <b>✕</b>. Moving, renaming, deleting and restoring a file keep its versions with it.</li><li><b>Pinned</b> shows the documents a project admin pinned for everyone; <b>Starred</b> shows your own. <b>Recent</b> lists the newest files.</li><li><b>Deleting:</b> the person who uploaded a file, or a project admin. Deleted things go to <b>Recently deleted</b>, from where they can be put back; <b>Ctrl+Z</b> also brings them back at once.</li><li><b>Sorting and columns:</b> click <b>Name</b>, <b>Modified</b>, <b>Size</b> or <b>Uploaded by</b> to sort (▲, ▼, then the usual order; folders stay first). Drag the edge of the folder tree or of the preview to size it.</li><li><b>Folder templates (project admins):</b> ⋯ (top right) &gt; <b>Save these folders as a template</b> keeps this project's folders (no files) by name. In another project, <b>Lay out folders from a template</b> makes the folders it is missing; nothing is deleted.</li><li><b>To the Sheets page:</b> a PDF's ⋯ &gt; <b>Add to the Sheets page</b> turns its pages into sheets in a set of their own (choose the set and the sheet number), ready for markups and issues.</li><li>Files put into the project's folder on the server some other way (for example from Windows Explorer) show up here too.</li></ul>"},{"id":"s22","ch":"Sheets (2D)","h":"Sheets (2D)","lv":2,"html":"<figure class=\"shot\"><img src=\"help-img/sheets.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><ol><li>The sheets - click one to open it</li><li>Search sheet numbers, names and the words on the drawings</li><li>Set: which sheets to show (from Revit, or an uploaded PDF set); rename, archive, delete a set</li><li>The mark-up tools, in families (next picture)</li><li>Comment / + Issue: what you draw becomes a comment or an issue</li><li>Files: download PDFs, import PDF / CAD, BCF, export</li><li>+ Task: keep this sheet on a task</li><li>View: split, compare two versions, sync, links between sheets</li><li>Undo / redo</li><li>Zoom: 100% is the sheet fitting the width; rotate, zoom out / in, Fit</li><li>The sheet, with its issues and comments - click one to open it</li><li>All / Issues / Comments</li><li>Show or hide the mark-ups on the drawing</li><li>Hide closed issues</li><li>Group the list by sheet, status, person ...</li><li>Search the issues and comments</li><li>Filter by type and status; sort</li><li>An issue: number, title, who, when, status - click to open it</li><li>Copy a link to this sheet</li></ol></figure><p>The Sheets page shows every published sheet as the real PDF, searchable and ready for markup; markups save by themselves, there is no Save button.</p>"},{"id":"s23","ch":"Sheets (2D)","h":"Finding a sheet","lv":3,"html":"<ul><li>The <b>Sheets</b> list on the left shows number and name. \"x/y mapped\" means that many views on the sheet are linked to the 3D model.</li><li>Click a sheet to open it. The viewer remembers the last sheet you had open.</li><li><b>Search all sheets</b> finds sheet numbers, names and any words printed on the drawings (room names, notes, grid labels). Matches are highlighted on the sheet. The first search on a project can take a moment while the drawings are read.</li><li><b>Page Down / Page Up</b> go to the next or previous sheet.</li><li>To add an outside PDF (a consultant drawing, a sketch), use the <b>PDF</b> upload button and name its <b>set</b> (e.g. \"Uploaded PDFs\" or \"Consultant 2026-10\"). Each set is its own entry under <b>Set:</b> at the top of the sheet list, apart from the sheets from Revit (<b>Revit sheets</b>). Its sheets show \"Imported 2D only\" and can be removed with their <b>✕</b>.</li><li><b>Groups and hidden sheets:</b> the sheet list can be in <b>groups</b> (topics - Plans, Elevations, Sections ...): ☰ in the Sheets heading &gt; <b>New group</b>, then ☰ &gt; <b>Move / hide sheets</b>: tick the sheets and use <b>Move to ▾</b> or <b>Hide</b> in the bar that stays at the top of the list (or right-click any ticked sheet - all the ticked ones move). The choice clears after each move, ready for the next; <b>Esc</b> or <b>Done</b> finishes - project members make the groups, for everyone. Click a group's heading to fold it; its ⋯ has <b>Show only this group</b> and <b>Show all groups</b> (folding is your own). An <b>admin</b> can <b>hide</b> sheets from the viewer: right-click &gt; <b>Hide ... from the viewer</b> (or Select several &gt; <b>Hide</b>). A hidden sheet stays hidden after the next publish from Revit; admins still see it, dimmed, under <b>Hidden from the viewer</b>, to show it again. To leave sheets out for good, publish from Revit with only the sheets wanted and <b>Keep sheets published before</b> unticked.</li><li><b>Putting sheets in order:</b> drag a sheet (or the ticked ones) onto another - it goes before or after it, into that sheet's group; drop on a group's heading to put it at the end of that group. Or right-click a sheet &gt; <b>Move up</b> / <b>Move down</b>. Each group keeps its own order, and so do the sheets in no group, for everyone. <b>Hidden is the recycle bin</b> (admins): right-click a hidden sheet &gt; <b>Delete from the server ...</b>, or ⋯ on the Hidden heading &gt; <b>Delete all ...</b> - the sheet and its PDF go for good and do not come back with the next publish from Revit; its markups and issues are kept.</li><li>A move into a group, or a hide, shows at once and is saved behind it - the sheet list is not read again, so even a big project can be sorted quickly without slowing the server for others. If a change cannot be saved, the status line says so and the list is shown again as the server has it.</li><li>Importing a PDF opens one window: the <b>sheet number</b> (a prefix for a PDF of several pages), the <b>set</b>, and <b>Keep the PDF in Folders</b> - by default in <b>00 BIM &gt; Import &gt; PDF &gt; (the set)</b>; <b>Change folder ...</b> picks another project or folder (or <b>+ New folder</b>); <b>Don't keep a copy</b>. The choice is remembered for the project. The model has to be in a Folders project (Projects page) for this.</li><li><b>Set: ... ▾</b> (at the top of the sheet list) chooses which sheets to show - <b>Revit sheets</b> or a set of uploaded PDFs - and, on a set of imported PDFs: <b>Select sheets</b> - tick several (shift-click for a run) and <b>Delete</b> them together; <b>Rename set</b>; <b>Archive set</b> - it leaves the Sheets page and Folders, nothing is deleted, and <b>Set ▾ &gt; Archived sets &gt; Bring back</b> restores it; <b>Delete set</b> - its sheets and their PDFs; a window lists the set's <b>files kept in Folders</b> and asks: <b>Delete the set, keep the files</b> or <b>Delete the set and its files</b> (they go to the Folders bin, where they can be restored). Markups and issues on deleted sheets stay in the project. The menu's actions are buttons; <b>Delete set</b> is the red one.</li><li>Each browser tab keeps its own project (it shows in the address), so two projects can be open side by side and each issue is saved in its own.</li><li>The zoom says <b>100%</b> when the sheet fits the window's width (<b>Fit</b>); 200% is twice that. With no markups or issues yet, the issue list folds away to its edge (the tab there brings it back, and it then stays open). The grey bar at the bottom starts with <b>which version you are looking at</b>: <i>Output 21 Oct 2026, 14:05 · Rev C (15/10/2026)</i> - when the sheet was output from Revit and its current revision - or <i>Uploaded ... by ...</i> for an uploaded PDF (a sheet published before this shows <i>Published ...</i>, the time of its publish).</li><li><b>Where the file comes from:</b> <b>Files &gt; A PDF drawing</b> or <b>A CAD drawing</b> first asks: <b>Files on this PC ...</b> (the usual file picker), for CAD also <b>A folder on this PC ...</b>, or <b>From Folders ...</b> - a file already in the project's Folders (e.g. 01 Incoming): browse to it and tick one or more. A file taken from Folders stays where it is there (nothing more is kept).</li><li><b>CAD drawings:</b> <b>Files &gt; A CAD drawing (DWG / DXF)</b> - choose the drawing(s), or a whole folder (or one .zip). Tick the drawings to make into sheets (files in a folder named like Xref are left unticked); name the set; choose black lines (as plotted) or the drawing's colours; and where the CAD files are kept in Folders (by default <b>00 BIM &gt; Import &gt; CAD &gt; (the set)</b>, or <b>Change folder ...</b>, or <b>Don't keep a copy</b>). <b>Each layout becomes a sheet</b>: its border and title block, and each viewport's view of the model at its scale, with the xrefs and the layers frozen in that viewport left out. Sheet numbers come from the layout names (A-101 ...). <b>The xrefs are found by themselves:</b> the drawings are read first, and each xref they use (and the xrefs' own xrefs) is taken from the files or folder chosen on this PC - only the ones needed are sent - then from anywhere in the project's <b>Folders</b> (the newest copy). Only what is still missing is asked for: <b>Choose files ...</b>, <b>Choose a folder ...</b> or <b>Make the sheets without them</b> (they are then listed as not found). No need to bind the xrefs. Long file names, and names with &amp; or brackets, are fine. Fonts are drawn with a standard font and complex line types as plain dashes; 3D views, images and OLE objects are not drawn - for the exact look, publish a PDF from AutoCAD and import that. DWG needs the <b>ODA File Converter</b> on the server (the server's admin installs it once); DXF works without it.</li></ul>"},{"id":"s24","ch":"Sheets (2D)","h":"Moving around a sheet","lv":3,"html":"<table><tr><th>Action</th><th>Mouse</th><th>iPad / touch</th></tr><tr><td>Zoom</td><td>Scroll wheel (zooms round the pointer)</td><td>Pinch</td></tr><tr><td>Pan</td><td>Hold the middle button, or the <b>Pan</b> tool (H)</td><td>Two fingers; after you use an Apple Pencil, one finger pans</td></tr><tr><td>Whole sheet</td><td><b>Fit</b></td><td><b>Fit</b></td></tr><tr><td>Rotate the page</td><td>Rotate button in the toolbar</td><td>Same</td></tr><tr><td>Menu</td><td>Right-click</td><td>Long press</td></tr><tr><td>Undo / redo</td><td>Ctrl+Z / Ctrl+Y</td><td>Two-finger tap / three-finger tap</td></tr></table>"},{"id":"s25","ch":"Sheets (2D)","h":"Useful sheet tools","lv":3,"html":"<figure class=\"shot\"><img src=\"help-img/sheet-view-menu.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><ol><li>View: the menu below</li><li>Split: a second sheet beside this one</li><li>Compare: with an earlier version - red removed, green added</li><li>2D + 3D: the model beside the sheet, in step</li><li>Links: section marks and callouts open their sheets</li></ol></figure><p><b>Split</b>, <b>Compare</b>, <b>2D + 3D</b> and <b>Links</b> are under <b>View ▾</b> in the sheet toolbar (a dot on View says Split, Compare or 2D + 3D is on). The markup properties bar (layer, line, fill, text, font) shows only while a drawing tool is in hand or markups are selected, and the <b>1:</b> scale only with Measure, Dimension, Area and Angle - the rest of the time the drawing gets the room. <b>👁 Markups</b> and <b>Hide closed</b> are at the top of the issue list on the right, as on the 3D page.</p><ul><li><b>Split</b> opens a second sheet beside the first, with its own zoom.</li><li><b>Links</b> turns section marks, callouts and elevation markers into links to their sheets; <b>← back</b> returns.</li><li><b>Compare</b> shows what changed against an earlier upload of the same sheet, another sheet, or a PDF from your computer: red = removed, green = added. <b>N / Shift+N</b> jump between changes.</li><li><b>2D + 3D</b> opens the 3D model beside the sheet. Choose <b>Stand there</b> or <b>Look at</b>, then click a plan: the 3D view goes to that spot. A \"you are here\" marker on the plan follows the 3D camera; tick <b>Follow</b> to keep it in view and switch plans as you walk between floors. Only plan views take part, not sections or elevations.</li></ul><figure class=\"shot\"><img src=\"help-img/sheet-split.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><ol><li>View &gt; Split</li><li>The sheet you opened</li><li>The second sheet: pick any sheet of the project</li><li>Zoom the second sheet on its own: -, +, Fit</li><li>The second sheet</li><li>Close the split</li></ol></figure><figure class=\"shot\"><img src=\"help-img/sheet-compare.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><ol><li>Compare with: an earlier upload of this sheet, another sheet, or a PDF</li><li>Changes, Earlier or Current</li><li>Red: removed; green: added; grey: unchanged</li><li>Step through the changed areas</li><li>Outline: a box round each changed area</li><li>What it was compared with</li><li>The drawing, coloured by the changes</li><li>Close Compare</li></ol></figure><figure class=\"shot\"><img src=\"help-img/sheet-2d3d.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><ol><li>You: where you stand, and the way you look</li><li>Stand there: click the plan to stand at that point</li><li>Look at: click the plan to turn to that point</li><li>Walk through the model</li><li>Follow: the plan keeps you in view as you move</li><li>Issue: raise an issue at a point in the 3D</li><li>Issues: show the pins; Depth: depth shading</li><li>What the mode does (walking: W A S D, drag to look)</li><li>Open the full 3D page; close</li><li>Models: which to show</li><li>The model, in step with the plan</li><li>Walking: Stop to end the walk</li></ol></figure>"},{"id":"s26","ch":"Sheets (2D)","h":"Markup tools","lv":3,"html":"<figure class=\"shot\"><img src=\"help-img/markup-tools.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><ol><li>Select (V): pick, move and change mark-ups</li><li>Pan (H): move the sheet</li><li>Shapes: rectangle, circle, line, arrow, polyline, polygon - the arrow beside lists them</li><li>Clouds: the usual issue mark, or a free shape</li><li>Pen and highlighter</li><li>Text, text box, callout</li><li>Stamp: Approved, Rejected ...</li><li>Measure, dimension, area, angle - at the sheet's scale</li><li>Snip, select text, eraser, match properties</li><li>Keyboard shortcuts: one key per tool</li></ol></figure><table><tr><th>Group</th><th>Tools</th></tr><tr><td>Shapes</td><td>Rect, Circle, Line, Arrow, Cloud, Polyline, Polygon</td></tr><tr><td>Freehand</td><td>Pen (hold still at the end of a stroke to snap it to a line, circle or rectangle), Highlighter</td></tr><tr><td>Text</td><td>Text, Text box, Callout</td></tr><tr><td>Stamps</td><td>APPROVED, APPROVED AS NOTED, REVISE &amp; RESUBMIT, REJECTED, REVIEWED, FOR INFORMATION, VOID (signed with your name and time)</td></tr><tr><td>Measuring</td><td>Measure, Dimension, Area, Angle (use the scale in the <b>1:</b> box, or the view's own scale when it is empty)</td></tr><tr><td>Other</td><td>Snip (copies a region as an image; you can also paste an image), Select text, Eraser, Match properties, Select, Pan</td></tr></table><ul><li><b>Polyline / Polygon:</b> click the points, then press Enter, double-click or <b>✓ Finish</b>. Backspace removes the last point.</li><li><b>Style bar:</b> Layer, Line / Fill / Text colour, Opacity, Weight (paper mm), line Type, Font, Size (text height in mm), Align.</li><li><b>Editing:</b> select a markup to move, resize or restyle it; R / Shift+R rotate it 90°; Ctrl+C / Ctrl+V copy and paste (paste on another sheet lands at the same spot); Delete removes it.</li><li><b>Comment or Issue:</b> the <b>Comment / + Issue</b> switch on the drawing's toolbar decides what happens when you finish a markup. In <b>Issue</b> mode the <b>Raise issue</b> window opens straight away. A comment can be turned into an issue later with <b>Issue</b> or right-click <b>Raise issue</b>.</li><li><b>Layers:</b> markups sit on layers (default \"General\"). Admins can lock a layer or hide it from some people. <b>👁 Markups</b> at the top of the issue list hides all markups.</li></ul>"},{"id":"s27","ch":"Sheets (2D)","h":"Exporting","lv":3,"html":"<ul><li><b>PDF</b> (download) exports this sheet, every sheet with markups, or all sheets, with markups either <b>Editable</b> (real PDF comments for Bluebeam, Acrobat or PDF-XChange) or <b>Flattened</b>, at 100, 150 or 200 dpi, optionally with an issue report at the end.</li><li><b>JSON</b> (download / upload) saves or loads all comments and issues, for backup or moving between projects.</li><li><b>BCF</b> exports the sheet issues for Revit or Navisworks (see Issues and BCF).</li></ul>"},{"id":"s28","ch":"3D: moving around","h":"3D: moving around","lv":2,"html":"<figure class=\"shot\"><img src=\"help-img/model.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><ol><li>Floor: cut the model at a floor, seen as a plan</li><li>Perspective or parallel view</li><li>Issue pins: show or hide the issues on the model</li><li>Plan overlay: lay the sheet over the model</li><li>More: copy a link to this view, BCF, set front / world, + Task</li><li>Orbit: turn, pan and zoom the model</li><li>Walk through it at eye level</li><li>Fit: the whole model</li><li>Section box on or off</li><li>Measure with snapping</li><li>+ Add issue: click the model to place one</li><li>The project's models - tick to show</li><li>Elements: show or hide each category</li><li>The view cube: click a face; Home for the overview</li><li>Selection: the clicked element's properties (one line until you click one)</li><li>Issues in 3D: the list, with filters</li></ol></figure><p>The 3D page uses the same mouse as most BIM viewers: right button orbits, middle button pans, wheel zooms, left button picks.</p>"},{"id":"s29","ch":"3D: moving around","h":"Mouse, touch and keys","lv":3,"html":"<table><tr><th>Action</th><th>Mouse</th><th>iPad / iPhone</th></tr><tr><td>Orbit</td><td>Hold the right button and drag</td><td>One finger</td></tr><tr><td>Pan</td><td>Hold the middle button (wheel) and drag</td><td>Two fingers</td></tr><tr><td>Zoom</td><td>Scroll wheel (towards the pointer)</td><td>Pinch</td></tr><tr><td>Focus on a surface</td><td>Double-click it</td><td>Double tap</td></tr><tr><td>Select an element</td><td>Left click</td><td>Tap</td></tr><tr><td>Set the orbit centre</td><td>Right-click without dragging, or right-click menu <b>Set orbit centre here</b></td><td>-</td></tr><tr><td>Menu of actions</td><td>Right-click</td><td>-</td></tr><tr><td>New issue at a spot</td><td><b>Add issue</b>, then click</td><td>Long press (0.6 s)</td></tr><tr><td>Floor above / below</td><td>Page Up / Page Down</td><td>Floor plan list</td></tr><tr><td>Cancel measure or walk</td><td>Esc</td><td>Stop button</td></tr></table><p>With a mouse the view stops exactly where you let go; with a finger it glides a little, as on any tablet app.</p>"},{"id":"s30","ch":"3D: moving around","h":"Right-click menu","lv":3,"html":"<p>On an element: <b>Set orbit centre here</b>, <b>Zoom to this element</b>, <b>Isolate</b>, <b>Hide</b>, <b>Show all</b>, <b>Walk from here</b>, <b>Add issue here</b>, <b>Section box around this element</b>, <b>See-through</b> (this element, its type, or its whole category), <b>Make all solid again</b>, <b>Section on this face</b>, <b>Square section box to this face</b>, <b>Turn section on/off</b>, <b>Measure</b>, <b>Save view...</b>, <b>Fit model</b>. On empty space: Show all, Turn section on/off, Measure, Save view..., Fit model.</p>"},{"id":"s31","ch":"3D: moving around","h":"View cube and camera","lv":3,"html":"<ul><li>Click a <b>face</b> of the cube for that view, an <b>edge</b> for the view between two faces, a <b>corner</b> for an isometric view. Drag the cube to orbit. The ring under it shows north.</li><li>The house button returns to the 3D overview. Under the cube: <b>Walk</b> (see Walking through the model) and <b>Fit</b>, which frames all loaded models - or, with a section box on, what is inside the box.</li><li><b>Perspective / Parallel</b> switches the projection (plans are always parallel).</li><li><b>Set front:</b> click a wall to tell the cube which way is \"Front\" for this building; <b>World</b> goes back to the world axes.</li></ul>"},{"id":"s32","ch":"3D: moving around","h":"Floors","lv":3,"html":"<ul><li>The <b>Floor plan</b> drop-down (in the 3D header with <b>Navigate / Add issue / Measure</b>, <b>Plan overlay</b>, the view link and <b>BCF</b> - all on one line on a wide window, on the second line on a smaller one) lists <b>Whole building</b> and every level from the top down. <b>Search</b>, the bell and <b>+ Task</b> are at the top right, as on every page.</li><li>Picking a level cuts the model from 0.5 m below to 1.2 m above that floor and looks straight down, like a Revit plan.</li><li><b>Page Up / Page Down</b> step up and down; <b>Whole building</b> returns to the full 3D model.</li><li><b>Plan overlay</b> (beside the floor list) lays that floor's plan sheet over the model, so you can compare drawing and model.</li></ul><figure class=\"shot\"><img src=\"help-img/model-floorplan.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><ol><li>Floor plan: cut the model at a floor</li><li>Plan overlay: lay the floor's sheet on the cut</li><li>Which drawing</li><li>The drawing over the cut, with its annotations and dimensions</li><li>Which drawing is shown</li></ol></figure>"},{"id":"s33","ch":"3D: moving around","h":"Models panel","lv":3,"html":"<ul><li>One tick box per model (the host model and each link). Untick to hide a model and free memory; <b>All on / All off</b> switch them together and keep your view.</li><li><b>▸</b> beside a model shows its size and number of copies, and <b>Compare with previous export</b> to see what was added, changed or removed since the last publish.</li><li><b>Apply link transforms</b> (on) places links where they sit in Revit.</li><li><b>Light mode (phones, tablets)</b> loads repeated typical floors only near where you are looking. It is on by default on phones and tablets.</li><li><b>In stages:</b> the main model shows as soon as it has loaded, and you can work at once; the other models keep loading behind it, the ones nearest your view first (\"Main model ready - N more model(s) loading behind it\").</li><li><b>Open with the main model only</b> (under the list, remembered on this device): only the main model loads on opening; another model loads when you tick it or come near it. Useful on a slow connection or a computer with little memory.</li><li>Every panel heading (Models, Section, Measure, and so on) folds away when clicked, and stays folded next time.</li></ul><p>The left panel is in three coloured groups, so a topic is quick to find:</p><table><tr><th>Group</th><th>Colour</th><th>Sections</th></tr><tr><td><b>Model</b></td><td>Blue</td><td>Models, Elements, Model browser - what is loaded and what is in it</td></tr><tr><td><b>Tools</b></td><td>Teal</td><td>Section, Measure, Checks - working on the model</td></tr><tr><td><b>View</b></td><td>Amber</td><td>Display, Saved views - how it looks</td></tr></table><p>On the model: the <b>toolbar at the bottom</b> has <b>Orbit</b>, <b>Walk</b>, <b>Fit</b>, <b>Section box</b>, <b>Measure</b> and <b>+ Add issue</b>; the <b>chips at the top left</b> are <b>Floor</b> (cut the model at a floor), <b>Perspective</b>, <b>Issue pins</b> (show or hide them), <b>Plan overlay</b> and <b>⋯</b> (copy a link to this view, BCF, Set front / World, + Task). The view cube keeps its <b>Home</b>. <b>Shaded / White / X-ray</b> and <b>Depth</b> are at the top of <b>Display</b>; <b>Hide closed</b> is at the top of <b>Issues in 3D</b> on the right. The Selection panel stays one line until you click an element. On a tablet the side panels slide in from the buttons at the top left; on a phone they come up from the bottom.</p>"},{"id":"s34","ch":"3D: selecting, finding and display","h":"3D: selecting, finding and display","lv":2,"html":"<p>Click any element to see what it is; use the Model browser to find elements by name, type, level or property.</p>"},{"id":"s35","ch":"3D: selecting, finding and display","h":"The Selection panel","lv":3,"html":"<p>A click shows the element's <b>Model</b>, <b>Category</b>, <b>Family / type</b>, <b>Level</b>, <b>Revit id</b> (ElementId), <b>UniqueId</b>, <b>IFC GUID</b>, the clicked <b>Point</b> (x, y, z in metres) and <b>Shared E,N,Z</b> (survey coordinates), followed by all its Revit parameters in folding groups.</p><ul><li><b>Copy Revit ID</b> copies the ElementId; in Revit use <b>Manage &gt; Select by ID</b> and paste it to select the same element there. <b>Show in Revit</b> asks the LWK add-in to select it (see Revit elements). <b>+ Task</b> keeps the element on a task.</li><li><b>Isolate</b> shows only the selected element(s). <b>Hide</b> hides them. <b>Show all</b> brings everything back. A counter shows how many are hidden.</li><li>Hiding and isolating only change your own view. Nothing is deleted.</li></ul>"},{"id":"s36","ch":"3D: selecting, finding and display","h":"Elements panel","lv":3,"html":"<p>One tick box per category (Walls, Floors and slabs, Columns, Windows, Doors, Furniture, Railings...) with a count. Untick a category to hide it; <b>Show all</b> turns them all back on. Your choice is remembered.</p>"},{"id":"s37","ch":"3D: selecting, finding and display","h":"Model browser","lv":3,"html":"<ul><li>A tree of <b>model › category › family / type › elements</b>. Click a row to open it and pick that group; click an element to highlight and zoom to it.</li><li><b>Search names, types, levels, properties</b>: plain words match name, category, family, type and level. Use <b>property:value</b> to match a parameter, for example Fire Rating:2 hr or Mark:D101.</li><li><b>Select</b> colours what you found, <b>Isolate</b> shows only that, <b>Zoom</b> frames it. After <b>Select</b>, <b>+ Task</b> at the top keeps all the selected elements on a task as \"Elements to change\", and <b>Copy Revit ID</b> copies all their ids.</li><li>The browser works with models published in the fast 3D format (the normal Publish to Viewer output).</li></ul>"},{"id":"s38","ch":"3D: selecting, finding and display","h":"Display","lv":3,"html":"<figure class=\"shot\"><img src=\"help-img/model-display.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><ol><li>Shaded, White or X-ray</li><li>Depth: depth shading</li><li>Background colour</li><li>Ground and its colour</li><li>Grid</li><li>Depth shading: shadow and edges, their colours</li><li>Usual depth shading</li><li>Saved views: Save keeps the camera, section and what is shown</li></ol></figure><table><tr><th>Mode</th><th>Use it for</th></tr><tr><td><b>Shaded</b></td><td>Normal viewing with the model's own colours</td></tr><tr><td><b>White</b></td><td>A clean, colour-free look for reviews and screenshots</td></tr><tr><td><b>X-ray</b></td><td>See through walls and floors to what is inside</td></tr></table><p>These three buttons, and <b>Depth</b> (soft shadows in corners and lines on edges), are at the top of the <b>Display</b> panel, which also sets the background colour, the ground (on/off and colour), the grid and the depth shading.</p>"},{"id":"s39","ch":"3D: selecting, finding and display","h":"Saved views","lv":3,"html":"<ul><li><b>Save</b> (or right-click <b>Save view...</b>) stores the camera, section and hidden elements with a name and a thumbnail. Saved views are shared with the whole project.</li><li>Click a saved view to return to it; <b>✕</b> deletes it.</li><li>When you go from 3D to Sheets and back, your last 3D view comes back as you left it.</li></ul>"},{"id":"s40","ch":"Section box, section plane and floor plans","h":"Section box, section plane and floor plans","lv":2,"html":"<p>Use the section box to cut a part of the building open, and a section plane to cut along any surface; cut solids show an orange hatch, as on a drawing.</p>"},{"id":"s41","ch":"Section box, section plane and floor plans","h":"Section tools","lv":3,"html":"<figure class=\"shot\"><img src=\"help-img/model-tools.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><ol><li>Box: a section box round the model - drag its orange arrows</li><li>Plane: click a face to cut there</li><li>Align, Flip, Reset the cut</li><li>Solid fill on the cut; plan look for floor plans</li><li>Measure: Distance, Angle, Area</li><li>Straight: along X, Y or Z only</li><li>Undo, Clear; Keep makes a dimension that stays</li><li>Show the kept dimensions</li><li>Checks: Clash, Headroom, SBD</li><li>The clash rule to run</li><li>+ a new rule; ✎ edit; ✕ delete</li><li>Where: whole model, floors, or inside the section box</li><li>Run</li></ol></figure><table><tr><th>Button</th><th>What it does</th></tr><tr><td><b>Box</b> (tick)</td><td>Turns the section box on, fitted round the whole project</td></tr><tr><td><b>Plane</b></td><td>Click a surface: the model is cut on that face</td></tr><tr><td><b>Align</b></td><td>Click a wall: the box turns square to that wall</td></tr><tr><td><b>Flip</b></td><td>Keeps the other side of the section plane</td></tr><tr><td><b>Reset</b></td><td>Removes all cuts</td></tr><tr><td><b>Solid fill on the cut</b></td><td>Cut walls, slabs and columns show an orange hatch (on by default)</td></tr><tr><td><b>Plan look for floor plans</b></td><td>In a floor plan, surfaces are paler and floors below fade out (on by default)</td></tr></table><p>The Floor plan drop-down (see 3D: moving around) is a ready-made section box for one storey.</p>"},{"id":"s42","ch":"Section box, section plane and floor plans","h":"Moving a cut","lv":3,"html":"<ul><li>Each face of the box has a <b>coloured dot on a short stem</b>: red for X, green for Y, blue for height. The single section plane has an orange dot.</li><li><b>Mouse:</b> hover over a dot, or over the edge of a cut face (the face lights up orange), then drag. The cut only moves along its own direction.</li><li><b>iPad / iPhone:</b> drag a dot with one finger. Two fingers always move the view, never the cut, so you can pinch and orbit freely while a section is on.</li><li>On a computer, a brown outline traces the cut edges once the cut stops moving. Phones and tablets show the hatch only.</li></ul>"},{"id":"s43","ch":"Section box, section plane and floor plans","h":"Handy shortcuts","lv":3,"html":"<ul><li>Right-click a wall or floor: <b>Section on this face</b> cuts right there; <b>Square section box to this face</b> lines the box up with it.</li><li>Right-click empty space: <b>Turn section on/off</b>.</li><li><b>Section box round one element:</b> click it and press <b>Section box</b> in the Selection panel, or right-click it &gt; <b>Section box around this element</b>. The box closes round that element with a little room on every side, and the view moves to it. In the <b>Model browser</b>, tick or pick a group (a category, a type, a level) and press <b>Section box</b> for a box round all of them.</li></ul>"},{"id":"s44","ch":"Section box, section plane and floor plans","h":"See-through elements","lv":3,"html":"<p>To look past walls, floors or ceilings without hiding them, make them see-through: they stay in place as a pale screen, and a click goes through them to what is behind.</p><ul><li><b>One element:</b> click it, then <b>See-through</b> in the Selection panel; or right-click &gt; <b>See-through: this element</b>.</li><li><b>Its type or its whole category:</b> right-click &gt; <b>See-through: its type (n)</b> or <b>See-through: all Walls (n)</b> (the name of its category).</li><li><b>A chosen group:</b> in the <b>Model browser</b>, search or pick a category, type or level and press <b>See-through</b>.</li><li>The Selection panel counts them (<b>5 see-through</b>). <b>Show all</b>, or right-click &gt; <b>Make all solid again</b>, makes them solid.</li></ul>"},{"id":"s45","ch":"Measuring in 3D","h":"Measuring in 3D","lv":2,"html":"<p>Every measured point snaps to a real corner, edge or midpoint, and the label tells you which, so you know whether to trust the figure.</p>"},{"id":"s46","ch":"Measuring in 3D","h":"How to measure","lv":3,"html":"<ol><li>Click <b>Measure</b> on the toolbar at the bottom (or right-click <b>Measure</b>) and choose <b>Distance</b>, <b>Angle</b> or <b>Area</b>.</li><li>Move the pointer over the model. A coloured dot and label show the snap under it.</li><li>Click the first point, then the next. The distance updates live as you move, with its <b>plan</b> and <b>height</b> parts.</li><li>Press <b>Esc</b> to drop a measurement you started by mistake.</li></ol><table><tr><th>Mode</th><th>Points</th><th>Result</th></tr><tr><td><b>Distance</b></td><td>2</td><td>Length (mm under 1 m, otherwise m), plus plan and height parts</td></tr><tr><td><b>Angle</b></td><td>3</td><td>Degrees at the middle point</td></tr><tr><td><b>Area</b></td><td>3 to 64</td><td>Area in m² of the polygon</td></tr></table>"},{"id":"s47","ch":"Measuring in 3D","h":"Snaps","lv":3,"html":"<table><tr><th>Colour</th><th>Snap</th><th>Meaning</th></tr><tr><td>Red</td><td>corner</td><td>A vertex of the element, or a corner of the cut in a section</td></tr><tr><td>Purple</td><td>midpoint</td><td>The middle of an edge</td></tr><tr><td>Green</td><td>perpendicular</td><td>The foot of a square line from your last point to an edge</td></tr><tr><td>Blue</td><td>edge</td><td>Anywhere along an edge</td></tr><tr><td>Grey</td><td>surface</td><td>No feature nearby: the point on the face (less exact)</td></tr></table><ul><li>A ring runs out from each new snap (and the phone vibrates) so you know it caught.</li><li>In a floor plan or section, the snaps follow the cut outline, so you can measure wall to wall in plan.</li><li>Curved surfaces are made of small flat faces, so there is no tangent or centre-of-arc snap yet.</li></ul>"},{"id":"s48","ch":"Measuring in 3D","h":"Straight and other buttons","lv":3,"html":"<ul><li><b>Straight</b> keeps the next point in line with the last one along X, Y or height, for true orthogonal distances. Hold <b>Shift</b> to switch it for one point.</li><li><b>Undo</b> removes the last point, <b>Clear</b> removes all measurements.</li><li><b>Keep</b> saves a finished distance as a dimension that everyone on the project sees. The <b>Dimensions</b> tick box shows or hides kept dimensions, and each one can be removed with <b>✕</b>.</li></ul>"},{"id":"s49","ch":"Clash and headroom checks","h":"Clash and headroom checks","lv":2,"html":"<p>The <b>Checks</b> section of the 3D page's left panel finds elements that run into each other, and places where the clear height is too low - in the project's own model and against the consultants' models loaded with it. It checks what the viewer draws (Revit at medium detail, the IFC as converted): quick everyday coordination, not a formal clash report.</p>"},{"id":"s50","ch":"Clash and headroom checks","h":"Clash: a rule, then Run","lv":3,"html":"<figure class=\"shot\"><img src=\"help-img/clash-rule.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><ol><li>Name the rule</li><li>Set A: the models and categories on one side</li><li>Set B: what A is checked against (A and B can be the same model)</li><li>A saved set of models and categories; Save as set</li><li>The models: ours and the consultants'</li><li>Categories (All / None)</li><li>Name has / has not: only some elements</li><li>Overlap that counts; clearance round A</li><li>Leave out doors and windows in their walls</li><li>Leave out the joins Revit cleans up</li><li>Open surfaces crossing each other</li><li>Save the rule (shared with the project)</li></ol></figure><ol><li>Load the models you want in the Models panel (a consultant's IFC, another project overlaid).</li><li>Checks &gt; <b>Clash</b> &gt; <b>+</b>. Name the rule, and choose <b>Set A</b> and <b>Set B</b>: on each side tick one or more models (or <b>All models</b>, which also takes in links loaded later) and the categories to check - for example <i>Ceilings</i> in the architectural model against <i>Beams</i> in the structural one, or <i>Walls</i> in every architectural link against <i>Ducts</i> and <i>Pipes</i> in every MEP link. A and B can be the same models: clashes inside them. <b>All</b> / <b>None</b> above the models tick or untick them all at once. <b>Name has</b> / <b>Name has not</b> keeps only elements with (or without) those words in their name, type or family - for example <i>Name has not: Finish</i> (a comma between words: any of them).</li><li><b>Selection sets</b> (like Navisworks): <b>Save as set</b> keeps a side's models, categories and name filter under a name, shared with the project. In any rule, pick it from the list at the top of a side. A rule following a set checks the set as it is now, so changing the set (pick it, change the ticks, <b>Save as set</b> with the same name) changes every rule using it. <b>Delete set</b> removes it; rules that used it keep its selection.</li><li><b>Overlap that counts</b> (default 10 mm): two elements overlapping less than this are touching, not clashing. <b>Clearance</b>: also report elements that come closer than this without touching (0 = off).</li><li>Choose where: <b>Whole model</b>, <b>Floors</b> from one floor to another, or <b>Inside the section box</b> (quicker on a big model), then <b>Run</b>. When very many elements touch (more than 30,000 pairs), the panel says how many and about how long it takes, with <b>Check them all</b> (it runs with a progress bar; <b>Stop</b> keeps what is found so far) or <b>Choose floors instead</b>.</li></ol><p>The three options at the bottom of a rule:</p><table><tr><th>Option</th><th>What it does</th></tr><tr><td><b>Leave out doors and windows in their walls, floors and roofs</b></td><td>A door or a window always sits inside the wall it is in; without this, every one is reported against its own wall.</td></tr><tr><td><b>Leave out joins between walls, floors, roofs, columns, beams and stairs</b></td><td>Where these meet (a wall on a slab, a finish under a wall, a landing into a wall) Revit cleans the join up, but each element is exported whole, so they overlap. On: only one mostly inside the other (a duplicate, one buried in another) counts. Services, furniture and ceilings are not affected. Off: every join is listed - usually hundreds.</td></tr><tr><td><b>Report open surfaces crossing each other</b></td><td>Some elements are surfaces, not closed solids (some IFC exports, a pipe without end caps); they have no inside, so how deep they cross cannot be measured. Off: a surface counts only where it goes into a solid. On: two surfaces that just cross are reported too - more thorough, more noise.</td></tr></table><p>Rules are shared: everyone on the project sees them under the rule list, can run them and change them, and sees the last result (people who can only view can run a rule, but its result is not saved). A consultant model is named by its name and company, so a rule still works after they send the next version.</p><table><tr><th>Shown as</th><th>Meaning</th></tr><tr><td><b>Overlap 120 mm</b></td><td>The two solids overlap; the figure is how deep, at the thinnest</td></tr><tr><td><b>Inside</b></td><td>One element is buried in the other (a pipe inside a wall)</td></tr><tr><td><b>Too close 30 mm apart</b></td><td>They do not touch, but are closer than the clearance</td></tr><tr><td><b>Crossing</b></td><td>Two surfaces that are not closed solids cross each other (no depth can be given) - only when the rule ticks <b>Report open surfaces crossing each other</b></td></tr></table><ul><li>Not reported: walls butting into each other, walls standing on floors, layered walls and floors touching (a millimetre or two either way is touching), and (ticked by default) doors and windows in their walls, floors and roofs. An open surface (not a closed solid) against a solid is measured by how deep it goes in.</li><li><b>Leave out joins</b> (ticked by default): walls, floors, roofs, columns, beams and stairs overlap where they meet in the exported models - a wall through a slab, a finish or waterproofing under a wall, a landing into a wall, a beam into a wall or column. These are not reported. A duplicate element, two walls overlapping side by side, or anything through a ceiling still is.</li><li>The list shows the clashes of the place chosen above it: the whole model, the floors chosen, or inside the section box, with when it was last checked there (\"Not checked on L2 yet\" until it is). Clashes found elsewhere in earlier runs are kept: \"<i>N</i> more elsewhere\" - <b>Show</b> lists them too.</li><li><b>Hide under ... mm</b> above the list hides shallower overlaps without running again (kept per rule on this computer); <b>Deepest first</b> sorts the list by depth.</li><li>Clashes that sit together and share an element are grouped (\"5 clashes around Beam 12\").</li><li>Click a clash: the storey is cut out round it with a section box a few metres across, the two elements are coloured (A orange, B blue - choose your own colours with the two colour boxes <b>A</b> and <b>B</b> above the list; they are kept on this computer) and a red dot marks the spot. A key at the bottom left of the 3D view says which element is A and which is B. When both are in the same Revit model they share colour A (one highlight colour per model), and the key says so. <b>Section off</b> shows the whole model again; <b>Only these</b> hides everything else (<b>Show all</b> brings it back).</li><li><b>Make issue</b> opens the issue form filled in: the title <b>Clash issue 007 - Ducts x Beams (L2)</b> (numbered in turn for the project), a description with both elements (model, category, name, type, id), the kind and depth, the floor and where in project coordinates, and the due date <b>3 working days</b> ahead (Monday to Friday, Hong Kong public holidays left out). Assign it and Save; it can be sent by BCF to Revit or Navisworks.</li><li><b>Raise issues for all <i>N</b></i> (over the list) raises one such issue for every clash listed that is open, not <i>Not an issue</i> and has no issue yet - each shown and pictured in turn (<b>Stop</b> ends it). Type a name in <b>Assign to</b> first to give them all to one person.</li><li><b>Save view:</b> turn the view, move the section box or hide elements until the clash is clear, then <b>Save view</b> on it. The clash opens at that view for everyone (📷 <i>view</i> beside it), its issue - one at a time or Raise issues for all - is raised from it, and a saved result keeps it. <b>Clear view</b> forgets it.</li><li><b>Not an issue</b> keeps that pair off the list in every later run and in the saved results too (find them under <b>Not an issue</b>; <b>Count again</b> undoes it).</li><li><b>Save result</b> (beside the result list) keeps the result shown under a name, for everyone on the project - as many as needed (before and after a design freeze, each consultant issue). Pick one in the list above the clashes to look at it again; <b>Latest run</b> goes back. Its author or a project admin can <b>Delete</b> it.</li><li><b>Consultant IFC models:</b> the rule form lists the project's consultant models even when they are not loaded on the page (<i>consultant IFC - not loaded</i>): ticking one loads it. <b>All consultant models</b> takes every one, <b>All LWK BIM models</b> every model of our own; <b>Our models x consultant models</b> fills in a rule of our models against all the consultants' models, every category. When the rule runs, the consultant models it names are loaded first.</li><li><b>Export the list</b>: <b>Spreadsheet</b> saves the clashes listed as a CSV file for Excel (status, kind, depth, floor, both elements with their ids, where in project coordinates, the issue). <b>Report</b> opens a report in a new tab - <b>With pictures</b> shows and pictures each clash in turn (about a second each; <b>Stop</b> ends it), <b>Without</b> is immediate - then <b>Print / Save as PDF</b>, or <b>Save to Folders (PDF)</b> to keep it in the project's Folders. Allow pop-ups for the site if the browser blocks the tab.</li><li><b>Run again</b> after a new publish or a new consultant model: each clash is marked <b>New</b>, still there, or <b>Gone</b>. A clash that has gone still shows its issue, so it can be closed.</li></ul><figure class=\"shot\"><img src=\"help-img/clash-results.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><ol><li>Floors from ... to ...</li><li>The latest run, or a saved result</li><li>Save result: keep this run</li><li>Set A and B, and their colours in the model</li><li>Hide clashes smaller than</li><li>Group the list: by floor, category ...</li><li>Open, New since the last run, Gone, Not an issue</li><li>Raise issues for all of them</li><li>Export the list: spreadsheet, report</li><li>A clash: inside or overlap, depth, floor; Make issue, Only these, Section off, Save view, Not an issue</li><li>The clash in the model, cut out round it</li><li>What the colours are</li><li>What is shown; Section off shows the whole model</li></ol></figure>"},{"id":"s51","ch":"Clash and headroom checks","h":"Headroom","lv":3,"html":"<figure class=\"shot\"><img src=\"help-img/headroom.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><ol><li>Checks &gt; Headroom</li><li>Probe: click a floor or a tread for the height to what is above</li><li>The least height over floors, and over stairs and ramps</li><li>Ignore lower than: leave out low things (a desk, a sill)</li><li>Models counted</li><li>Stood on: what you stand on</li><li>Overhead: what counts above you</li><li>Usual categories</li><li>Where: whole model, floors, or inside the section box</li><li>Scan</li></ol></figure><ul><li><b>Probe:</b> Checks &gt; <b>Headroom</b> &gt; <b>Probe</b>, then click a floor, a stair tread or a landing. A line goes straight up to the first thing above, with its height - red under the stair limit, amber under the floor limit, green otherwise. <b>Keep</b> saves it as a dimension for everyone. <b>Esc</b> stops.</li><li><b>Scan:</b> set the limits (<b>Floors</b>, default 2.30 m; <b>Stairs, ramps</b>, default 2.00 m; <b>Ignore lower than</b>, default 1.5 m - a lower space is not one people use: under a WC or a bench, in a duct or a ceiling void, where a stair runs in under the floor above), choose the floors (from ... to ...) or inside the section box, then <b>Scan</b>. Floors, stairs, landings and ramps are measured on a 0.25 m grid (0.2 m on stairs, finer under narrow ducts, pipes and beams) up to what is overhead: slabs, ceilings, beams, stairs above, ducts, pipes, trays, equipment.</li><li><b>Models counted</b> chooses which models count - tick the consultants' MEP and structure models to see their effect. <b>What counts</b> lists the categories <b>Stood on</b> and <b>Overhead</b>; furniture, WCs and basins, casework and generic models are not overhead unless ticked. <b>Usual categories</b> puts the defaults back. These settings are shared with everyone on the project.</li><li>Places under the limit are red squares on the floor (amber: within 100 mm over it), and each place is listed with its lowest height, what is overhead and its area. <b>Look</b> cuts the storey round it, colours what is overhead and draws the height where it is lowest (<b>Keep</b> saves it as a dimension); <b>Make issue</b> raises it. <b>Clear</b> takes the squares away. The colour box beside <i>under the limit</i> chooses its colour (kept on this computer); a key in the 3D view names what is overhead.</li><li><b>Export</b>: <b>Spreadsheet</b> (each place: floor, standing on, lowest height, limit, area, what is overhead, where) or <b>Report</b>, with or without a picture of each place, to print or save as PDF, or <b>Save to Folders (PDF)</b>.</li><li><b>Make issue</b>, <b>Raise issues for all</b>, <b>Not an issue</b> and <b>Save result</b> work as for clashes: issues are titled <b>Headroom issue 001 - 2.05 m under Ducts (L1)</b>, due in 3 working days; a place marked <i>Not an issue</i> stays so on every scan (it is known by the two elements and where it is, to half a metre); saved results are listed above the places for everyone. <b>Save view</b> keeps a view for a place, as for clashes. A headroom issue also keeps the height line: it is drawn again whenever the issue's view is opened.</li><li><b>Include consultant models</b> (under Models counted, on by default): the consultants' IFC models count too - those not loaded on the page are loaded when you scan.</li><li>A floor finish laid on a slab, or a stair standing on a floor, is not counted as overhead. Height is measured vertically from where people stand (on a stair, from the treads).</li></ul><figure class=\"shot\"><img src=\"help-img/headroom-results.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><ol><li>Scan the whole model or chosen floors</li><li>The probe: the height found; Keep makes it a dimension</li><li>This scan, or a saved result; Save result</li><li>Red: under the limit; orange: within 100 mm over it</li><li>Open, Not an issue</li><li>Raise issues for all of them</li><li>Export: spreadsheet, report</li><li>A low spot: height, limit, floor, what is above; Look, Make issue, Save view, Not an issue</li><li>The low area in red, with the height</li><li>What the colours are</li></ol></figure>"},{"id":"s52","ch":"Clash and headroom checks","h":"SBD: how to prepare the model and send it","lv":3,"html":"<p>What Checks &gt; <b>SBD</b> needs from Revit, and the steps to get the masses to the viewer. Everything is read from the model - nothing is drawn by hand for each zone.</p><p><b>Requirements</b></p><ul><li><b>Buildings as Masses:</b> each building (podium, each tower) as a <b>Mass</b> (Massing &amp; Site &gt; In-Place Mass, or a Mass family), modelled to its true height and shape. Voids through a block (a podium garden under a tower) are modelled as voids - they become PE. Floors, walls and rooms are not needed.</li><li><b>The masses stand on the ground:</b> the lowest mass starts at the zones' ground (mean street level); towers can start on the podium. A model on the wrong level shifts every zone - Checks &gt; SBD warns.</li><li><b>Site boundary:</b> a Property Line, or lines that close within 10 mm.</li><li><b>Streets:</b> each street fronting the site as a <b>Floor</b> whose type name has <b>Street</b>, <b>Road</b>, <b>Lane</b> or <b>Path</b> in it, drawn kerb to kerb at the street's level; its <b>type name</b> is the street's name on the drawings (e.g. a type <i>Yeung Fan Lane North Street</i>). A junction is not a strip - pick its centreline and the opposite boundary as lines instead. A street may be several Floors of the same type, or a sloped or shape-edited Floor: the slabs of one type that touch are joined into one street.</li><li><b>Neighbours</b> (optional): masses outside the site boundary are shown hatched and not counted.</li></ul><p><b>Steps</b></p><ol><li>In Revit, open the model and check the masses, the Property Line and the street floors (3D view: the masses sit on the street level).</li><li><b>LWK &gt; Viewer tools &gt; SBD Export.</b> Choose the site boundary; untick any street not fronting the site; choose the <b>viewer project</b> - it asks every time (an export replaces that project's SBD model), with the project last used with this Revit file listed first. The ground is not asked: Level 0 is the mean level of the lowest street abutting the site (each street's own slab level), or the masses' base when there is no street.</li><li>The masses go to the viewer and are assessed at once; the Revit window shows P, the required P and each street. The masses also appear in the project's 3D as <b>SBD masses - (model)</b>.</li><li>On the viewer, open the model's <b>3D</b> page &gt; <b>Checks &gt; SBD</b>. <b>Run</b> assesses again (the planes are found automatically); <b>Plan ...</b> shows each zone's plan and elevations with their working; <b>Save</b>, <b>Make issue</b> and <b>Report</b> keep the result.</li><li>After a design change, run <b>SBD Export</b> again - it replaces the masses and the result (saved results stay).</li></ol><p><b>If something looks wrong</b></p><ul><li><b>\"The lowest mass starts ... above the zones' ground\":</b> the ground or the masses are on the wrong level - export again choosing the right ground.</li><li><b>No street:</b> Plane X of the Low zone falls back to the site's main direction; model the street floors.</li><li><b>The masses' model sits in the wrong place in the 3D:</b> move it in the Models list (it is placed on the exporting model's internal origin).</li></ul>"},{"id":"s53","ch":"Clash and headroom checks","h":"SBD without Revit: draw the model in CAD","lv":3,"html":"<p>No Revit model? Draw the SBD model in AutoCAD (or SketchUp, Rhino, any program that saves DXF) on the <b>CAD template</b>'s layers and import it: it becomes the project's SBD model, assessed exactly as one sent from Revit, and its masses appear in the 3D.</p><p><b>Requirements</b></p><ul><li><b>Units:</b> metres (millimetres and centimetres are read from the drawing's units and scaled). Explode blocks - they are not read.</li><li><b>SBD-SITE:</b> the site boundary as <b>one closed polyline</b>.</li><li><b>SBD-STREET-&lt;street name&gt;:</b> each street's slab as a closed polyline from the site boundary to the far side of the street (the opposite site boundary), its <b>Elevation = the street's mean level</b>. One layer per street - <i>SBD-STREET-TLO Street</i>, <i>SBD-STREET-Second Street</i> - the name after the dash is the street's name; a street at two levels can have two slabs on its layer. Level 0 is the lowest street abutting the site.</li><li><b>SBD-MASS</b> (or <i>SBD-MASS-&lt;name&gt;</i>): the buildings as closed polylines with an <b>Elevation</b> (the base) and a <b>Thickness</b> (the height) - stack them for a podium and a tower - or as 3D faces, polyface meshes or MESH. An AutoCAD solid (3DSOLID) is not read: turn it into a mesh first (<b>CONVTOMESH</b>). SketchUp and Rhino save meshes.</li></ul><p><b>Steps</b></p><ol><li>On the 3D page &gt; <b>Checks &gt; SBD</b>, click <b>CAD template</b> (No Revit?) and open the DXF: the layers and the rules - with the project's <b>own site boundary and streets</b> when it has an SBD model (sent from Revit once), at <b>shared (survey) coordinates and mPD levels</b> when the project's 3D (its Revit export) says where they are; otherwise an example (a site, two streets, a podium and a tower). Keep the note <b>LWK-SBD-FRAME: SHARED</b> in the drawing: on import the drawing is brought back to the Revit model's origin, so the masses sit right in the 3D.</li><li>Draw your site, streets and masses on those layers (delete the example), in the site's own coordinates, and save as DXF (or DWG).</li><li><b>Import CAD model ...</b> and choose the file. It is read, assessed at once and shown as <i>CAD: (file name)</i>; notes on anything not read (a block, a solid, a polyline with no thickness, a street that is not a strip) are listed.</li><li>After a change, import the drawing again - it replaces the model and the result (saved results stay).</li></ol>"},{"id":"s54","ch":"Clash and headroom checks","h":"SBD (PNAP APP-152)","lv":3,"html":"<figure class=\"shot\"><img src=\"help-img/model-sbd.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><ol><li>Checks &gt; SBD (Clash and Headroom beside it)</li><li>Run the check again</li><li>Plan level for each zone (all levels, or one height)</li><li>Latest run, or a saved result; Save keeps this one</li><li>Permeability: P against the required P - PASS or FAIL</li><li>Design Requirement (1): Lp against 5U</li><li>P on Plane X and Y per zone - red: does not comply, green: complies</li><li>What the colours mean</li><li>Plan ...: plans, elevations and street canyons of each zone</li><li>3D: show or hide the SBD masses and zone limits in the model</li><li>Make issue: an issue for what fails</li><li>Report: every zone's plan and working, to print</li><li>CAD ...: every drawing as DXF or DWG</li><li>Remove the masses and the result</li><li>CAD template: draw the model in CAD (no Revit)</li><li>Import CAD model: the drawing becomes the SBD model</li></ol></figure><figure class=\"shot\"><img src=\"help-img/sbd-plan.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><ol><li>Plan / Elevation / Street canyon</li><li>Projection Plane X or Y</li><li>The zones, each with its P</li><li>This drawing as DXF or DWG</li><li>Close</li><li>The drawing: gaps S1, S2 ... hatched, the planes, dimensions</li><li>The working: each gap's area, depth and S</li><li>Zoom in / out, Fit</li></ol></figure><p>Checks &gt; <b>SBD</b> assesses Design Requirement (2) - the permeability <b>P</b> and the separating distances <b>S1 / S2 / S3</b> - and Design Requirement (1), the street canyon <b>U</b>, from the building <b>masses</b> of the Revit model. No Filled Regions are drawn and nothing is picked per zone: each height zone is cut from the masses.</p><ul><li><b>In Revit - what to model:</b> each building (podium, towers) as a <b>Mass</b> (Massing &amp; Site &gt; In-Place Mass, or a Mass family); the <b>site boundary</b> as a Property Line (or lines that close within 10 mm); and each <b>street as a Floor</b> whose type name has <b>Street</b> in it (e.g. <i>SBD Street</i>), drawn from street boundary to street boundary, at the street's level (its <b>type name</b> is used as the street's name). No floor levels are needed - the heights come from the masses.</li><li><b>What is read from a street slab:</b> its <b>centreline</b> (half-way between its two long sides, round any bend), its <b>far side</b> = the opposite site's boundary (for Case 1 U), and its <b>level</b>. Axis 1 (Projection Plane X) runs along the street fronting the site the longest. The zones are measured from the <b>street level</b> = the mean top level of the street slabs near the site (by area); you can choose a Level instead. A slab that is not a strip (a junction) is left out - pick its centreline and the opposite boundary as lines instead.</li><li><b>LWK &gt; Viewer tools &gt; SBD Export:</b> choose the site boundary, untick any street not fronting the site, choose the viewer project, and the masses go to the viewer, which assesses them straight away; the result shows in the Revit window too, with each street's length, width and level. The model is sent at once and the viewer assesses it in the background (a progress bar waits for the result, up to 5 minutes); Checks &gt; SBD shows <i>Assessing ...</i> until it is ready. A street slab that is not a strip is reported once, and you can pick its centreline and opposite boundary straight away.</li><li><b>The zones:</b> <b>Low (0-20 m), Middle (20-60 m), High (60 m +)</b>. Each zone's buildings are the masses' outlines at the heights inside it, so the Middle zone of a podium + tower scheme is the towers - not the podium. A zone with no building in it is not assessed. Masses outside the site boundary (neighbours) are shown hatched and not counted.</li><li><b>The table:</b> P on Plane X and Plane Y for each zone ((IS + PE) / (W x H) on the zone's elevation, with each plane's angle under it), the gaps that count, the <b>controlling P</b> (the lowest) against the <b>required P</b> of Table 1 (from the site area and Lp), and PASS / FAIL. Lp is the length of all the buildings projected on Axis 1; where the SBD panel's Lp (the shorter side of one building) would give another required P, both are shown. <b>Case 1:</b> for each street, U = canyon area / length along the centreline (from the facade within 30 m of the centreline to the opposite boundary), Lp and 5U.</li><li><b>Run</b> assesses again (the projection planes are found automatically - see below). <b>Save</b> keeps a result for everyone; the list shows saved results (open one to compare, ✕ deletes it).</li><li><b>Plan ...</b> opens a plan of each zone, for Axis 1 or 2: the site, the zone's buildings, each gap as a strip across the site - <b>green</b> when it counts, <b>red</b> when it does not (too narrow, or blocked) - with its type and width, the S2 pinch points, the <b>air corridors</b> of 15 m or more (dashed blue) and the axis.</li><li><b>3D</b> draws the masses and the site at ground, 20 m and 60 m over the model (for a model published with LWK Publish). <b>Make issue</b> raises an issue with the result and what does not count; <b>Report</b> makes a report with the table and a plan of each zone and axis, to print or <b>Save to Folders (PDF)</b> (00 BIM &gt; Exports &gt; SBD).</li><li>The engine is the SBD panel's own (Check &amp; Comply &gt; Shared.scripts, 27/08), run on each zone's footprints: <b>S1</b> is each side region's average width, <b>Area / Depth</b> (its edge follows the outer building corners, up to 15°) - the Plan lists the working, e.g. <i>S1 (left side) = A / D = 706.9 m² / 70.83 m = 9.98 m</i>; <b>S2</b> corridors may turn up to 15° and return; <b>S3</b> = A / D for an angled boundary. <b>Plane Y</b> takes the best angle within <b>75-105°</b> of Plane X in every zone; in the <b>Middle and High</b> zones <b>Plane X</b> also turns to the angle giving the most P (15° steps, then to the degree, the best few confirmed with the full rules); the Low zone keeps Plane X along the street. The table shows each zone's angles under its P.</li><li><b>SBD masses in the 3D:</b> each SBD Export also puts the masses into the project's 3D as a model (<b>SBD masses - (model)</b> in the Models list: on / off, transparency, move like a consultant model; placed on the exporting model's internal origin). <b>Remove ...</b> in Checks &gt; SBD takes away the masses, the latest result and that model (saved results stay).</li><li><b>Heights:</b> the zones are measured from Level 0 (the lowest abutting street, or the masses' base when there is no street). If the lowest mass does not start there, Checks &gt; SBD says so (a 10 m podium would otherwise count in the Middle zone).</li><li><b>Elevations (Plan ... &gt; Elevation):</b> each zone's elevational projection on its own Plane X and Plane Y (Fig B10 / B11), drawn from the masses: the buildings, the <b>IS</b> (dotted green: the gaps that count on plan, at least 2/3 of the zone's height, and open to above over a lower building - a podium roof - where the open run with the IS beside it is 7.5 m or more), the <b>PE</b> (blue grid: a void through the building at least 3 m wide and 3 m high) and the zone frame (dashed red). The working is listed as in the BD sample case: zone area W x H, IS area, P by the IS, PE area, P by the PE and P = IS + PE. PE counts up to 1/3 of the required P, and IS alone must reach 2/3 of it. The table's P is this P (the plan's IS / W is given under the working).</li><li><b>Low zone exemption:</b> the portion of the Low zone up to 1/3 H (6.67 m) is disregarded - hatched on the elevation, not counted as IS, and left out of the zone's footprints and of Lp (a 6 m podium edge does not close a setback). Table 1's Lp (whether P is required) still takes all the Low zone's buildings.</li><li><b>Case 1 per zone:</b> U = canyon area / its length along the centreline, and Lp = the facade projected on the street, for the podium in the Low zone (above 1/3 H) and the towers in the Middle and High zones; Lp must not exceed 5U (the BD sample: U = 15 m, 5U = 75 m, Lp = 80 - 7.5 x 2 = 65 m; tower U = 15 + 4 = 19 m, 5U = 95 m, Lp = 32 m). <b>Plane Y:</b> a site under 2 ha is checked on Plane X; Plane Y is shown for information (greyed). From 2 ha, Plane X needs 20 % and Plane Y 25 % (33.3 % with a building over 60 m).</li><li><b>Deformed elevation (as the SBD panel):</b> each zone's elevation on Plane X and Plane Y is laid out from the plan, along the site's edge nearest the plane (the street side): each <b>gap at its S value</b> (S1 = A / D of the side region, S2 = the corridor's width - the numbers on the plan) and each <b>building group at its width on that edge</b> (between the gaps beside it, so a corridor turned by a few degrees makes the shadow beside it wider or narrower). So <b>W = the S values + the shadows</b>, and P = (IS + PE) / (W x H). A gap that does not count (e.g. S2 below 15 m) is drawn hatched red and is not IS. Both drawings carry the same dimension chain: on the plan along the near edge (each gap's projected width, its S and the shadows), on the elevation under the strip.</li><li><b>Planes found automatically:</b> the Low zone keeps Plane X along the street (BD sample case); in the Middle and High zones the plane pairs are assessed in full and the one giving the most P (as reported, on the elevation) is used - the Plan lists the pairs tried. Plane Y takes the best angle within 75-105° of X in every zone. There is no axis to choose.</li><li><b>On the plan:</b> each corridor and side region is drawn to the site boundary (its band, clipped to the site); its label gives the turn (any angle from 0 to 15°, e.g. <i>S2 16.9 m · 7.6°</i>); the buildings are named B1, B2 ... as on the elevation.</li><li><b>Street canyon (Plan ... &gt; Street canyon):</b> Design Requirement (1) as its own check, zone by zone: each building facing a street, its canyon (from the facade within 30 m of the centreline to the opposite site boundary) hatched, U written in it, and Lp drawn along the street; beside it the working - U = canyon area / length, Lp, 5U and the result. The summary shows its own verdict (Street canyon: Lp ≤ 5U · PASS / FAIL, with the buildings that fail), and the Report and Make issue include it.</li><li><b>Design Requirement (1) - Lp of building(s) abutting a street (as GB081):</b> a building or group abuts a street when <b>any part</b> of it is within 30 m of the street's centreline. Only the part of it within 30 m of the centreline counts: its canyon runs over that part's projected length on the street, from its facade to the opposite site boundary: <b>U = Street Canyon Area / Length</b>. With two streets the smaller U controls (UB1 &lt; UB2). <b>Max Lp = 5 x U</b>, and the Actual Lp (the facade projected on the street) must not exceed it. The Street canyon view draws each canyon (STREET CANYON AREA A = ... m²), ACTUAL Lp, LENGTH and a typical width, with the calculation beside it; where no building is within 30 m it says the requirement does not apply. The report has a Design Requirement (1) page for each zone.</li><li><b>Drawings:</b> the gaps are numbered <b>S1, S2, S3 ...</b> along the plane (the same numbers on the plan, the near-edge chain, the elevation and the working); each side region shows its area <b>A1</b> and depth <b>L1</b> (S1 = A1 / L1); each turned edge has an angle symbol with its value; Axis 1 (X) and Axis 2 (Y) are drawn with the angle between them; a scale bar (0 - half - length); the street's centreline is marked <b>℄</b> with its name. The elevation dimensions every step of the buildings' profile and its height, numbers the IS areas (IS1, IS2 ...) and gives the levels also as the model's levels in brackets. Every number is given to 3 decimals.</li><li><b>Streets and Plane X (report 3):</b> a street that turns (an L-shaped street round the site's corner) is taken leg by leg: Plane X of the Low zone runs along the leg fronting the site the longest, and Design Requirement (1) assesses each leg as a street, e.g. <i>TLO Street (leg 2)</i>; two separate streets on two boundaries are each assessed, the smaller U controls. A side region's edge turns <b>once</b>: perpendicular to the plane, then at most 15° to the end. A gap that does not reach its S (S1 under 7.5 m, S2 under 15 m) but is at least 3 m wide counts as a <b>PE</b> on the elevation (PE up to 1/3 of the required P); narrower, it is not counted. A sloped face's thin steps are one IS (or PE) area, given as a triangle (½ x w x h) or a stepped area, and one sloped step in the profile dimensions. The plan shows the street's name along it, <b>℄</b> at its end and the <b>mean street level</b> (Level 0 of the assessment); the Street canyon view adds each building's <b>Lp rectangle</b> (dashed - also for buildings more than 30 m away, whose Lp is still given), the <b>30 m line</b> from the centreline and the street's width. The report's drawings are cropped to the site and printed larger.</li><li><b>Report 4 rules:</b> <b>Level 0</b> is the mean level of the lowest street abutting the site; each street shows its own mean street level on the plan. A <b>side region next to a street</b> (not a common boundary) runs on to the street's <b>centreline</b> (S = A / L grows). Both side regions are measured from <b>one projection plane</b> - the plane on one side of the site (the street's side, or the side giving the most), their edges perpendicular from it and turning once away from it. Each corridor's edges both reach the boundary. <b>IS and PE are taken horizontally:</b> at each height, a gap short of its S together with the space open to above over the lower building beside it is IS where together it is as wide as the gap's S; the rest of the gap is PE (≥ 3 m wide). <b>Design Requirement (1):</b> only the part of a building within 30 m of the centreline counts (its Lp, canyon and rectangle stop at the 30 m line); buildings <b>less than 15 m apart</b> are one group for Lp (the spacing is dimensioned); each street has its own U and the smallest controls. The drawings name <b>Projection Plane X</b> and <b>Projection Plane Y</b>, keep every label clear of the others, and put the planes' symbol and the scale bar where the drawing is empty.</li><li><b>Report 5 rules:</b> a <b>side region</b> is worked out exactly: its inner edge is perpendicular to the plane and turns once (up to 15°); it is the piece <b>nearest the plane</b>; its corners lie on the site boundary; beside a street it runs on to the centreline only along the boundary that faces the street, between lines through that frontage's two corners <b>parallel to the plane</b>. An <b>air corridor</b> keeps its width all along - where it turns, its far edge is offset square to the turned edge, not sideways. The faint projection strips are no longer drawn. <b>Design Requirement (1):</b> where a facade is set back beyond 30 m between two parts, the canyon is in parts - <i>A1(a) + A1(b)</i> - with <b>U = (A(a) + A(b)) / (L(a) + L(b))</b> and Lp the parts' projections added (Fig B7); between two buildings of a group the facade counts as continuous. A building not abutting a street has <b>Lp = the shorter side of its smallest bounding rectangle</b>, dimensioned on the drawing. The 30 m offset from each centreline is a dashed line; each street's name, level and width are placed clear of the canyons.</li><li><b>Report 6 rules:</b> a side region's inner edge always starts <b>square to the plane</b> and turns only at a building corner (never angled from the plane on), so its corners stay on the boundary. The street part is found from the <b>street slab</b> beside the boundary (not from the centreline's distance), so a street of any name, or a slab drawn a little off the boundary, still extends the region - only across the street, never along it. An <b>air corridor is one straight band</b> of the same width from end to end, at its angle (up to 15°). <b>Design Requirement (1):</b> only where the ray meets the building's real facade within 30 m does the canyon count - a facade set back beyond 30 m between two wings gives <b>two canyons A(a) + A(b)</b>, also on a street that is not quite straight.</li><li><b>Report 7 rules:</b> where a side region narrows to a point at the site boundary (its edge meeting the boundary), that last piece is part of it - the hatch ends <b>exactly at the boundary's corner</b>, never cut square short of it. A short step (under 3 m) in the boundary facing a street, or a sliver between the boundary and the street slab, does not split the street part: one extension up to the centreline. The air corridor's ends also lie exactly on the boundary.</li><li><b>Report 8 rules:</b> where the turned edge leaves the site through its far boundary and the site carries on round a corner beyond it, the side region takes that corner too - all of the site outward of the edge's line, on to the boundary's corner. A tower whose plan bends (a Y or a U) is always drawn in the elevation (each cut is matched to its building by a point inside it), and every building block is marked <b>B1, B2 ...</b> on the elevations. <b>Lp (Design Requirement 1)</b> is the <b>longer side of the notional rectangle</b> round the building or group (buildings under 15 m apart are one group), the rectangle lying flush with the building and turned to the side that gives the <b>smaller</b> Lp (Fig B3: \"as L2 &gt; L1, Lp = L1\") - for every building, abutting a street or not (it replaces the shorter side of report 5 and the canyon parts' projections). The street canyon still gives U = (A(a) + A(b)) / (L(a) + L(b)) and Max Lp = 5U.</li><li><b>TMTL496 rules (L-shaped streets, ramps, junctions):</b> model <b>one Floor type per street</b> (its name is the street's name); an L-shaped or curved street is one type - one Floor or several, it need not be cut, the viewer takes it leg by leg itself - and a junction belongs to the through road. Slabs of one street that overlap or leave a small gap (a ramp beside a flat part, a shape-edited ramp) are joined end to end, and Revit lists each street with the Floors and top faces it was made of. A street's end drawn as two edges no longer swings its centreline across. A side region next to a street runs on round a rounded or splayed site corner towards a junction, up to the street's centreline, and its street part ends where its inner edge meets the site boundary, cut parallel to the plane. Air corridors that overlap on plan are <b>one corridor</b>: the one that counts (15 m or more) is kept - of two that do not, the one turned least; beside it the two are one opening, apart from it the other's gap is <b>omitted</b> (crossed out, blocked, no IS). An opening at a turn (up to 15°) that the straight projection hides is shown as an <b>angled gap</b> (A1 ...); one 15 m or wider is flagged to check. Two streets with different names are two Floors (two types): the through road keeps the junction, the other street ends on its kerb line. <b>Model (JSON)</b> in Checks &gt; SBD downloads the model as sent, to send for a check. Each street has <b>one 30 m line</b> (its whole centreline offset 30 m), and every pair of separate building groups is dimensioned (15 m or more, separate).</li><li><b>TMTL496, 3rd review:</b> a side region's street part runs exactly between the two points where its inner edge meets the site boundary, cut <b>parallel to the plane</b> at both ends. Past the last building corner the edge may also turn 15° away from the plane, so the region takes in more area where no building stands in the way. Openings are found <b>level by level</b>: one clear from some height up - over a low building between towers - is an <b>air corridor (S2) from that height</b>, blocked below it on the elevation and IS above (slits under 3 m beside the low building are part of it; a wider gap there is kept as found, and the space over the low building is taken horizontally). An opening at a turn of 15 m or more is now counted as an air corridor too. Each corridor is measured at its <b>widest</b> band through the same opening, turned up to 15°; one that reaches 15 m that way counts. Hover a building's name on the plan for its top above Level 0 - a building that shows at a plan level above its top means Level 0 is lower than you expect (it is the lowest street abutting the site).</li><li><b>While a check runs:</b> each SBD check runs in its own process on the server, at lower priority, so the viewer and publishing from Revit carry on meanwhile. A big model can take some minutes - the panel says it is running. A check that takes over 20 minutes is stopped with a message: send the model (Model (JSON)) for a look.</li><li><b>Run</b> starts the check on the server and the panel says it is running; the result shows by itself when it is ready (a big model with many tower steps takes under a minute, since 2026-12-09). You can leave the panel and come back - the rest of the viewer works meanwhile. Under the result, <b>took ...</b> says how long the check took and in which steps (plane search, elevations, Case 1 ...).</li><li><b>Street canyon widths</b> are measured square to the street's leg (its overall direction), over the whole frontage of the building or group, wherever its facade is within 30 m of the centreline - a small bend in the centreline where the street's Floors were joined does not turn the canyon askew.</li><li><b>On the elevation</b>, at a building's ends, the open space above a part that is all within the disregarded 1/3 H (and over a lower step beside it) is the space beside the side setback: it joins the setback's IS horizontally (with a setback that does not count on its own, when together they reach 7.5 m). Every step of the buildings' profile has its width written, a narrow one placed clear of its neighbours. The <b>3D</b> box in Checks &gt; SBD shows or hides everything of the SBD in the 3D - the outline and zone limits, and the <b>SBD masses</b> model each export adds.</li><li><b>In the panel:</b> a P or Lp that complies sits on green, one that does not on solid red, as the legend under the table says (grey: for information only); the actions (Plan, 3D, Make issue, Report, CAD, Remove, CAD template, Import CAD model) are buttons.</li><li><b>Plan level:</b> every zone has a <b>Plan level</b> menu: <i>All levels (worst)</i>, the default, takes every height in the zone; choosing a level takes that zone's plan (the gaps, side regions and corridors) from the masses cut at that height. The elevation is always the true 3D, so what blocks at other heights still blocks. The table, the plans, the elevations and the report say which level each zone used (<i>all levels</i> or <i>plan at +x</i>).</li><li><b>CAD export:</b> <b>CAD ...</b> &gt; <b>DXF</b> (or <b>DWG</b>, made on the server by the ODA File Converter) saves every plan, elevation and street canyon, a row per zone, each titled; in the Plan window <b>DXF / DWG</b> saves the drawing shown, a plan in the model's own coordinates (it lies over the site plan). One layer per kind - SBD-SITE, SBD-STREET, SBD-BLDG, SBD-IS, SBD-PE, SBD-NOT, SBD-CANYON, SBD-LP, SBD-DIM, SBD-TEXT ... - in metres.</li><li><b>Zoom:</b> in the Plan, Elevation and Street canyon views, the mouse wheel (or a pinch) zooms at the pointer, a drag pans, and <b>+</b>, <b>-</b> and <b>Fit</b> (or a double-click) are at the bottom right.</li></ul><figure class=\"shot\"><img src=\"help-img/sbd-report.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><ol><li>Print / Save as PDF</li><li>Save to Folders (PDF): into the project's folder</li><li>How many zone drawings</li><li>The result: P against the required P, Lp against 5U, site, planes, Level 0</li><li>Each zone: plan level, P on Plane X and Y, Case 1</li><li>Every zone's plans and elevations, with the working</li></ol></figure>"},{"id":"s55","ch":"Clash and headroom checks","h":"Light & Ventilation (window area check)","lv":3,"html":"<p>The <b>Light &amp; Vent</b> check in Revit works out, for each room, the lighting (room area x 1/10) and openable (x 1/16) window area required against what its windows and curtain panels give. Its result can be reviewed in the viewer <b>on the plan sheets</b> - even when the check runs in one model (the <b>Calculation Master Model</b>, with the accurate room areas) and the plan sheets are published from another (the <b>Layout Master Model</b>). The two only need to be on the <b>same shared coordinates</b>.</p><p><b>In Revit</b></p><ul><li><b>Calculation model:</b> <b>Light &amp; Vent</b> as before, then answer <b>Yes</b> to <i>Send the result to the viewer?</i> and pick the viewer project. Each room goes with its outline, its windows and its result; the diagrams PDF (when made) goes too, and is also kept in Folders &gt; 00 BIM &gt; Exports &gt; Light &amp; Ventilation.</li><li><b>Layout model:</b> publish its plan sheets <b>once with the updated add-in</b> (2026-12-10 or later). Each plan then carries where it sits in shared coordinates. Until then, a plan sheet that also has a room schedule shows the rooms matched by <b>room number and name</b> to its own rooms; the legend says which plans still need publishing.</li><li><b>Rooms</b> are always the Calculation model's own (since 2026-12-11); the windows and curtain panels can still come from its linked models. A linked model naming the same floor differently (5/F for 4/F) no longer adds its rooms.</li><li><b>The full report:</b> if this PC cannot make the diagrams PDF (it needs Python and reportlab), the diagrams are sent and the server makes the PDF; if they were not made, Light &amp; Vent offers to make them for the viewer.</li></ul><p><b>On the sheets</b></p><ul><li><b>View &gt; Light &amp; Vent</b> colours each checked room on the plans of <b>its own floor</b>: green <b>OK</b>, red <b>NOT OK</b> / <b>NO WINDOW</b>, amber <b>NEEDS DATA</b> (a window type to confirm). A room counted together with another (a kitchen with the living room: <i>WITH 131</i>) is dashed in that room's colour. The dots are its windows and panels.</li><li>The legend at the bottom left gives the counts, the model and when it was checked, and a switch: <b>Filled</b> (rooms tinted - the drawing's lines stay dark through the colour), <b>Outline</b> (only each room's outline and a dot in its result colour, the drawing fully readable) or <b>Off</b>. The choice is remembered on this device.</li><li><b>Drawing missing under the colours?</b> If the plan was published while a linked model (the towers' flats, for example) was not loaded or its workset was closed, the sheet has no drawing there: the legend and the status bar name the link. Open the Layout model with the links loaded and their worksets open, and publish the sheet again.</li><li><b>Click a room</b> (Select tool): its card shows the area, the required and provided lighting and openable area (measured glass, and width x height x 70 % beside it), each window (mark, type, size, how it opens, its share) and the notes. <b>Show in 3D</b> shows its windows in the model; <b>Make issue</b> draws a cloud round the room and opens the issue form, filled in. <b>Esc</b> clears it.</li></ul><p><b>The table and the Dashboard</b></p><ul><li><b>3D &gt; Checks &gt; Light &amp; Vent:</b> <b>Show on sheets</b> at the top opens the plan sheet showing the most of the rooms chosen (floor, tower, flat), coloured. The table has a <b>Tower</b> column; filter by floor, tower, flat and result (rooms to look at first). Click a row for its card: <b>Show in 3D</b> selects and zooms to its windows on the same page (nothing reloads); <b>Make issue (3D)</b> opens the 3D issue form there, filled in (at the room itself when its windows are not in the models shown); <b>Show on plan ...</b> opens the sheet with the room shown. When no plan shows it, the card says why (plans not published again yet, or no plan of that floor).</li><li><b>Full report</b> (3D tab, the legend on the sheets, the Dashboard): every room's schedule by floor and flat, then each room's windows - <b>Print / Save as PDF</b>, or <b>Save to Folders</b> (Light &amp; Ventilation, as a PDF). <b>Table (CSV)</b> and <b>Diagrams (PDF)</b> download the table and the diagrams.</li><li><b>Dashboard:</b> a Light &amp; Ventilation card with the counts and the date of the last check.</li><li>If the rooms land in the wrong place on the plans, the two models are not on the same shared coordinates: check with the BIM team (Manage &gt; Coordinates in Revit).</li></ul>"},{"id":"s56","ch":"Walking through the model","h":"Walking through the model","lv":2,"html":"<p>Walk mode puts you at eye level inside the building, following floors, stairs and ramps.</p><p><b>Start:</b> click <b>Walk</b>, then click a floor (clicking a wall places you on the floor in front of it). Or right-click a spot and choose <b>Walk from here</b>. Walking turns off the floor plan and section box.</p><table><tr><th>Action</th><th>Keyboard / mouse</th><th>iPad / iPhone</th></tr><tr><td>Forward / back</td><td>W / S or ↑ / ↓</td><td>On-screen pad</td></tr><tr><td>Step sideways</td><td>A / D</td><td>On-screen pad</td></tr><tr><td>Turn</td><td>← / →, or drag with the mouse</td><td>Drag with a finger, or the pad</td></tr><tr><td>Look up and down</td><td>Drag with the mouse</td><td>Drag with a finger</td></tr><tr><td>Faster</td><td>Hold Shift (3× speed)</td><td>-</td></tr><tr><td>Step forward or back</td><td>Scroll wheel</td><td>-</td></tr><tr><td>Floor above / below</td><td>Page Up / Page Down</td><td>-</td></tr><tr><td>Up / down (Gravity off)</td><td>E / Q</td><td>-</td></tr><tr><td>Stop walking</td><td>Esc or <b>Stop</b></td><td><b>Stop</b></td></tr></table><p><b>Walking panel settings</b> (remembered):</p><ul><li><b>Eye</b> height, 0.8 to 3 m (default 1.6 m).</li><li><b>Speed</b>, 0.5 to 8 m/s (default 1.5 m/s).</li><li><b>Gravity</b> (on): stay on the floor, climb stairs and ramps, ignore desk-height steps.</li><li><b>Walls block</b> (off): stops you walking through walls. Doors are closed in the model, so doorways block too when this is on.</li></ul><p>On the Sheets page, <b>2D + 3D</b> with <b>Walk</b> lets you walk in 3D while the plan beside it shows where you are.</p>"},{"id":"s57","ch":"Consultant models (IFC)","h":"Consultant models (IFC)","lv":2,"html":"<p>Models from other companies (structure, MEP, interior, facade) can be shown with the project's own. Ask them for <b>IFC</b> (IFC 2x3 or IFC4): SketchUp, Revit, Tekla, ArchiCAD and Rhino all export it, and it keeps the elements, their properties and their real coordinates. (\"WebGL\" is how a browser draws; it is not a file to exchange.)</p><table><tr><th>Use</th><th>How</th></tr><tr><td>Add to this project's 3D</td><td><b>Models</b> panel &gt; <b>+ Consultant model (IFC)</b>: choose the .ifc, give its name, company and discipline, <b>Upload and convert</b>. The server converts it (a bar shows the progress); it then appears under <b>Consultant models</b></td></tr><tr><td>Overlay another project's model</td><td><b>+ Overlay another project</b>: pick a project you can open and one of its models. It is shown here on the shared coordinates both use</td></tr><tr><td>A 3D page of its own</td><td>An admin makes it with <b>New 3D project from IFC</b> (Admin). For a model whose coordinates match nothing: a standalone reference, which can still be overlaid later</td></tr></table><ul><li>Each consultant model has a tick box (on / off for you) and a slider to make it see-through.</li><li><b>One colour, to compare:</b> the small circle beside a consultant model (and beside each model in the <b>Models</b> list) shows the whole model in one colour - red, orange, yellow, green, cyan, blue, purple, grey or any colour - for example the project grey and the structure red. <b>↺ Original colour</b> (in the colours, or the <b>↺</b> beside a coloured model) puts it back; <b>↺ Reset colours</b> at the top of the Models panel puts every model back. It is remembered on this device, works with the see-through slider, and stays in <b>White</b> mode.</li><li>A model set <b>in the middle</b> (no coordinates) keeps that spot for everyone, phones included - phones load fewer linked models, so it is no longer worked out again on each device.</li><li><b>Place</b> (the person who added it, or a project admin) sets where it sits for everyone: <b>Shared coordinates</b> (what a coordinated consultant exports), <b>This model's origin</b>, or <b>No coordinates: set in the middle</b>; then <b>East / North / Up</b> (mm) and <b>Turn</b> (°) move it by hand while you watch. <b>Save for everyone</b> keeps it; <b>Cancel</b> puts it back.</li><li>Its elements can be clicked and issues raised on them like the project's own.</li><li><b>×</b> removes it from the project (who added it, or a project admin).</li></ul>"},{"id":"s58","ch":"Issues and BCF","h":"Issues and BCF","lv":2,"html":"<p>An issue is a markup or a 3D point with a title, type, owner, due date and a conversation; it is numbered by the server (#N) and the same issue appears on Sheets, in 3D, on the Dashboard and in Revit.</p>"},{"id":"s59","ch":"Issues and BCF","h":"Raising an issue","lv":3,"html":"<figure class=\"shot\"><img src=\"help-img/issue-new.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><ol><li>Template: fill the issue from a saved one</li><li>Save as template: keep this one for the project</li><li>Title</li><li>Description</li><li>Type: General, Design, Coordination, Clash ...</li><li>Assign to: a name or e-mail</li><li>Due date</li><li>Status</li><li>Priority</li><li>Where it is: the sheet, the view and the point in the model</li><li>Save issue (Cancel drops it)</li></ol></figure><table><tr><th>Where</th><th>How</th></tr><tr><td>On a sheet</td><td>Switch the drawing's toolbar to <b>+ Issue</b> and draw a markup; or select a markup and press <b>Issue</b>; or right-click it and choose <b>Raise issue</b>. A sharp picture of the drawing is attached automatically: it is drawn from the PDF itself at about 200 dpi, whatever the zoom or the speed settings of your computer.</td></tr><tr><td>In 3D</td><td>Click <b>Add issue</b>, then click the spot (on iPad: long press). The camera, section and hidden elements are saved with it, and a snapshot is attached. <b>Mark up snapshot</b> lets you draw on the picture (clouds, arrows, text and more).</td></tr></table><p>Fill in the issue window, then <b>Save issue</b>:</p><table><tr><th>Field</th><th>Notes</th></tr><tr><td><b>Title</b></td><td>Required, up to 120 characters. Say what is wrong and where, for example \"L12 corridor: fire door swing clashes with riser\"</td></tr><tr><td><b>Type</b></td><td>General, Design, Coordination, Clash, Fire safety, Statutory / BD, Structure, MEP, Facade, Drawing error, Query / RFI</td></tr><tr><td><b>Description</b></td><td>What is wrong, what you expect, any reference</td></tr><tr><td><b>Assign to</b></td><td>Pick a project member (or type a name)</td></tr><tr><td><b>Due</b></td><td>The date an answer is needed</td></tr><tr><td><b>Status</b></td><td>Open, In progress, Resolved, Closed</td></tr><tr><td><b>Priority</b></td><td>Low, Normal (default), High, Critical</td></tr><tr><td><b>Template</b></td><td>Load a saved set of fields; <b>Save as template</b> shares the current one with the project</td></tr></table><figure class=\"shot\"><img src=\"help-img/issue-3d.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><ol><li>Template; Save as template</li><li>Title (filled in from the check)</li><li>Type</li><li>Description (filled in from the check)</li><li>Assign to; due date</li><li>Status and priority</li><li>Where it is in the model</li><li>The snapshot of the view</li><li>Mark up the snapshot: cloud, arrow, text ...</li><li>Save issue</li></ol></figure>"},{"id":"s60","ch":"Issues and BCF","h":"Working an issue","lv":3,"html":"<ul><li>Click an issue in the list (or its pin in 3D) to open it. In 3D the view goes back to exactly what the author saw: the same eye and direction, the section box with its turn (or the section plane), hidden elements, parallel or perspective view and the floor plan. <b>Show in view</b> and links to the issue do the same.</li><li><b>In Revit</b> (LWK Issues &gt; <b>Go to</b>): an issue seen through the viewer's normal camera, or raised while walking, opens in a perspective camera view <b>LWK Issue - &lt;you&gt; (camera)</b> from the same eye, with the same section box, not a view of the whole building from outside.</li><li>In the issue window: edit the title and fields, <b>Add photo</b> (site photos, several at once), and write in <b>Discussion</b> then press <b>Post</b>. Type <b>@</b> to mention a project member.</li><li><b>Photos in the discussion</b> (Sheets and 3D alike): <b>📷 Photo</b> beside Post picks pictures - on a phone or iPad it can take one with the camera - or paste a screenshot (<b>Ctrl+V</b>) into the message box, or drop picture files on it. They wait under the box (✕ leaves one out) and go with the message when you <b>Post</b>; a message can be photos alone. Large photos are made smaller (1920 px) first. Click a photo in the discussion to see it large (← → for the next, <b>Esc</b> to close). The issue report shows them under the message.</li><li><b>Show in view</b> returns to the spot; <b>Show in 3D</b> opens the 3D page there.</li><li><b>Not an issue</b> closes it with a reason that everyone can read; the same button reopens it.</li><li><b>Delete</b> removes it for everyone. Members can delete only their own issues; project admins can delete any.</li><li><b>Revit element</b> (3D issues): the element it was raised on, with <b>Copy Revit IDs</b>, <b>Show in 3D</b> and <b>Show in Revit</b>.</li><li><b>Tasks:</b> the tasks that point at this issue, with their owner and due date. <b>+ New task from this issue</b> makes one (see Issues and tasks together); <b>Send to chat</b> posts the issue into a chat.</li><li>Setting the status to <b>Resolved</b> or <b>Closed</b> and pressing <b>Save</b>: if tasks on the issue are still open, the viewer offers to mark them done.</li></ul>"},{"id":"s61","ch":"Issues and BCF","h":"Status: who does what (team practice)","lv":3,"html":"<table><tr><th>Status</th><th>Set by</th><th>Meaning</th></tr><tr><td>Open</td><td>Author</td><td>Raised, waiting for the assignee</td></tr><tr><td>In progress</td><td>Assignee</td><td>Being worked on</td></tr><tr><td>Resolved</td><td>Assignee</td><td>Fixed or answered; waiting for the author to check</td></tr><tr><td>Closed</td><td>Author or project admin</td><td>Checked and done</td></tr></table>"},{"id":"s62","ch":"Issues and BCF","h":"Finding issues","lv":3,"html":"<ul><li><b>Sheets:</b> the right panel lists <b>All / Issues / Comments</b>, grouped by Sheet, Status, Assigned to, Raised by, View, Issue type or Markup type, with a <b>Search</b> box. Right-click an entry to open it, show it on the sheet or in 3D, or change its status.</li><li><b>3D:</b> <b>Issues in 3D</b> groups by Status, Floor, Issue type, Assigned to, Raised by or Model. <b>Sheet issues</b> also shows issues raised on sheets as diamonds in the model. <b>Hide issues</b> (at the top of the panel; on Sheets, <b>👁 Markups</b>) hides the pins, and <b>Hide closed</b> hides resolved and closed ones (nothing is deleted) - on a sheet, with every markup grouped with that issue.</li><li><b>Dashboard:</b> filters, overdue lists and the responsibility table (see Dashboard and projects).</li></ul>"},{"id":"s63","ch":"Issues and BCF","h":"BCF: issues with Revit, Navisworks and others","lv":3,"html":"<ul><li><b>Export BCF</b> (3D page) and <b>BCF</b> (Sheets page) download a BCF 2.1 file with each issue's title, status, priority, dates, author, assignee, description, camera, selected element and snapshot. Plain comments without an issue are left out, as are the issue type, the comment thread and added photos.</li><li>The selected element is written with its IFC GUID <b>and its Revit ElementId</b> (AuthoringToolId), so Revit BCF tools such as Autodesk BCF Manager, BCFier and Revizto select it in Revit.</li><li><b>Import BCF</b> (3D page only) reads BCF 2.0, 2.1 and 3.0 from Revit, Navisworks, Solibri or ACC. It first asks which coordinates the file uses: choose <b>Work it out (recommended)</b> unless you know. Issues already imported (same ID) are skipped.</li></ul>"},{"id":"s64","ch":"Issues and tasks together","h":"Issues and tasks together","lv":2,"html":"<p>An issue says what is wrong; a task says who fixes it by when. The two are linked and each offers to close the other.</p><ul><li><b>A task from an issue:</b> in the issue window press <b>+ New task from this issue</b>. The task list and group of this project come first, the owner is the issue's <b>Assigned to</b>, and the due date is the issue's. The issue, its files and its Revit element go on the task. Tick <b>Open the task when made</b> to go to it.</li><li><b>Task done → issue:</b> when you <b>Mark complete</b> a task whose linked issues are still open, Tasks asks <b>Resolve its issues too?</b> Tick the ones to change and choose Resolved or Closed. They are changed as if you did it in the viewer: history, emails, the chat card, and a comment naming the task.</li><li><b>Issue resolved → task:</b> set an issue to Resolved or Closed and <b>Save</b>; if its tasks are still open, the viewer offers to mark them done. The tasks also get a line in their activity.</li><li>The task window shows each linked issue's status now; the task list shows <b>#n open</b> or <b>#✓</b>.</li></ul>"},{"id":"s65","ch":"Revit elements","h":"Revit elements","lv":2,"html":"<p>A 3D issue keeps the Revit element it was raised on: <b>ElementId</b>, <b>UniqueId</b>, IFC GUID, category, family / type and level. Models published by the LWK add-in know all of these; older ones only the IFC GUID.</p><table><tr><th>To</th><th>Do this</th></tr><tr><td>Select it in Revit now</td><td><b>Copy Revit ID</b> (or <b>Copy Revit IDs</b>), then in Revit <b>Manage &gt; Select by ID</b> and paste. Works today, no add-in change needed</td></tr><tr><td>See it in 3D</td><td><b>Show in 3D</b>: the 3D page picks the element(s) out and zooms to them</td></tr><tr><td>Have Revit select it</td><td><b>Show in Revit</b> asks the LWK add-in to select it in Revit. Until the add-in supports this, the ids are copied for Select by ID instead</td></tr><tr><td>Hand it to a colleague</td><td>Select elements on the 3D page and press <b>+ Task</b>: they go on the task as <b>Elements to change</b>, with the same buttons</td></tr><tr><td>Send it to another tool</td><td><b>Export BCF</b>: Revit BCF tools select the element from its ElementId</td></tr></table>"},{"id":"s66","ch":"Search","h":"Search","lv":2,"html":"<p>One box for everything: press <b>Ctrl+K</b> or <b>/</b> on any page, or click the magnifier at the top.</p><ul><li>It finds <b>projects</b>, <b>tasks</b> (title, description, T-12), <b>issues</b> (#12, title, description, sheet, assignee, Revit element and id), <b>sheets</b>, saved <b>3D views</b>, <b>messages</b>, and <b>files and links</b> on tasks and issues.</li><li>Type one or more words; every word must match. Results are grouped by kind; ↑ ↓ and <b>Enter</b> open one, <b>Esc</b> closes.</li><li>You only see what you may open. Your last searches are listed when the box is empty.</li></ul>"},{"id":"s67","ch":"Working offline","h":"Working offline","lv":2,"html":"<p>On site with no signal, a project downloaded to the device keeps working: sheets, the 3D model, issues and markups.</p><ol><li>With a connection, open the project and choose <b>Work offline ...</b> in your profile menu (top right), then <b>Download for offline</b>. The download shows its progress and can be continued if it stops.</li><li>Without a connection the header says <b>Offline - copy of &lt;date&gt;</b>. Look at sheets and the model, raise and answer issues, draw markups.</li><li>Changes made offline wait on the device (<b>N changes waiting</b>) and upload by themselves when the connection is back (<b>All changes uploaded</b>).</li></ol><ul><li>The Dashboard, Admin, Board, Tasks, Messenger, comparing with earlier versions and adding PDFs need a connection.</li><li>On iPad and iPhone, <b>Add to Home Screen</b> first: Safari may clear a website it has not seen for some weeks, but keeps the Home Screen app.</li></ul>"},{"id":"s68","ch":"Phones and tablets","h":"Phones and tablets","lv":2,"html":"<p>The same address works on iPad and iPhone in Safari; the viewer detects the device and loads a lighter 3D model so it fits in the device's memory.</p><p><b>What is different on a phone or tablet</b></p><ul><li>The side panels become drawers: <b>☰ Models</b> / <b>☰ Sheets</b> on the left and <b>ⓘ Details</b> / <b>Issues</b> on the right. Tap outside a drawer to close it. A dot on Details means something was picked.</li><li>3D loads a phone copy of each model, made on the server after every publish. On big projects, geometry is fetched in pieces as you look around (\"streaming\"), coarse first, then finer.</li><li><b>Light mode</b> is on: repeated typical floors load only near where you are looking.</li><li>Small items such as furniture are drawn only near the camera, and far parts use simpler shapes.</li><li>Cut solids show the orange hatch but no brown outline.</li><li>The pages in the header scroll sideways: swipe them to reach Board, Tasks, Chat, Calendar and Folders. On Sheets the mark-up tools are along the bottom of the screen, and the sheet and issue lists come up from the bottom.</li><li><b>Search</b> fills the screen. In <b>Messenger</b>, tap a message to show its buttons; Enter makes a new line and the round button sends.</li></ul><p><b>Gestures</b></p><table><tr><th>Gesture</th><th>3D</th><th>Sheets</th></tr><tr><td>One finger</td><td>Orbit</td><td>Draw with the current tool (pans after you have used an Apple Pencil)</td></tr><tr><td>Two fingers</td><td>Pinch to zoom, drag to pan</td><td>Pinch to zoom, drag to pan</td></tr><tr><td>Double tap</td><td>Focus on that surface</td><td>-</td></tr><tr><td>Long press</td><td>New issue at that point</td><td>Right-click menu</td></tr><tr><td>Two-finger / three-finger tap</td><td>-</td><td>Undo / redo</td></tr></table><p><b>Tips</b></p><ul><li>Use landscape on iPad for the most drawing space.</li><li>If a model was published minutes ago, its phone copy may still be being prepared; the page offers to prepare it and you can try again a few minutes later.</li><li>If Safari reloads the page by itself, the device ran out of memory: untick models you do not need in <b>Models</b>, stay on one floor, and send a report (see Troubleshooting).</li></ul>"},{"id":"s69","ch":"Performance panel and settings","h":"Performance panel and settings","lv":2,"html":"<p>The <b>Performance</b> link at the bottom right of the 3D page opens load times, frame rate and memory, plus a few settings; <b>Copy</b> puts the whole report on the clipboard to paste into an email or Teams message when you report a problem.</p><table><tr><th>Setting</th><th>Choices</th><th>What it does</th></tr><tr><td><b>Streaming</b></td><td>automatic / on / off</td><td>Fetch big models in pieces as the view needs them (automatic = on for phones and tablets)</td></tr><tr><td><b>Memory budget</b></td><td>automatic / 150 to 1500 MB</td><td>How much geometry the device keeps before letting go of what is out of sight</td></tr><tr><td><b>Drawing with</b></td><td>WebGL (standard) / WebGPU (trial)</td><td>The graphics method; the page reloads to switch. Keep WebGL unless asked to test</td></tr><tr><td><b>While moving</b></td><td>follow the frame rate / always full quality</td><td>When the frame rate drops while you move, draw a lighter moving picture; the still view is always full quality</td></tr></table><p>Streaming and memory budget apply after reloading the page. The status bar also shows the live frame rate, triangles drawn and graphics memory; \"moving step 1 to 4\" means the lighter moving picture is in use.</p><p><b>Loading speed</b></p><ul><li>The viewer's files are sent compressed (the 3D library drops from 4.8 MB to 0.7 MB) and are kept by your browser: from the second visit on, a page opens from your own computer and only its data comes from the server.</li><li>Each page asks for all its data at once while it loads. The Messenger and the Projects page also show what they showed last time straight away, then update.</li><li>After an update of the viewer, changed files are fetched again by themselves; you never get a mix of old and new.</li></ul>"},{"id":"s70","ch":"For BIM coordinators: publishing from Revit","h":"For BIM coordinators: publishing from Revit","lv":2,"html":"<p>One button, <b>Publish to Viewer</b>, exports the sheets and the 3D model and uploads them; the other buttons are for doing the same steps by hand or overnight.</p>"},{"id":"s71","ch":"For BIM coordinators: publishing from Revit","h":"Setup (once per computer)","lv":3,"html":"<ul><li>Install the LWK pyRevit extension. It adds an <b>LWK</b> tab with the <b>Viewer &amp; Issues</b> panel: <b>Publish to Viewer</b>, <b>LWK Issues</b> and the <b>Viewer tools</b> pulldown.</li><li>Sign in once (in <b>LWK Issues</b> or from <b>Publish</b>). The sign-in is kept for a year so nightly uploads keep working.</li><li>To upload to an existing project you must be its <b>project admin</b>; a new project name needs a <b>site admin</b>.</li></ul>"},{"id":"s72","ch":"For BIM coordinators: publishing from Revit","h":"Publish to Viewer","lv":3,"html":"<ol><li>Open the model in Revit and click <b>Publish to Viewer</b>.</li><li><b>Where:</b> pick the <b>Viewer project</b> (or type a new name: letters, digits, - and _), check the <b>Server</b> shows \"signed in\", and the <b>Export folder</b>.</li><li><b>What:</b> tick <b>3D model (fast format, with its linked models)</b> and choose the detail: <b>Coarse (lightest)</b>, <b>Medium (recommended)</b> or <b>Fine (most detail)</b>. Tick <b>Sheets</b> and choose <b>All sheets</b>, <b>A Revit sheet set</b>, or <b>These sheets</b>. <b>Keep sheets published before</b> keeps earlier sheets that are not in this choice.</li><li><b>Then:</b> <b>Send to the viewer server (only what changed)</b>, <b>Open it in the browser when done</b>, and optionally <b>Publish this model again every night at</b> 01:00 (Mon-Fri only if you like; ACC models only).</li><li>Press <b>Publish</b>. Choices are remembered for this model. The Revit model is not changed or saved.</li></ol><p>After the upload the server needs a few minutes to prepare phone copies and read the sheet text. The server keeps the last 12 versions of each sheet PDF (for <b>Compare</b>) and the last 2 of each 3D model (for <b>Compare with previous export</b>).</p>"},{"id":"s73","ch":"For BIM coordinators: publishing from Revit","h":"Viewer tools pulldown","lv":3,"html":"<table><tr><th>Button</th><th>Use it to</th></tr><tr><td><b>Fast 3D Export</b></td><td>Export only the 3D model (and links) in the fast format; sheets are kept</td></tr><tr><td><b>Export Viewer</b></td><td>Export sheets and the manifest by hand (older IFC route)</td></tr><tr><td><b>Upload Now</b></td><td>Send the last export to the server again</td></tr><tr><td><b>Add Model</b></td><td>Register an ACC model for the automatic export: sheets, IFC schema, categories to leave out, typical-floor groups</td></tr><tr><td><b>Run Export</b></td><td>Export and upload every registered model now (Shift-click: only the open model)</td></tr><tr><td><b>Night Export</b></td><td>Schedule every night or weeknights, remove the schedule, or see status and logs</td></tr><tr><td><b>Export Link</b></td><td>Export a link that the automatic export cannot open (for example an older-version cloud model)</td></tr><tr><td><b>Link Places</b></td><td>Write every link instance's placement to the export folder</td></tr><tr><td><b>Test Links</b></td><td>Quick check of links placed more than once</td></tr></table><p><b>Nightly export needs:</b> the PC left on and logged in (a locked screen is fine), Revit closed at the scheduled time, and Revit signed in to Autodesk. Allow about 15 minutes per model. Logs are in %APPDATA%\\LWK\\nightly.</p><ul><li>Every workset of the model is opened by name and unloaded links are loaded. If a workset is still closed, or the 3D model comes out empty, the viewer <b>keeps the last good 3D model</b> (the sheets still go), and the log ends with <b>result FAILED</b> and the reason.</li><li>Known dialogs are answered so the night is not stopped: a DWG with an empty paper space (Yes), a DWG with <b>extents greater than 1E9</b> (OK: it is imported without the far part), DWG import notes such as <b>Elements Lost on Import</b> (Close), <b>External Tools - Add-in Assembly Not Found</b> and any other add-in's <b>cannot find xxx.dll</b> message (Close), and any message that has only one button. Dialogs that come before the LWK tools load, or while a model opens, are answered by the launcher's watcher, which finds every window of that Revit. Every dialog is written to nightly\\dialogs.log. The launcher and its watcher are renewed by themselves the next time Revit is opened by hand after an update. Best: repair or remove the broken add-in on that PC.</li><li><b>Revit 2023-2026 (watcher 2026-11-31):</b> the launcher's watcher also sees the newer WPF windows, and presses by the button's label: <b>Load Once</b> for an unsigned add-in, <b>Ignore and continue opening the project</b> for missing links, <b>Continue working with the file</b> for missing third-party updaters, and Close on What's New and similar notices. It never presses <b>Cancel</b>, <b>Do Not Load</b> or <b>Always Load</b> - a progress window with only Cancel is left alone, so a model still opening is not stopped. A dialog it does not know is written to nightly\\dialogs.log with its picture in nightly\\dialogs\\ - send both, so a rule can be added. After this update, open <b>Auto-export</b> on each PC and <b>save the schedule once</b>: that writes the new launcher and watcher.</li><li><b>Only changed files are sent (update 2026-12-08):</b> an unchanged 3D model gives the same file as the night before, and a sheet PDF whose drawing did not change (Revit stamps a new date into it each time) is recognised as the same - neither is uploaded again. The log says e.g. \"upload: sending 6 of 108 file(s), 12.4 MB - the rest unchanged (40 sheet PDF(s) exported again with only their dates changed)\". Update the add-in (LWK.extension) on the PC; the first night after the update still sends everything once.</li><li><b>Only what changed is published at night:</b> after opening a model, the night run reads the version of the model and of every linked model (Revit numbers each save). If none has been saved since the last publish, and the job's settings are the same, nothing is exported and the night log says <b>UNCHANGED</b>. A test run, Run Export by hand, a changed setting or an update of these tools always publishes. The model still has to be opened to read its version.</li><li><b>Time:</b> each Revit version may run for 3 hours (limit_hours in nightly_schedule.json); the versions run one after another (2023, then 2024, then 2025), and a version whose Revit is open on that PC is skipped that night. Start the night run early (e.g. 01:00), so every version finishes before people open Revit in the morning.</li></ul>"},{"id":"s74","ch":"For BIM coordinators: publishing from Revit","h":"LWK Issues window in Revit","lv":3,"html":"<ul><li>Lists the viewer's issues for a project: <b>Show</b> open and in progress, assigned to me, or all; search; columns #, Title, Type, Status, Priority, Assigned to, Due, Where.</li><li><b>Go to issue</b> (or double-click) opens a personal 3D view \"LWK Issue - your name\" with a section box round the issue, or zooms the sheet. <b>Open its plan view</b> and <b>Open in web viewer</b> are beside it.</li><li><b>Place pins for the list</b> / <b>Remove pins</b> add \"LWK #n\" markers on the workset \"LWK Issues\". <b>Clouds on sheets</b> adds revision clouds under the revision \"LWK Viewer issues\".</li><li>Choose a status and/or type a comment, then <b>Send to viewer</b>: it appears in the web viewer under your name.</li></ul>"},{"id":"s75","ch":"For BIM coordinators: publishing from Revit","h":"Revit elements and the LWK add-in","lv":3,"html":"<ul><li>Every issue raised in 3D on a published model carries the element's ElementId and UniqueId. Reviewers can copy the ids for <b>Manage &gt; Select by ID</b>, and BCF exports carry them as AuthoringToolId.</li><li><b>Show in Revit</b> in the viewer leaves a request on the server for the add-in to pick up; the add-in can also send what is selected in Revit to the viewer. What the add-in needs to do is written in <b>server/REVIT_ADDIN_API.md</b>, for whoever maintains it.</li></ul>"},{"id":"s76","ch":"For admins","h":"For admins","lv":2,"html":"<p>Project admins manage their project's people and settings on the <b>Admin</b> page; site admins also manage accounts, every project, the bin and device reports.</p>"},{"id":"s77","ch":"For admins","h":"Roles","lv":3,"html":"<table><tr><th>Role</th><th>Can</th></tr><tr><td><b>Viewer</b></td><td>Look at everything; cannot add or change issues or comments</td></tr><tr><td><b>Member</b></td><td>Raise and edit issues and comments; delete only their own</td></tr><tr><td><b>Publisher</b></td><td>Everything a member can, plus publish the sheets and the 3D model from Revit (LWK tab &gt; <b>Publish to Viewer</b>)</td></tr><tr><td><b>Project admin</b></td><td>Everything a publisher can, plus manage the project's members, edit or delete anything, override layer locks, upload models</td></tr><tr><td><b>Site admin</b></td><td>Every project; add, deactivate and reset accounts; create, delete and restore projects</td></tr></table><p>Every project must keep at least one project admin.</p>"},{"id":"s78","ch":"For admins","h":"Projects and members","lv":3,"html":"<ul><li><b>Add people to this project:</b> search, narrow by <b>team</b>, <b>office</b> or <b>company</b>, tick several (or <b>Select all shown</b>), choose the Role and press <b>Add N people</b>; or fill in <b>Someone without an account yet</b> (Email, Name, Office, Company, Role) and <b>Create and add</b>. A temporary password is shown <b>once</b>.</li><li>Send it with <b>Email invitation</b> (opens your own Outlook) or <b>Copy invitation</b>. The person must choose their own password at first sign-in.</li><li>Change a role in the members table, or <b>Remove</b> someone (their issues and comments stay).</li><li><b>Teams channel:</b> paste the Teams Workflow webhook address, <b>Save</b>, <b>Send a test</b>, and choose the day and hour (Hong Kong time) for the weekly summary.</li><li><b>Markup layers:</b> for each layer set who can change it (every member, project admins only, or named people), who can see it, and whether it starts hidden.</li><li><b>Phones and tablets:</b> <b>Prepare this project now</b> re-makes the phone copies if a phone reports none; <b>Show progress</b> (site admins) shows the server's background work.</li></ul>"},{"id":"s79","ch":"For admins","h":"Projects (Admin > Projects and members)","lv":3,"html":"<ul><li><b>+ New project</b>: <b>Project name</b> (e.g. HKA-P-01681-ARC - SKW; the code is taken from it), <b>Code</b>, <b>Status</b>, <b>Group / team</b>, <b>Owners</b>, and <b>Folders and files</b> (OneDrive, SharePoint or ACC links). <b>Import</b> reads a project table exported from Lark Base or Excel.</li><li><b>Models and sheets:</b> the viewer projects (export folders) that show this job. Ctrl+click several when a job has several Revit models and sheet sets, such as Site 1 and Site 2. Choosing one already used elsewhere moves it here; an entry the server made for it alone is removed, and its task groups move with it.</li><li>Members belong to each part (they are what lets someone open that model). With several parts, a <b>Part</b> selector appears above the members table.</li><li><b>Remove from Projects</b> takes a job off the Projects page; its tasks, issues, model and files stay.</li></ul>"},{"id":"s80","ch":"For admins","h":"Site admin only","lv":3,"html":"<ul><li><b>People:</b> add accounts, <b>Reset password</b>, <b>Make / Remove site admin</b>, <b>Deactivate / Reactivate</b> (signs the person out everywhere), <b>Edit</b>, <b>Delete</b> (for accounts made by mistake).</li><li><b>Delete project ...:</b> type the project name to confirm. Models, sheets, issues, markups and members move to the bin on the server; <b>Restore</b> in the bin list puts everything back, as long as the name has not been reused.</li><li><b>Devices:</b> reports sent by the 3D page from each device: what loaded, peak memory, frame rate, stalls and crashes. Filter to crashes or to phones and tablets to see where the viewer struggles.</li><li><b>Speed (site admins):</b> how fast the server answers and how long people wait, measured all the time. <b>Days</b>: answers, the typical and slowest times, and <b>stalls</b> - moments the server stopped answering everyone (as when the viewer showed Offline). Each stall says what the server was busy with: send it to have that part fixed. <b>Pages, as people waited</b>: each page's time until it was ready on people's own devices (the first sheet or the models shown), with its slowest data. <b>Server answers</b> and <b>Slow answers</b> (over 2 s) show which parts take the time. The chat's waiting-for-news requests are counted but not as slow.</li><li><b>Server:</b> email needs the server's LWK_SMTP_ settings. If a proxy in front of the server has trouble with the compressed, browser-kept files, start the server with --plain-assets (or set PLAIN_ASSETS=1 in run.bat).</li></ul>"},{"id":"s81","ch":"Troubleshooting and FAQ","h":"Troubleshooting and FAQ","lv":2,"html":"<p>Most problems are an old cached page, a slow connection or a device short of memory; the table gives the first thing to try.</p><table><tr><th>Problem</th><th>Try this</th></tr><tr><td>Something looks old or a new feature is missing</td><td>Check the version next to \"LWK Viewer\" at top left; press Ctrl+F5 (Windows) or Cmd+Shift+R (Mac). On iPad, close the tab and open it again</td></tr><tr><td>\"Wrong email or password\"</td><td>Check the email; ask an admin to <b>Reset password</b>. After 10 tries, wait 15 minutes</td></tr><tr><td>\"You are not a member of this project\"</td><td>Ask the project admin to add you</td></tr><tr><td>I cannot add or change issues</td><td>You are a <b>Viewer</b> on this project; ask the project admin for Member</td></tr><tr><td>Publish to Viewer says \"You need to be a Publisher or project admin\"</td><td>You are a <b>Member</b> (or Viewer) on that project. A project admin opens <b>Admin</b>, chooses the project and sets your role to <b>Publisher</b> in the members table</td></tr><tr><td>\"N waiting to save\"</td><td>Your connection dropped. Keep the page open; it saves when the connection returns</td></tr><tr><td>The header says <b>Offline</b> (or <b>Server busy</b>)</td><td>Point at it for the reason. <b>The server did not answer:</b> on the server PC check the server window is still open (start <b>server\\run.bat</b> again, also after each update), and <b>tunnel.bat</b> when you use the link from outside the office; on the server PC, http://127.0.0.1:8713/api/ping should answer. <b>Server busy:</b> the server is running but answered too slowly; it comes back by itself - if it happens often, an admin can look at <b>Admin &gt; Performance</b></td></tr><tr><td>The newest sheets or model are not there</td><td>The publish may still be running, or the server is preparing it; wait a few minutes and reload</td></tr><tr><td>3D is slow or jerky on a computer</td><td>Untick models you do not need, use a floor plan, check <b>While moving</b> is on \"follow the frame rate\"</td></tr><tr><td>iPad or iPhone reloads the page by itself</td><td>It ran out of memory: open fewer models, stay on one floor, keep <b>Light mode</b> on; send the Performance report</td></tr><tr><td>An element cannot be clicked in a section</td><td>Only the visible side of the cut can be picked; move the cut or use the Model browser</td></tr><tr><td>The measure snaps to the wrong thing</td><td>Zoom in closer; hold still until the label shows <b>corner</b>, <b>midpoint</b> or <b>edge</b></td></tr><tr><td>A Revit link is missing or misplaced</td><td>Check <b>Apply link transforms</b> is on; tell the BIM coordinator</td></tr><tr><td>Pages look different after switching to WebGPU</td><td>In Performance, press <b>Drawing with</b> to go back to WebGL (or add &amp;gpu=webgl to the address once)</td></tr><tr><td>A page is slow to open over a VPN or from home</td><td>The second visit is much quicker (the files stay in your browser). If first visits stay slow, ask IT to turn on HTTP/2 on the server's proxy</td></tr><tr><td>Search finds nothing</td><td>Type at least 2 letters; every word must match. You only see projects, lists and chats you are a member of</td></tr><tr><td>\"Revit's LWK add-in is not listening\"</td><td>The ids were copied instead: in Revit use <b>Manage &gt; Select by ID</b> and paste</td></tr><tr><td>WhatsApp import: \"does not look like a WhatsApp chat export\"</td><td>Use WhatsApp's <b>Export chat</b> file (.txt or .zip), not a screenshot or a forwarded message</td></tr><tr><td>A task or message link opens nothing</td><td>You may not be a member of that list, chat or project; ask its owner</td></tr><tr><td>There is no Delete for a message or a chat</td><td>Only the sender deletes a message. A group is deleted by its admins, a project channel or topic by the project's admins</td></tr></table><p><b>When you report a problem,</b> send: the project, the page (Sheets or 3D), your device and browser, what you did, a screenshot, and on the 3D page the <b>Performance → Copy</b> report.</p><p><b>FAQ</b></p><ul><li><b>Does it change the Revit model?</b> No. Publishing only reads the model. Only the LWK Issues window adds pins or clouds, and only when you ask.</li><li><b>Who can see my markups?</b> Everyone on the project, unless the markup is on a layer an admin has restricted.</li><li><b>Does it send email?</b> Yes, when the server's mail is set up: task assignments, @mentions, comments and completions on tasks you follow, and a daily list of tasks due. Teams posts as before.</li><li><b>Can I use it offline?</b> Yes, for a project downloaded to the device (see Working offline). Short drops are fine anyway: changes wait and save when the connection returns.</li><li><b>Does the Messenger replace WhatsApp?</b> It is for project work, next to the drawings and tasks. Messages can be sent to WhatsApp and brought in from it, but the two are not linked automatically.</li><li><b>Can consultants use it?</b> Yes, with their own account, usually as <b>Viewer</b> or <b>Member</b> on that project only.</li></ul>"},{"id":"s82","ch":"Shortcuts cheat sheet","h":"Shortcuts cheat sheet","lv":2,"html":"<p>Print this table or keep it beside the screen for the first week.</p><table><tr><th>Where</th><th>Key or button</th><th>Action</th></tr><tr><td>3D</td><td>Right button drag</td><td>Orbit</td></tr><tr><td>3D</td><td>Middle button drag</td><td>Pan</td></tr><tr><td>3D</td><td>Wheel</td><td>Zoom towards the pointer</td></tr><tr><td>3D</td><td>Double-click</td><td>Focus on that surface</td></tr><tr><td>3D</td><td>Right-click (no drag)</td><td>Menu, and move the orbit centre there</td></tr><tr><td>3D</td><td>Page Up / Page Down</td><td>Floor above / below</td></tr><tr><td>3D</td><td>Esc</td><td>Cancel a measurement, stop walking, close a menu</td></tr><tr><td>3D measure</td><td>Shift</td><td>Straight on or off for one point</td></tr><tr><td>3D walk</td><td>W A S D, ↑ ↓</td><td>Move and step sideways</td></tr><tr><td>3D walk</td><td>← →</td><td>Turn</td></tr><tr><td>3D walk</td><td>Shift / Q / E</td><td>Faster / down / up (Gravity off)</td></tr><tr><td>Sheets</td><td>Wheel / middle drag</td><td>Zoom / pan</td></tr><tr><td>Sheets</td><td>Page Down / Page Up</td><td>Next / previous sheet</td></tr><tr><td>Sheets</td><td>V / H</td><td>Select tool / Pan tool</td></tr><tr><td>Sheets</td><td>Enter, Esc, Backspace</td><td>Finish, end, or remove the last point of a polyline</td></tr><tr><td>Sheets</td><td>Delete</td><td>Delete the selected markup</td></tr><tr><td>Sheets</td><td>Ctrl+A</td><td>Select all markups on the sheet</td></tr><tr><td>Sheets</td><td>Ctrl+C / Ctrl+V</td><td>Copy / paste markups (also to another sheet)</td></tr><tr><td>Sheets</td><td>Ctrl+Z / Ctrl+Y</td><td>Undo / redo</td></tr><tr><td>Sheets</td><td>R / Shift+R</td><td>Rotate the selection 90° clockwise / anticlockwise</td></tr><tr><td>Sheets compare</td><td>N / Shift+N</td><td>Next / previous change</td></tr><tr><td>Every page</td><td>Ctrl+K or /</td><td>Search everything</td></tr><tr><td>Search</td><td>↑ ↓, Enter, Esc</td><td>Move, open, close</td></tr><tr><td>Tasks</td><td>K / J</td><td>Previous / next task</td></tr><tr><td>Messenger</td><td>Enter / Ctrl+Enter</td><td>New line / send</td></tr><tr><td>Messenger</td><td>@ # ! $ %</td><td>Mention a person / link a task, issue, sheet, 3D view</td></tr><tr><td>Messenger</td><td>Ctrl+Enter / Esc (editing)</td><td>Save / cancel an edited message</td></tr><tr><td>Messenger</td><td>Ctrl+B / Ctrl+I / Ctrl+Shift+X</td><td>Bold / italic / strikethrough</td></tr></table>"},{"id":"s83","ch":"Feedback and what to try first","h":"Feedback and what to try first","lv":2,"html":"<p>This is a trial: please try the tasks below and tell us what works, what is confusing and what is missing.</p><ul><li>☐ Sign in and change your password</li><li>☐ Find a sheet by searching for a room name or note</li><li>☐ Mark up a sheet with a cloud and text, then turn it into an issue</li><li>☐ Open the same area in 3D and cut a floor plan</li><li>☐ Measure a room wall to wall in plan, with <b>Straight</b> on</li><li>☐ Raise an issue in 3D, assign it to a colleague, and comment with an @mention</li><li>☐ Try <b>2D + 3D</b> and walk a corridor while watching the plan</li><li>☐ Open the viewer on an iPad or iPhone and look at one floor</li><li>☐ Make a task from your test issue, then complete it and resolve the issue from the Tasks page</li><li>☐ Send a message in your project's channel with a # task and a $ sheet link</li><li>☐ Open a topic in your project channel, pin a message, and send a poll and an event</li><li>☐ Find your test issue with Ctrl+K</li><li>☐ In 3D, click an element, press Copy Revit ID and select it in Revit with Select by ID</li><li>☐ Delete your test issues and tasks when you finish</li></ul><p>Send feedback, questions and problem reports to [name / Teams channel]. Include the Performance report for anything to do with speed or crashes.</p>"}],"yue":[{"id":"s1","ch":"LWK Viewer 係乜嘢","h":"LWK Viewer 係乜嘢","lv":2,"html":"<p>LWK Viewer 喺網頁瀏覽器入面顯示 project 嘅 Revit sheet 同 3D model，所以團隊入面任何人唔使開 Revit 都可以睇圖、度尺、畫 markup 同開 issue。電腦、iPad 同 iPhone 都用得，每個開咗嘅 issue 會即時同晒成個團隊分享，仲可以喺 Revit 入面跟返。</p><p>除咗圖則同 model，佢仲放埋團隊嘅工作：project 清單、task list（取代 Lark Tasks）、白板同 Messenger，全部都連住同一批 sheet、3D 視圖同 issue，仲有一個搜尋可以一次過搵晒所有嘢。</p><p><b>邊個會用</b></p><table><tr><th>邊個</th><th>通常用嚟</th></tr><tr><td>建築師同設計師</td><td>睇圖同 3D model，開設計同協調 issue，回覆指派俾自己嘅 issue</td></tr><tr><td>Project lead 同 director</td><td>用平板睇進度，喺 Dashboard 跟進未完成同過咗期嘅 issue</td></tr><tr><td>BIM coordinator</td><td>由 Revit publish model 同 sheet，行晚間 export，喺 Revit 入面處理 issue</td></tr><tr><td>顧問同地盤同事（Viewer 角色）</td><td>任何裝置都只係睇同讀</td></tr><tr><td>Team lead</td><td>安排團隊嘅 task list，跟進邊個幾時要做乜，喺 project channel 傾</td></tr><tr><td>Project admin 同 site admin</td><td>加人、set 角色、管理 project</td></tr></table><p><b>可以做乜</b></p><ul><li><b>Sheets (2D)：</b> 打開每張 publish 咗嘅 sheet，係清晰嘅 PDF；搜尋所有圖則上面嘅字；用 20 幾款工具畫 markup；同舊版本比較；連 markup 一齊 export PDF。</li><li><b>3D：</b> 轉、移、喺 model 同佢嘅 link 入面行；切平面圖同剖面；有 snap 咁度尺；睇元件 property；儲存視圖。</li><li><b>Issue：</b> 喺 sheet 或者 3D 開 issue，會連一張截圖；指派俾人、set 限期、用 @mention 留言，一路跟到關為止。Issue 可以透過 BCF 同 Revit、Navisworks、BIMcollab 互通。</li><li><b>2D + 3D 並排：</b> 喺 sheet 上面撳平面圖，3D 就會去返嗰度；喺 3D 行嘅時候，平面圖會顯示你喺邊。</li><li><b>Revit 連接：</b> Revit 入面嘅 LWK Issues 視窗會列出同一批 issue，可以 zoom 去嗰度，亦可以傳回覆返嚟。</li><li><b>Projects：</b> 每個 job 嘅人、圖則、model、task、issue、檔案同 chat 都喺同一版。</li><li><b>Tasks：</b> 團隊 task list，有 List、Kanban、Gantt 同 Dashboard 幾種睇法，可以由 Lark import，亦連住 issue、sheet 同 3D 視圖。</li><li><b>Board：</b> 每個 project 一塊共用白板，可以寫 note、整 mind map 同畫草圖。</li><li><b>Messenger：</b> project channel、group chat 同私訊；task 同 issue 嘅更新會自動貼入嚟；可以連去 task、issue、sheet 同 3D；仲可以同 WhatsApp 互傳訊息。</li><li><b>Issue 同 Task 打通：</b> 由 issue 直接開 task；完成其中一樣，會問你要唔要一齊關埋另一樣。</li><li><b>Revit 元件：</b> 3D issue 會記住 Revit ElementId，用嚟做 Select by ID、BCF 同 LWK add-in。</li><li><b>搜尋：</b> 一個搜尋框（Ctrl+K）搵晒 task、issue、sheet、3D 視圖、訊息同檔案連結。</li><li><b>Offline：</b> 將 project 下載落平板，喺地盤冇訊號都照用得。</li></ul>"},{"id":"s2","ch":"開始之前","h":"開始之前","lv":2,"html":"<p>你需要一個 account、一個支援嘅瀏覽器同 viewer 嘅網址；電腦唔使裝任何嘢。</p><p><b>啲圖點睇：</b>每個頁面嘅章節開頭都有一張截圖，每個 panel、按鈕同選項都有紅色編號；圖下面嘅清單講每個編號做乜。大部分截圖嚟自一個示範 project，少數嚟自真實 project，所以名同圖則會同你嘅唔一樣。喺 Help 入面，撳一下張圖就可以睇原尺寸。</p><p><b>你嘅 account</b></p><ul><li>Admin 會幫你開 account，再寄邀請俾你，入面有一個<b>臨時密碼</b>。</li><li>打開 viewer 網址，用你嘅 <b>Email</b> 同臨時密碼登入，跟住喺彈出嚟嘅 <b>My account</b> 版揀返自己嘅密碼（最少 8 個字）。</li><li>每個瀏覽器會保持登入 30 日。15 分鐘內打錯 10 次密碼，登入會停 15 分鐘。</li><li>角色係逐個 project 設定：<b>Project admin</b>、<b>Publisher</b>、<b>Member</b> 或者 <b>Viewer</b>（睇「俾 admin 嘅」）。只有 Publisher 或者 project admin 先可以由 Revit publish。Viewer 會見到一條橫額，話佢只可以睇同讀，唔改得任何嘢。</li></ul><p><b>Viewer 網址：</b>[寄出之前喺度貼上 viewer 網址]</p><p><b>瀏覽器同裝置</b></p><table><tr><th>裝置</th><th>瀏覽器</th><th>備註</th></tr><tr><td>Windows 或者 Mac</td><td>Chrome 或者 Edge（建議）、Safari、Firefox</td><td>有中鍵（滾輪）嘅滑鼠，用 3D 會容易好多</td></tr><tr><td>iPad</td><td>Safari</td><td>Apple Pencil 可以畫 markup；建議打橫用</td></tr><tr><td>iPhone</td><td>Safari</td><td>最適合睇同讀；3D 會載一個輕啲嘅 model</td></tr></table><p><b>保密</b></p><ul><li>當 viewer 係 project folder 咁對待：只可以加 project 團隊入面嘅人。</li><li>唔好分享密碼、唔好轉寄邀請 email，亦唔好喺團隊以外貼連結。</li><li>截圖同 export 出嚟嘅 PDF，跟其他 project 文件一樣嘅規矩。</li></ul>"},{"id":"s3","ch":"點樣串埋一齊","h":"點樣串埋一齊","lv":2,"html":"<p>BIM coordinator 由 Revit publish sheet 同 3D；團隊喺瀏覽器 review；issue 再返去 Revit 俾做 model 嘅人。</p><p>LWK Viewer 流程 · publish、review、喺 Revit 回覆</p><ol><li><b>Publish。</b> 喺 Revit 撳 <b>Publish to Viewer</b>，會將揀咗嘅 sheet export 做 PDF，model（連 link）export 做快速 3D 格式，然後只上載有改動嘅檔案。可以每晚自動做。</li><li><b>準備。</b> Server 會幫每個 3D model 整一個俾手機同平板用嘅輕身版本，同埋讀晒每張 sheet 上面嘅字俾人搜尋。每次上載之後要幾分鐘。</li><li><b>Review。</b> 團隊用任何瀏覽器打開 Sheets、3D 或者 Dashboard。Markup 同 issue 會自動儲存，所有人都即刻見到。</li><li><b>回覆。</b> 被指派嘅人會喺 viewer 見到個 issue，喺 Revit 嘅 <b>LWK Issues</b> 視窗都見到；嗰度可以 zoom 過去，亦可以傳回覆同狀態返嚟。</li><li><b>關閉。</b> 開 issue 嘅人或者 project admin 將 issue 改做 Resolved，再改做 Closed。Dashboard 會跟住邊啲未完成、過咗期、喺邊個手上。</li></ol><p>圍住呢個流程：實際工作喺 <b>Tasks</b> 安排（可以由 issue 開 task，task 做完會幫手關 issue），喺 <b>Messenger</b> 討論（每個 project 有一個 channel，task 同 issue 更新會出喺度），再用 <b>Search</b> 搵返。<b>Projects</b> 版就將每個 job 串埋一齊。</p>"},{"id":"s4","ch":"快速上手：頭十分鐘","h":"快速上手：頭十分鐘","lv":2,"html":"<figure class=\"shot\"><img src=\"help-img/header.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><ol><li>你而家喺邊個 project - 撳一下轉 project（每一頁都喺同一個位）</li><li>各頁：Projects、Dashboard、Sheets、3D、Board、Tasks、Chat（數字：未讀）、Calendar、Folders</li><li>搜尋全部 (Ctrl+K)</li><li>通知</li><li>Help - 呢本手冊，可以搜尋</li><li>你嘅資料：名、密碼、深色模式、登出</li></ol></figure><p>登入、打開一張 sheet、喺 3D 睇返同一個位，再開一個測試 issue。</p><ol><li><b>登入。</b> 打開 viewer 網址，輸入 email 同密碼，到時跟指示改咗個臨時密碼佢。</li><li><b>揀 project。</b> 撳左上角嘅 project（每一版都喺同一個位），喺清單揀另一個；或者喺 <b>Projects</b> 版揀。</li><li><b>打開一張 sheet。</b> 喺 <b>Sheets</b> 撳左邊清單入面嘅 sheet，或者喺 <b>Search all sheets</b> 打房名、grid 或者 note。滾輪放大縮細，㩒住中鍵拖動，撳 <b>Fit</b> 睇成張圖。</li><li><b>去 3D。</b> 撳左上角嘅 <b>3D</b>。㩒住右鍵轉，㩒住中鍵移，滾輪放大縮細。Double-click 一個面就會 zoom 埋去。</li><li><b>睇一層。</b> 喺 <b>Floor plan</b> 下拉選單揀一層：model 會喺嗰層上面 1.2 m 切開，由上面望落去。<b>Page Up / Page Down</b> 上落一層；<b>Whole building</b> 返去 3D。</li><li><b>撳一件元件</b>，右邊嘅 <b>Selection</b> panel 會顯示佢嘅 property。</li><li><b>開一個測試 issue。</b> 撳 <b>Add issue</b>，撳一個面，打個標題例如「TEST - please ignore」，然後 <b>Save issue</b>。所有人都會喺 <b>Issues in 3D</b> 見到。</li><li><b>試吓 2D + 3D。</b> 返去 Sheets，打開一張平面圖，撳 <b>2D + 3D</b>；喺平面圖上面撳，3D 就會移去嗰度。</li><li><b>由佢開一個 task。</b> 打開個測試 issue，撳 <b>+ New task from this issue</b>，睇吓 list、負責人同限期啱唔啱，再撳 <b>Make the task</b>。</li><li><b>喺 Chat 打個招呼。</b> 打開 <b>Chat</b>，揀 project 嘅 channel，打 <b>#</b> 揀你個測試 task，再撳 <b>Send</b>。</li><li><b>搜尋。</b> 按 <b>Ctrl+K</b>（或者撳頂部個放大鏡），打 issue 標題入面一個字：issue、task 同你個訊息都會搵到。</li><li><b>做完記得刪除測試 issue 同 task：</b> issue 喺佢嘅詳情視窗撳 <b>Delete</b>，task 喺佢嘅視窗撳垃圾桶掣。</li></ol>"},{"id":"s5","ch":"Dashboard 同 project","h":"Dashboard 同 project","lv":2,"html":"<figure class=\"shot\"><img src=\"help-img/dashboard.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><ol><li>篩選：幾耐內解決、類型、負責人、專業</li><li>只睇自己</li><li>更多篩選：辦公室、團隊、已撤銷嘅 issue</li><li>Export：報告、CSV、BCF、每週摘要</li><li>Project 嘅 task</li><li>未完、過期、期內解決、平均幾多日解決</li><li>今個星期：新開、解決、未完、過期</li><li>每星期新開同解決</li><li>每人同每個專業嘅未完 issue</li></ol></figure><p>Dashboard 係 project 嘅 issue 計分板：幾多個未完成、幾多個過咗期、喺邊個手上，同埋今個星期有乜改變。</p><p><b>四圍行</b></p><ul><li>每一版嘅頂部都一樣：個 logo，跟住係<b>你而家嘅 project</b>（左上角，有簡寫、名同編號 - 撳一下轉 project），再係各頁 <b>Projects</b>、<b>Dashboard</b>、<b>Sheets</b>、<b>3D</b>、<b>Board</b>、<b>Tasks</b>、<b>Chat</b>（有未讀訊息數目）、<b>Calendar</b> 同 <b>Folders</b>。右邊有：<b>Search</b>（Ctrl K）、鈴、<b>Help</b> 同<b>你嘅頭像</b>（你個名嘅簡寫，上線時有綠點）。撳頭像有 <b>Work offline ...</b>、<b>Admin</b>（只限 admin）、<b>Account</b>（密碼）、<b>Theme</b>（Light、Dark、Auto）同 <b>Sign out</b>。手機上面各頁可以左右掃。</li><li><b>Project 選單</b>會列出 Projects 版嘅 project 名，例如「SKW · HKA-P-01681-ARC」。由幾個 model 組成嘅 project，例如 MOS Site 1 同 Site 2，會喺下面列出佢嘅部分。最底嘅 <b>All projects →</b> 打開 Projects 版。</li><li><b>成個 project 一個 dashboard：</b> 由幾個 model 或者 sheet set 組成嘅 project（例如 TKO 有 CAL 同 LAY）會開一個合埋所有部分嘅 dashboard：數字同圖表會加埋計，<b>Part</b> 篩選同 <b>Open issues by part</b> 分開每部分，<b>Where</b> 會寫明係邊部分（CAL · A102 ...），<b>How this project is published</b> 每部分一個表。標題下面嘅 <b>All parts</b> / <b>CAL</b> / <b>LAY</b> 可以轉去單一部分再轉返嚟。喺 Dashboard 嘅 project 選單，撳 project 名會開晒所有部分，撳某一部分就淨係開嗰部分。</li><li><b>My dashboards－幾個 project 一齊睇：</b> <b>+ Combine projects …</b>（標題下面，或者 project 選單入面）可以整你自己嘅 dashboard：改個名，再剔 project（佢所有部分，連之後加嘅）或者單一部分。佢會幫你記住，喺任何電腦嘅 <b>My dashboards</b> 都見到；打開咗嘅時候隔籬有 <b>Edit</b> 同 <b>Delete</b>。可以印嘅 report 係逐部分嘅：先喺 Part 篩選揀一部分（試算表就全部都有，多一欄 Part）。</li><li>連線標籤只會喺有嘢要講嗰陣出現：<b>N waiting to save</b>（斷咗線；你嘅改動排緊隊，有返線就會送出）或者 <b>offline</b>。有改動等緊儲存嘅時候唔好 reload：排緊隊嘅嘢只會保留到你離開嗰版為止。</li></ul><p><b>Dashboard 顯示乜</b></p><table><tr><th>部分</th><th>話俾你知</th></tr><tr><td>篩選</td><td>一排 chip：<b>Resolved within</b>（Any time 至 Last 12 months）、<b>Type</b>、<b>Assigned to</b>、<b>Discipline</b>、<b>Only mine</b>；<b>More filters</b> 再有 <b>Office</b>、<b>Team</b> 同 <b>Show dismissed issues</b></td></tr><tr><td>今個星期</td><td>今個星期開咗、關咗、未完成同過咗期嘅 issue，同埋每個人手上未完成嘅 issue；<b>Send to Teams</b> 會貼去 project channel</td></tr><tr><td>總結數字</td><td>Issues、Open、In progress、Resolved、Closed、Overdue、7 日內到期、未指派、平均開咗幾多日、平均幾多日關</td></tr><tr><td>圖表</td><td>每星期開同關嘅數目（最近 12 個星期），按狀態、類型、優先次序、喺邊度開（sheet 或者 3D）同 office 分</td></tr><tr><td>責任表</td><td>每個負責人手上未完成、進行中、過咗期同就快到期嘅數目，最舊嘅未完成 issue 同最後活動；撳一行就會篩選</td></tr><tr><td>清單</td><td><b>Overdue</b>、<b>Due in the next 14 days</b>、<b>Recently changed</b>、<b>Going quiet</b>（14 日或以上冇郁過）</td></tr></table><ul><li><b>Export ▾</b> 會攞篩選緊嘅 issue：<b>Report</b>（有相、可以列印或者儲存做 PDF 嘅報告）、<b>Spreadsheet (CSV)</b> 俾 Excel，或者 <b>BCF</b> 俾 Revit、Navisworks 或 Solibri。</li><li>呢版每 2 分鐘自動更新；<b>Updated ... ago</b> 話你幾耐之前更新。四個主要數字係 <b>Open issues</b>、<b>Overdue</b>（最舊嗰個遲咗幾多日）、期內 <b>Resolved</b>（開咗幾多個入面）同 <b>Avg. time to resolve</b>；「Resolved」包括變咗 Resolved 或者 Closed 嘅 issue（Closed 即係開 issue 嘅人確認咗）。</li><li><b>呢個 project 嘅 task：</b> 如果呢個 project 喺 Projects 版上面，Dashboard 亦會顯示佢喺每個團隊 list 入面嘅 task：未完成、過咗期，同埋做咗幾多個 sub-task。</li><li><b>由你部機打開：</b> Dashboard 上次顯示嘅內容會留喺呢部機，即刻顯示；之後只會問 server 由上次到而家有改動嘅 issue。如果 server 冇回應，畫面會保留上次嘅版本，並會講明。</li></ul><p><b>通知</b></p><ul><li><b>Email</b>（server 設定好 email 嘅話）：有人將你設做 task 負責人、喺 task 或者 chat @mention 你、或者你 follow 緊嘅 task 有新留言或者完成咗，都會 email 你；每日仲會收到一封，列出聽日到期同已經過咗期嘅 task。</li><li><b>Teams：</b> 如果 admin 已經連接咗 project 嘅 Teams channel，issue 開咗、指派咗、改狀態或者限期、或者有新留言，都會貼去嗰度。留言入面嘅 @mention 會變成 Teams 嘅 mention。</li><li>每星期嘅總結可以貼去同一個 Teams channel（預設係星期一）。同一個星期嘅報告每星期嗰個時間都會以 PDF 存入 project 嘅 Folders <b>00 BIM &gt; Weekly dashboard</b>（有冇 Teams 都會）；<b>Dashboard &gt; Export &gt; Weekly report to Folders</b> 可以即刻存一份。</li><li><b>Messenger：</b> project 嘅 channel 會用卡片顯示新 task、指派、完成同留言，同埋新開或者改咗嘅 issue。</li></ul>"},{"id":"s6","ch":"Projects 項目","h":"Projects 項目","lv":2,"html":"<figure class=\"shot\"><img src=\"help-img/projects.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><ol><li>搜尋 project 或者人</li><li>狀態：Active、On hold、Completed、Archived</li><li>排序（或者撳欄頭）</li><li>管理 project（admin）</li><li>一個 project：撳名打開佢嘅頁</li><li>打開佢嘅 Sheets、3D、Chat、Dashboard、Folders</li></ol></figure><p><b>排序：</b> project 按狀態排 - <b>Active</b> 先，跟住 <b>On hold</b>、<b>Completed</b>、<b>Archived</b> - 同一狀態再按名排。Projects 版同所有 project 選單（Sheets、3D、Board、Dashboard、Folders、Messenger）都用呢個次序。喺 Projects 版撳欄目標題（Project、Status、Tasks、Completion、Overdue、Issues）或者用 <b>Sort</b> 可以轉其他排法；再撳一次就倒轉。會記住你嘅選擇。</p><p>每一版左上角嘅 project 選單列出每個 <b>project</b>（名 · 編號）同佢下面嘅<b>部分</b>（例如 Site 1／Site 2）。喺 Sheets，sheet 清單頂部嘅 <b>Set:</b> 揀「Revit sheets」或者上載咗嘅 PDF set。</p><p>喺 project 嘅資料欄，<b>Project information</b> 可以記低 project no.、client、地址、建築類型、地盤面積、GFA、層數、階段、開始同完成日期同簡介（<b>Edit</b>，project owner 同 admin 先改得）。撳或者拖一張相落資料欄頂部，就可以俾個 project 一張<b>相</b>，清單入面都會見到。</p><p><b>Projects</b> 版列出團隊嘅 job，每個 job 嘅人、圖則、model、task、issue、檔案同 chat 都喺同一個地方。呢版係俾人睇嘅；admin 喺 <b>Admin &gt; Projects and members</b> 設定 project（撳 <b>Manage</b> 掣會帶你去）。</p><p><b>清單</b></p><table><tr><th>欄</th><th>顯示</th></tr><tr><td>Project</td><td>簡稱同編號，例如 SKW · HKA-P-01681-ARC</td></tr><tr><td>Open</td><td><b>Sheets</b>、<b>3D</b> 同 <b>Dashboard</b> 掣。由幾個 model 組成嘅 project（MOS Site 1、Site 2），每個掣都會彈出一個細選單俾你揀邊部分</td></tr><tr><td>Tasks</td><td>進度（做咗幾多／總數）、過咗期嘅 task 同未完成嘅 task，嚟自每個有呢個 project group 嘅團隊 list</td></tr><tr><td>Issues</td><td>按狀態分色嘅 issue 條，同埋未完成／總數；過咗期嘅會用紅色。會加埋 project 所有 model</td></tr><tr><td>Folders</td><td>OneDrive、SharePoint 或者 ACC 嘅 folder</td></tr><tr><td>Chat</td><td>Messenger 入面 project 嘅 channel，同埋未讀訊息</td></tr></table><ul><li>頂部可以搜尋 project 或者人名，亦可以按狀態篩選。</li><li>撳一行睇<b>詳情</b>：按團隊分嘅成員、按狀態分嘅 issue（撳個數字會打開 Dashboard）、task 連 sub-task，同埋 <b>Models and sheets</b>：每個部分都有自己嘅 Sheets、3D 同 Dashboard 連結。</li><li><b>一個 project，幾個 model。</b> 一個 job 如果 export 做幾個 Revit model 同 sheet set，仍然係一個 project，分開幾個部分。成員係所有部分嘅人加埋，issue 數目會加埋所有部分，project 下拉選單會將佢顯示做一組。</li></ul>"},{"id":"s7","ch":"Tasks 工作","h":"Tasks 工作","lv":2,"html":"<p><b>Tasks</b> 係團隊嘅 task list，取代 Lark Tasks，同圖則、model 同 issue 連埋一齊。</p><p>之前打開過嘅 list 會即刻由呢部機顯示，然後只由 server 攞上次之後嘅改動。好長嘅 group 會先顯示頭 150 個 task；向下碌（或者撳 <b>Show more</b>）就會出下一批。搜尋同篩選一樣會睇晒所有 task。</p>"},{"id":"s8","ch":"Tasks 工作","h":"List、group 同睇法","lv":3,"html":"<figure class=\"shot\"><img src=\"help-img/tasks.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><ol><li>Owned、Subscribed、Activities：你嘅 task</li><li>快速篩選：全部、你開嘅、派俾人嘅、完成咗</li><li>Task list（+ 開新嘅）</li><li>People：每個人嘅 task</li><li>List、Kanban、Gantt、Dashboard、Activities</li><li>List 成員</li><li>+ New task（▾：匯入）</li><li>搜尋 task</li><li>Filter：狀態、負責人、優先、排序、分組</li><li>自訂欄位</li><li>撳欄頭排序 (▲ ▼)</li><li>一個 group（project）：收埋、打開佢嘅圖則同 dashboard</li><li>剔咗就完成</li><li>標題 - 撳一下打開 task</li><li>任何格都可以直接改</li></ol></figure><ul><li><b>Task list</b> 屬於一個團隊（例如 LWK-MANILA）。List 入面嘅 <b>group</b> 通常就係各個 job（SKW、Kai Tak 2A3 ...）。連咗 project 嘅 group 會有 <b>Project</b>、<b>Sheets</b> 同 <b>Dashboard</b> 掣；喺 <b>...</b> &gt; <b>Groups and projects</b> 連接。</li><li>左邊嘅<b>快速存取</b>：<b>Owned</b>（自己未完成嘅 task）、<b>Subscribed</b>、<b>All</b>、<b>Created</b>、<b>Assigned</b>（你派俾人嘅）同 <b>Completed</b>，跨晒所有你睇得到嘅 list。<b>People</b> 按團隊、office 或者公司顯示成個機構，同每個人未完成同過咗期嘅 task。</li><li><b>List：</b> 分組嘅表。直接喺度改；撳 ▸ 打開 sub-task；拖住一行可以排次序或者搬去另一個 group。有連住 issue 嘅 task 會顯示 <b>#2 open</b>，全部 issue 解決咗就變 <b>#✓</b>。</li><li><b>按欄頭排序：</b> 撳任何欄頭（Task title、Priority、Owner、Start、Due ...）- ▲ 由細到大，再撳 ▼ 由大到細，再撳返 list 原本次序；空白嘅排最後，sub-task 都會排，會記住你嘅揀法。拖側欄或者 task 面板嘅邊可以調闊窄（雙擊邊：還原）；task 面板嘅掣（包括 Delete）一定會見到。</li><li><b>Kanban：</b> 一行行卡片；拖張卡去另一行。成塊 board 跟視窗咁高，所以左右嘅 scroll bar 永遠喺畫面底，唔使拉到最底先見到；<b>Shift + 滑鼠轆</b>、拖 board 嘅空位，或者兩邊嘅 <b>‹ ›</b> 掣都可以左右捲。</li><li><b>Gantt：</b> 時間線上面嘅橫條；拖成條，或者拖佢兩頭改日期。每次改之前會彈出 <b>Change the dates?</b> 問你：<b>Save</b> 先會儲存，<b>Cancel</b> 條 bar 就返原位（剔 <b>Don't ask again today</b>，呢部機今日就唔再問）。圖例會解釋啲顏色；milestone 係金色。</li><li><b>Dashboard：</b> 總數、完成、未完成同過咗期，按負責人、按 project、平均用幾耐同就快到期。<b>Activities：</b> 所有改動，邊個改。</li><li><b>Filter ▾</b>（搜尋格旁邊）入面有：邊啲 task（全部、未完成、完成咗、過期、我嘅）、負責人同優先次序，仲有排序（<b>Sort</b>、<b>Group by</b>）；掣上面會講設咗幾多個篩選（「Filter · 2」），<b>Clear filters</b> 還原。用 <b>Customize</b> 揀顯示邊啲欄。每個 list 可以有自己嘅欄（人、選項、文字、日期、數字），例如 Modelers 同 Project Manager。</li></ul><figure class=\"shot\"><img src=\"help-img/tasks-kanban.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><ol><li>Kanban：task 變成卡，每個 group 一欄</li><li>一個 group，連佢嘅 Sheets 同 Dashboard</li><li>一張卡：剔、日期、負責人、sub-task、issue、comment、優先 - 撳打開；拖去另一欄</li><li>喺呢欄加 task</li></ol></figure><figure class=\"shot\"><img src=\"help-img/tasks-gantt.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><ol><li>Gantt：task 喺時間軸上</li><li>縮放：日、星期、月</li><li>Today：返去今日</li><li>每種條同符號嘅意思</li><li>一個 task 同負責人 - 撳打開</li><li>一條 bar：拖成條改日期，拖一端改開始或者完結</li><li>今日</li></ol></figure><figure class=\"shot\"><img src=\"help-img/tasks-dashboard.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><ol><li>Dashboard：用數字睇成個 list</li><li>Group 同時段；計唔計 sub-task</li><li>總數、完成、未完成、過期</li><li>按完成狀態</li><li>按過期狀態</li><li>按負責人 - 撳個名睇佢嘅 task</li><li>由開始到完成嘅平均日數</li><li>每星期完成數量</li></ol></figure>"},{"id":"s9","ch":"Tasks 工作","h":"一個 task","lv":3,"html":"<figure class=\"shot\"><img src=\"help-img/task-detail.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><ol><li>標記完成</li><li>上一個 / 下一個 task (K / J)</li><li>Follow：有改動會收 email</li><li>分享去 chat</li><li>複製 task 連結</li><li>刪除（Ctrl+Z 攞返）</li><li>標題</li><li>負責人、日期、group、優先同 list 自己嘅欄</li><li>描述</li><li>Sub-task</li><li>連結嘅 issue、圖則、3D 視圖同檔案</li></ol></figure><ul><li><b>Owners</b>（同 list 嘅人欄）只會列出 <b>task list 嘅成員</b>；清單最底嘅 <b>Show everyone</b> 可以加其他人。用右上角 <b>Members</b> 加人入 list。</li><li>撳一個 task 打開佢嘅視窗：標題、<b>Owners</b>、開始同到期 <b>Dates</b>、<b>Group</b>、<b>Priority</b> 同 list 自己嘅欄。<b>Mark complete</b> 就完成。</li><li><b>完成方式（Completion method）：</b> <b>OR</b> = 任何一個負責人完成就算完成；<b>AND</b> = 每個負責人都要完成自己嗰部分。</li><li><b>Sub-task：</b> 喺 <b>+ Add sub-task</b> 打字再按 Enter。好似 Lark 咁，sub-task 下面可以再有 sub-task，最多 5 層：打開個 sub-task 喺佢入面加，或者喺 List 撳行尾出現嘅 <b>+</b>。將一個 task 拖去另一個 task 標題嘅右半邊放手，就變成佢嘅 sub-task。刪一個 task 會連佢下面所有嘢一齊刪（<b>Ctrl+Z</b> 可以全部攞返）。 <b>複製同貼上 task：</b> Ctrl 撳幾行揀幾個（Shift 撳：揀一段），再按 <b>Ctrl+C</b> 或者右撳 &gt; <b>Copy</b>（或者 task 面板入面嘅複製掣）。右撳另一個 task &gt; <b>Paste as sub-tasks of ...</b> 或者 <b>Paste below ...</b>，又或者右撳組嘅標題 &gt; <b>Paste into ...</b>（揀咗一個 task 時 <b>Ctrl+V</b> 就貼喺佢下面）。每個副本都帶埋佢嘅 sub-task、標題、描述、負責人、日期、優先次序、欄位同連結，而且由頭開始：未完成、冇百分比、冇留言。貼去另一個 list 都得；一下 <b>Ctrl+Z</b> 就成次貼上收返。</li><li><b>拖動排 sub-task：</b> 喺 List 將一個 sub-task 拖到另一個 sub-task 上面，就會放喺嗰度－可以喺同一個 task 入面改次序，亦可以搬去另一個 task 下面。拖落某個 task 嘅 <b>+ Add sub-task</b> 嗰行，就變成嗰個 task 最後一個 sub-task；拖到一個頂層 task 上面（或者 group 度），就變返一個獨立 task。喺 task 嘅 panel 入面，可以拖 sub-task（⋮⋮）改次序。Task 唔可以放喺自己嘅 sub-task 下面。List 用某一欄排序嘅時候，次序會保留，轉返自己嘅次序就會見到。</li><li><b>相連嘅 issue</b> 會顯示佢而家嘅狀態（Open、In progress、Resolved）。<b>+ Link an issue</b> 可以揀 project 嘅一個 issue。</li><li><b>檔案、sheet 同 3D 視圖：</b> 貼 OneDrive、SharePoint 或者 ACC 網址，或者喺 Sheets 或 3D 版撳 <b>+ Task</b>，將你睇緊嘅 sheet 或者視圖放落 task。放咗落 task 嘅 Revit 元件會顯示做 <b>Elements to change</b>。</li><li><b>留言：</b> @名 可以通知人；可以貼截圖或者夾檔案（每個最大 50 MB）。自己嘅留言有 <b>edit</b> 同 <b>delete</b>。</li><li><b>Follow</b> 之後 task 有改動會 email 你；<b>Share</b> 會傳去一個 chat；連結掣會 copy 佢嘅網址。</li><li>▲ ▼ 掣，或者 <b>K</b> / <b>J</b>，去上一個／下一個 task。手機上面撳 <b>Back</b> 返去清單。</li></ul>"},{"id":"s10","ch":"Tasks 工作","h":"List 嘅成員","lv":3,"html":"<ul><li><b>Owner</b>（改 list 設定同成員）、<b>Editor</b>（加同改 task）同 <b>Viewer</b>（只可以睇）。Site admin 睇到所有 list。</li></ul>"},{"id":"s11","ch":"Tasks 工作","h":"由 Lark import","lv":3,"html":"<ol><li>喺 Lark 打開個 task list，揀 <b>...</b> &gt; <b>Export</b>（Excel）。</li><li>喺 Tasks 用 <b>+</b> &gt; <b>Import a Lark task list (.xlsx)</b> 開一個新 list，或者用 <b>...</b> &gt; <b>Import from Lark (.xlsx) / CSV</b> 放入而家打開緊嘅 list。</li><li>Group、sub-task、負責人、follow 嘅人、日期、完成狀態、優先次序、完成方式、milestone、Modelers 同 Project Manager 全部都會帶入嚟，每個 task 仲有一條連返去 Lark 嘅連結。</li><li>再 import 同一個 export 會更新啲 task，唔會重複加。未有 account 嘅人名會照保留；account 開好之後用 <b>...</b> &gt; <b>Match names to accounts</b>。</li></ol>"},{"id":"s12","ch":"Tasks 工作","h":"Queries 查詢","lv":3,"html":"<p><b>Queries</b>（Tasks 側邊最頂嗰個藍色掣）係每個 project（Projects 頁嗰啲）嘅查詢登記冊，編號 <b>Q-001</b>、<b>Q-002</b> ……例如漏咗尺寸、detail 唔清楚、或者要決定點處理嘅碰撞。佢同 issue 分開：query 係喺 viewer 入面問 team，同埋記低佢哋嘅答覆。<b>Queries</b> 隔離個數字係有幾多個未答、問你嘅 query（同埋你開、已答等你 close 嘅）；有過咗期嘅會多個紅色 <b>N overdue</b>。</p><ul><li><b>開一個 query：</b> 喺上面揀 project，再撳 <b>+ New query</b>：主題、問題、<b>To</b>（project 入面應該答嘅人；Ctrl-click 揀幾個）、<b>Due</b>（預設一星期後）同 <b>Priority</b>。被問嘅人會喺鐘仔收到通知同 email，project 嘅 chat channel 亦會有張卡。</li><li><b>準確視圖嘅相：</b> 喺 sheet 或者 3D model，撳 header 嘅 <b>+ Query</b>（喺 + Task 隔離；3D 喺 <b>⋯</b> menu）。會彈出一個細 menu 問張相放去邊：打主題再撳 <b>Create</b> 開新 query，或者揀 project 一個未完嘅 query（上次用嗰個喺最頂：<b>Add another to Q-...</b>）。<b>After adding：</b> <b>Stay here</b>（會有提示，你可以去下一張 sheet 或者 3D 視圖再撳 <b>+ Query</b>，咁一個 query 就可以有幾張 2D 同 3D 視圖）或者 <b>Open the query</b>（喺 Tasks 打開佢）。你揀咗邊個會記住。Project 入面每個人都可以加相落 query。</li><li><b>打開張相：</b> 喺 query 撳 sheet 嘅相，會打開同一張 sheet、zoom 返同一個位；3D 嘅相會打開 model 同一個鏡頭、section box 同 plane。撳相上面嘅 ✕ 可以拎走佢（開 query 嘅人、被問嘅人或者 project admin）。</li><li><b>自己嘅相：</b> 喺 <b>Pictures &amp; views</b> 下面，<b>+ Add picture</b> 加圖片檔（地盤相、顧問 markup、之前存低嘅 screenshot）；或者貼 screenshot（<b>Ctrl+V</b>），又或者將相拖落 query 個 panel 任何位置。<b>New query</b> 表格都一樣得。撳一下睇大圖；<b>‹ ›</b> 或者方向鍵睇 query 其他相，<b>Esc</b> 閂。Report 入面都有。</li><li><b>喺相上面 mark up：</b> query 每張相（sheet、3D 視圖或者自己嘅相）上面嘅 ✎ 會打開同 issue snapshot 一樣嘅 markup 工具：cloud、方框、圓形、箭咀、線、筆、文字、文字框、callout，可以揀顏色、粗幼同字大小。撳 <b>Done</b> 就會將畫嘅嘢留喺相上面；✎ 隔籬會顯示有幾多個記號，再打開可以繼續改（原本嘅相會保留喺底）。喺 sheet 或者 3D 嘅 <b>+ Query</b> menu 剔 <b>Mark up the picture first</b>，就可以喺加入之前先畫。</li><li><b>+ Sheet view / + 3D view：</b> 喺 query 入面（同 <b>New query</b> 表格，會先開咗個 query）撳呢兩個掣，會打開 project 嘅 sheet 或者 3D model，頂部有條 bar 講緊加去邊個 query；去到想要嘅視圖再撳 <b>+ Query</b>（或者右掣 &gt; <b>Add to query here</b>），嗰個 query 會排第一。<b>Back to the query</b> 返去。有幾部分嘅 project 會問你揀邊部分。</li><li><b>答、追問同 close：</b> 被問嘅人寫 <b>Answer</b> 再撳 <b>Mark answered</b>。之後喺 <b>Answer &amp; follow-ups</b> 下面，project 入面任何人都可以撳 <b>+ Follow-up question</b> 追問（query 會返去 Open），被問嘅人就用 <b>+ Answer</b> 再答，幾多次都得；成段對話用對話框顯示（問題喺左、答案喺右），每一步都會通知有關嘅人，同埋喺 project chat 貼張卡。搞掂之後，開 query 嘅人（或者 project admin）撳 <b>Close the query</b>。下面嘅 <b>Discussion</b> 係俾留言同檔案用。<b>Reopen</b> 重開已 close 嘅 query。<b>History</b> 列出每一步。</li><li><b>Sheet 同 3D 上面嘅 query：</b> query 每張 sheet 或者 3D 嘅相都會喺影嘅位置出現－喺 sheet 係一個標記（<b>Q12</b>，用狀態顏色：橙色未答、藍色已答、綠色已 close、紅色過期），仲有虛線框住當時睇緊嘅範圍；喺 3D 係一支 pin。喺 sheet 或者 model 撳右掣 &gt; <b>Add to query here</b>，會影低個視圖，標記就放喺你撳嘅位置（之後同 <b>+ Query</b> 一樣嘅 menu）。撳標記或者 pin 會彈張卡：query、狀態、due date、張相、<b>Open query</b> 同 <b>Delete marker</b>。</li><li><b>列表同隱藏：</b> Sheets 右邊有個 <b>Queries</b> tab（<b>All</b> 亦會排先列出）；3D 嘅 issue 列表最頂有 <b>Queries in 3D</b>。撳一下就會去嗰個 sheet 範圍或者 3D 視圖，再打開張卡。Status filter 同搜尋都用得。<b>? Queries</b>（Sheets）/ <b>Hide queries</b>（3D）收埋啲標記；<b>Hide closed</b> 亦會收埋已 close 嘅 query。</li><li><b>刪除：</b> <b>Delete marker</b>（喺張卡，或者右掣撳標記）會將嗰張相由 query 拎走－query 會保留，連埋其他相。刪咗 query，佢所有標記都會消失。開 query 嘅人、被問嘅人、project admin 或者加嗰張相嘅人都可以刪標記。</li><li><b>Tasks：</b> <b>+ New task from this query</b> 喺你嘅 list 開一個 task（負責人係被問嘅人、due date 同 query 一樣，仲有連結返去 query 同佢啲相）；<b>Link a task</b> 連一個已有嘅 task。啲 task 會顯示做完未。</li><li><b>List：</b> 用狀態篩選（Open and answered、Open、Overdue、Answered - to close、Closed、All），同 <b>To me</b> / <b>Raised by me</b>，或者搜尋。過咗期嘅 query 係紅色。</li><li><b>Calendar：</b> 問你或者你開嘅未完 query，due date 會喺 Calendar 出現（<b>My queries</b>）；撳一下打開佢。</li><li><b>Chat：</b> 打訊息時打 <b>?</b> 加幾個字就可以連一個 query（或者用連結掣 &gt; <b>? Query</b>）；<b>+</b> &gt; <b>Query</b> 喺 chat 嘅 project 開一個新 query 再貼張卡。query 上面嘅 <b>Send to chat</b> 會再貼張卡去 project 嘅 channel。</li><li><b>Dashboard</b> tab：未答、過期、7 日內到期、已答待 close、今個月 close 咗同平均幾多日答；按狀態、每人未答（紅色：過期）同每星期開咗同答咗幾多。撳一格就喺 list 睇返嗰啲 query。</li><li><b>Report (PDF)：</b> 登記表（編號、主題、邊個開、問邊個、due、狀態、幾時答）再逐個 query 列出問題、相同答覆，跟 list 而家嘅篩選。<b>Print / Save as PDF</b>，或者 <b>Save to Folders</b>（PDF 放喺 Folders &gt; Queries）。</li></ul>"},{"id":"s13","ch":"Board 白板","h":"Board 白板","lv":2,"html":"<figure class=\"shot\"><img src=\"help-img/board.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><ol><li>Boards：project 所有白板、新白板、範本</li><li>白板名稱</li><li>而家邊個喺白板</li><li>搵白板上嘅字</li><li>大家一齊睇嘅倒數計時</li><li>Present：逐個框展示</li><li>Export：圖片、PDF、備份</li><li>揀選同移動；拖動白板</li><li>便條、文字、形狀、連接線、思維圖、筆</li><li>框、圖片、連去 issue 或圖則嘅卡</li><li>復原 / 重做</li><li>白板：雙擊寫字</li><li>總覽地圖、縮放、Fit</li></ol></figure><p><b>Board</b> 係每個 project 一塊共用白板，好似 Miro 咁：便利貼、文字、形狀、連接線、mind map、相同 frame，仲有範本可以由頭開始。Project 入面所有人會即時見到改動。喺頂部揀 project；用 board 清單開新、改名、複製或者刪除 board。</p><p>之前打開過嘅 board 會即刻由呢部機顯示；之後其他人做嘅改動幾秒內就會到。Sign out 會清走留喺部機嘅版本（Board、Tasks、Dashboard）。</p><p><b>LWK BIM Workflow board</b></p><p>每個 project 一開始就有一塊叫 <b>LWK BIM Workflow</b> 嘅 board：公司嘅 BIM 工作流程，係呢個 project 自己嘅一份，可以按 project 需要改。第一個有權改嘢嘅人打開呢個 project 嘅 Board 頁，佢就會自動整出嚟。</p><ul><li><b>入面有乜：</b> 0 Project card（編號、名稱、階段、軟件、CDE 位置 - kick-off 時填）· 1 點用呢塊 board · 2 團隊同角色（職責、需要嘅知識、一欄填人名）· 3 工作階段（由 Inception 到 Completion，邊個主導、出乜嘢）· 4.0-4.6 流程圖：Project setup (1.0)、Modelling (2.0)、Model review / design changes (2.1)、用 SAM 發展 model (2.3)、ACC clash detection (3.0)、用 BD Area Tool 做 GBP submission (4.0 / 4.1) · 5 CDE folder 狀態（ISO 19650）· 6 QA/QC 檢查 · 7 BIM audit checklist · 8 會議 · 9 Viewer 點樣支援每一步 · 10 Project notes · 11 參考圖。</li><li><b>顏色：</b> 每個角色喺所有流程圖都用同一隻顏色（BIM Manager、HK Coordinator、Manila Senior Coordinator、Task Team Lead、BIM Authors、Project Team、Design Team、CAD Team）；每個圖下面有圖例。</li><li><b>Audit checklist：</b> board 上面列晒所有項目做指引。正式嘅 audit 紀錄仍然係 Excel：整 board 嗰陣，會喺 project 嘅 <b>Folders</b> 入面 <b>BIM QA</b> 放一份空白嘅 <b>LWK BIM Audit Checklist.xlsx</b>（如果嗰度未有同名檔案）。</li><li><b>本身已經有 board 嘅 project</b> 唔會自動加。用 <b>New board</b> &gt; <b>LWK BIM Workflow</b> 加；任何 project 都可以咁樣再加多一份。</li><li>入面全部都係普通 board 內容：搬、改色、加、刪都得。刪咗呢塊 board 唔會自己再出返嚟。</li></ul>"},{"id":"s14","ch":"Messenger 訊息","h":"Messenger 訊息","lv":2,"html":"<figure class=\"shot\"><img src=\"help-img/chat.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><ol><li>搜尋 chat（Enter：搜尋訊息）</li><li>新 chat：私訊或者 group</li><li>Project channel - 每個 project 一個</li><li>Group 同私訊</li><li>Task 討論</li><li>打開 project、圖則或者 3D</li><li>Chat 入面嘅檔案</li><li>成員</li><li>Topic：單一題目嘅子 channel</li><li>訊息</li><li>寫訊息：@ 人、# task、! issue、$ 圖則、% 3D 視圖</li><li>粗體、列表、引用、連結、程式碼</li><li>表情、提及、連結、檔案、投票 / 活動 / task</li><li>傳送 (Enter)</li></ol></figure><p>拖對話列表或者詳情面板嘅邊可以調闊窄；列表邊上嘅小標籤可以釘住，或者 - 唔釘 - 收埋列表，令對話闊啲（同 Sheets 同 3D 頁一樣）。</p><p><b>Chat</b> 會打開 Messenger：團隊嘅對話，就喺佢哋講緊嘅工作隔籬。</p><p><b>Chat 嘅種類</b></p><table><tr><th>Chat</th><th>係乜</th></tr><tr><td>Project channel</td><td>每個 project 一個，有自己嘅顏色同縮寫（入面嘅 topic 用同一隻顏色）。project 所有人都喺入面。新 task、指派、完成、task 留言、進度（task 過咗 25、50 或者 75 %）同新開或者改咗嘅 issue 會用卡片貼入嚟。Task 卡會顯示進度條同幾多個 sub-task 做完；sub-task 張卡亦會講佢屬於邊個 task，同埋嗰個 task 做到幾多</td></tr><tr><td>Topic</td><td>Project channel 入面講一樣嘢嘅分台（例如 Facade、MEP coordination、Site visits）。會列喺 channel 下面，亦會喺 channel 名下面做 tab 顯示：<b># General</b> 就係 channel 本身</td></tr><tr><td>Group</td><td>任何一班人，由開 group 嘅人改名</td></tr><tr><td>Direct message</td><td>兩個人</td></tr><tr><td>Task discussion</td><td>你 follow 緊嘅 task 嘅留言，可以喺度直接回覆</td></tr></table><ul><li>頂部支筆開新 chat。喺 chat 上面撳右鍵（手機就㩒住佢）會有 <b>Details</b>、<b>Mark as read</b>、<b>New topic</b>（project channel）、<b>Leave</b>、<b>Import WhatsApp chat ...</b>、<b>Send chat link to WhatsApp</b>，有權刪嘅人仲有 <b>Delete chat</b>。</li><li><b>開 topic：</b> project channel 入面任何人都可以喺 channel 名下面嘅 tab 撳 <b>+ Topic</b>（或者 channel 選單嘅 <b>New topic</b>，或者支筆 &gt; <b>Topic in a project channel</b>）。Channel 入面所有人都會加入去。</li><li><b>邊個可以刪 chat：</b> direct message 係兩個人任何一個（刪咗兩邊都冇）；group 係佢嘅 admin（開 group 嘅人）或者 site admin；project channel 同 topic 係 project 嘅 admin 或者 site admin。刪 channel 會連佢嘅 topic 一齊刪。</li><li><b>Chat info</b>（人仔掣）：描述、成員（加、移除、私訊）、<b>Pictures and files</b>、<b>Leave this chat</b> 同 <b>Delete this chat</b>。</li><li>每一版頂部 <b>Chat</b> 上面嘅數字係未讀訊息；<b>@</b> 即係有人 mention 你。</li></ul><p><b>打字</b></p><ul><li><b>Enter</b> 係換行；撳 <b>Send</b> 掣先會發送（用鍵盤嘅話，<b>Ctrl+Enter</b> 都會發送）。</li><li>可以貼或者拖截圖入嚟，或者用夾萬（📎）傳相同檔案，每個最大 50 MB。OneDrive、SharePoint 同 ACC 連結會顯示做卡片；影片連結會有播放卡，貼 OneDrive 或 SharePoint 嘅 <b>Embed</b> code 就可以喺 chat 入面直接播。</li><li><b>@</b> 一個人。<b>#</b> 一個 task、<b>!</b> 一個 issue、<b>$</b> 一張 sheet、<b>%</b> 3D model 或者儲存咗嘅視圖：一打就會彈出清單。<b>先揀 project</b>：清單最頂有一排 project 俾你揀（喺 project channel 會預先揀好嗰個 project）。夾萬隔籬嘅 <b>#</b> 掣會打開同一啲清單，有分頁。</li><li>揀咗嘅項目會喺訊息入面變成一條有名嘅連結，撳就打開。</li><li>🙂 可以加 emoji。</li><li><b>格式（Aa）：</b> 好似 Lark 咁，輸入框直接顯示發出去嘅樣。<b>Aa</b> 會顯示格式掣：<b>B</b>、<b>S</b>、<b>I</b>、<b>U</b>、編號同 bullet 清單、引用、連結、code 同 code block；<b>Ctrl+B</b>、<b>Ctrl+I</b>、<b>Ctrl+U</b> 同 <b>Ctrl+Shift+X</b> 對揀咗嘅字用。手機上面撳 <b>Aa</b> 之後格式掣會自己一行出現。轉去 WhatsApp 都會保留粗體、斜體同刪除線。</li><li><b>輸入框下面嘅掣：</b> <b>Aa</b>、🙂 emoji、<b>@</b> 人、<b>#</b> task、issue、sheet 或者 3D 視圖（喺框入面顯示做 chip）、夾萬、<b>+</b> 同 <b>Send</b>；<b>Send</b> 永遠喺畫面入面，手機都係。</li><li><b>+ 掣：</b> <b>Poll</b>、<b>Event / meeting</b>、<b>Task</b>，或者連結一個 task、issue、sheet 或者 3D 視圖。</li></ul><p><b>投票、活動同 task</b></p><ul><li><b>Poll（投票）：</b> 一條問題，2 至 10 個選擇；想嘅話剔 <b>Allow more than one answer</b>、<b>Anonymous</b> 或者揀截止日期。撳一個選擇就投票，再撳就取消。寫嘅人可以 <b>Close poll</b>（亦可以重開）。</li><li><b>Event（活動）：</b> 標題、日期、時間（或者 <b>All day</b>）、地點同 Teams 連結。Chat 入面所有人都會收到邀請（mail 設定好嘅話仲會有 email），可以答 <b>Going</b>、<b>Maybe</b> 或者 <b>Can't go</b>。<b>Add to calendar (.ics)</b> 可以放入 Outlook、Google 或者手機日曆。寫嘅人可以 <b>Change</b> 或者 <b>Cancel event</b>；chat 會收到通知。</li><li><b>Task：</b> 揀 task list 同 group（呢個 project 嘅排先）、負責人（揀咗嗰個 list 嘅成員；<b>Show everyone</b> 睇其他人）、到期日同優先次序。Task 會放入個 list，佢張卡片會出現喺 chat。喺任何訊息撳 ⋯ More &gt; <b>Make a task</b> 都一樣，訊息會變成描述，@mention 咗嘅人做負責人，仲有條連結返去嗰條訊息。</li></ul><p><b>一條訊息</b></p><ul><li>滑鼠移到訊息上面（手機就撳一下）：🙂 <b>React</b>、↩ <b>Reply</b>、✏ <b>Edit</b>（自己嘅訊息）同 ⋯ <b>More</b>：<b>Copy</b>、<b>Pin</b>、<b>Make a task</b>、<b>Forward to another chat</b>、<b>Send to WhatsApp</b>、<b>Copy link to this message</b> 同 <b>Delete</b>（自己嘅訊息）。</li><li><b>Edit</b> 直接喺原位改：<b>Ctrl+Enter</b> 儲存，<b>Esc</b> 取消；其他人會見到「(edited)」。<b>Edit</b> 同 <b>Delete</b> 只限發訊息嘅人（chat 嘅 admin 同 site admin 都唔得）；其他人會見到「message deleted」。</li><li><b>Pin 訊息：</b> chat 入面任何人都可以 pin 訊息，每個 chat 最多 100 條。Chat 名下面嗰條會顯示最新 pin 嘅一條；撳佢就去睇嗰條訊息，再轉去下一條；<b>All</b> 會列晒出嚟，可以 <b>unpin</b>。</li><li><b>Reaction</b> 會喺訊息下面顯示，連數目；撳一下就加或者攞走你嘅。</li><li>發唔到嘅訊息會留低，有 <b>send again</b> 俾你再試。</li></ul><p><b>WhatsApp</b></p><ul><li><b>轉出去：</b> 訊息上面嘅 <b>Send to WhatsApp</b> 會將文字、連結同檔案傳出去。手機上面相片會原本咁經分享選單傳過去；電腦就會打開 WhatsApp Desktop 或者 WhatsApp Web。</li><li><b>Copy 咗嘅訊息：</b> 喺 WhatsApp copy 幾條訊息，貼入輸入框，會問你係咪變成一個「From WhatsApp」引用。</li><li><b>匯出成個 chat：</b> 喺 WhatsApp 打開個 chat &gt; <b>More</b> &gt; <b>Export chat</b>，將 .zip（有相）或者 .txt 傳俾自己。然後喺 chat 選單揀 <b>Import WhatsApp chat ...</b>：啲訊息會變成一個引用，相片放返喺原本嘅位置。</li><li><b>Android：</b> 將 viewer 安裝做 app 之後，喺 WhatsApp 撳 <b>Share</b> &gt; <b>LWK Viewer</b>，再揀 chat。（iPhone 唔支援：用 copy 貼上，或者匯出。）</li><li>同 WhatsApp 之間冇自動雙向同步。</li></ul>"},{"id":"s15","ch":"Calendar 日曆","h":"Calendar 日曆","lv":2,"html":"<figure class=\"shot\"><img src=\"help-img/calendar.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><ol><li>上一頁 / 今日 / 下一頁</li><li>顯示緊嘅月份（或者星期）</li><li>Groups：睇一個團隊嘅假期</li><li>月、星期或清單</li><li>Sync to Outlook：喺 Outlook 睇呢個日曆，會自己更新</li><li>+ New：活動、會議、task 或者請假</li><li>Show：撳一類嚟隱藏或顯示；Holidays ▾ 揀香港 / 菲律賓</li><li>你嘅 task 喺到期日 - 撳一下打開</li></ol></figure><p><b>右撳某一日</b>（手機㩒住）可以喺嗰日加 <b>event</b>（全日）、<b>meeting</b>（10:00 開始，揀邀請邊個 chat）或者一個嗰日到期嘅 <b>task</b>。</p><p><b>Calendar</b> 按日期顯示你就嚟要做嘅嘢：Messenger 入面發嘅<b>會議</b>（連你嘅回覆）、<b>你嘅 task</b> 嘅到期日 - 連你負責嘅 task 下面嘅 <b>sub-task</b>（任何一層，會寫 <b>Sub-task of ...</b>），同埋下面有你嘅 sub-task 嘅 task（佢自己嘅到期日會同 sub-task 一齊顯示）- 同<b>派咗俾你嘅 issue</b> 嘅到期日。</p><ul><li>電腦係月曆，手機係清單（<b>Month</b> / <b>Week</b> / <b>List</b>）。<b>Show</b> 嗰行係圖例亦係開關：撳 <b>Issue due dates</b>、<b>Tasks</b>、<b>Holidays</b>、<b>Team leave</b> 或者 <b>Meetings</b> 就隱藏或者顯示。<b>Filter ▾</b> 仲可以設定 <b>Week starts on: Monday / Sunday</b>（會記住）。<b>‹ ›</b> 同 <b>Today</b> 轉月（或者星期）；手機就掃。</li><li>撳一項睇詳情，再打開個 chat、task 或者 issue。回覆會議要喺佢個 chat 入面。</li><li><b>+ New ▾：</b> <b>Event</b> 或者 <b>Meeting</b>（揀一個 chat，表格喺嗰度打開，chat 入面所有人都會被邀請）、<b>Task</b>，或者 <b>Leave</b>。</li><li><b>Sync to Outlook：</b> <b>Open in Outlook on this PC</b> 會令 Outlook 訂閱你嘅日曆（揀 <b>Yes</b>），或者 copy 個地址，用 Outlook 嘅 <b>Add calendar &gt; From Internet</b>。之後 Outlook 會喺你自己嘅日曆隔籬顯示，並自己更新。Outlook 網頁版同手機版要 viewer 喺互聯網上連得到先得。</li><li>個地址係你自己嘅：唔小心分享咗就撳 <b>Make a new address</b>（舊嗰個會停用）。</li></ul>"},{"id":"s16","ch":"Calendar 日曆","h":"公眾假期","lv":3,"html":"<ul><li><b>Holidays ▾</b> 喺日曆顯示<b>香港</b>同／或者<b>菲律賓</b>嘅公眾假期（剔一個或者兩個；會記住）。2026 同 2027 年嘅已經內置（香港：憲報；菲律賓：Proclamation No. 1006 同 1427，regular holidays 同 special non-working days）。</li><li>Site admin 可以加之後年份同遲啲先公佈嘅日子（菲律賓嘅 Eid'l Fitr 同 Eid'l Adha）：<b>Holidays ▾ &gt; Edit the list</b>，一行一個，例如 <i>2028-01-01 New Year's Day</i>。</li></ul>"},{"id":"s17","ch":"Calendar 日曆","h":"年假同日曆群組","lv":3,"html":"<ul><li><b>+ New ▾ &gt; Leave</b>、<b>右撳某一日 &gt; Add leave</b>，或者喺月曆<b>拖過幾日</b>：由邊日到邊日、類別（年假、病假、其他）、半日（AM／PM，只限一日）同備註。表格會計工作天（星期六日同剔咗嘅假期唔計；冇剔就用香港假期）。</li><li>你嘅假期會喺你同埋同你喺同一個<b>日曆群組</b>嘅人嘅日曆出現；佢哋嘅都會喺你嘅出現。撳一個假期睇詳情；<b>Remove this leave</b> 可以刪走你自己嘅。</li><li><b>Groups：</b> <b>+ New group</b>，改名同揀人（人人都開得；你自己一定喺入面）。開群組嘅人（或者 site admin）可以改或者刪；其他人可以 <b>Leave group</b>。<b>Filter ▾ &gt; Leave of</b> 只顯示某一個群組嘅假期。</li><li>Outlook（Sync to Outlook）只會有你自己嘅假期，唔會有同事嘅。</li></ul>"},{"id":"s18","ch":"通知同 app","h":"通知同 app","lv":2,"html":"<figure class=\"shot\"><img src=\"help-img/bell.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><ol><li>For you：派俾你嘅 task、@ 你、指派俾你嘅 issue - 剔咗就當睇咗</li><li>全部標記已讀</li><li>呢個瀏覽器嘅 chat 通知</li><li>通知我：每個訊息、只係 @ 我，或者乜都唔通知</li><li>冇開頁面都推送；Send a test 試吓</li><li>App：安裝之後有自己嘅視窗同數字標記</li><li>外觀：淺色、深色、自動</li><li>Viewer 有咩新嘢</li></ol></figure><p>有新訊息唔使 refresh 都會通知你，viewer 仲可以裝成一個 app。</p><ul><li><b>開住任何一版 viewer 嘅時候</b>（任何一版、背景嘅分頁，或者個 app）：新訊息會喺 Windows、Mac 同 Android 彈通知；撳一下就打開嗰個 chat 去到嗰條訊息。你睇緊嗰個 chat 就唔會彈。分頁標題會顯示未讀數，例如 <b>(3) LWK Viewer</b>，app 個 icon 都會有。</li><li><b>頂部嘅鈴</b>：撳 <b>Turn on notifications</b>（瀏覽器會問一次），再揀 <b>Every message</b>（所有訊息）、<b>@mentions and direct messages</b>（只係 @你 同私訊）或者 <b>Nothing</b>（唔通知）。</li><li><b>某個 chat 靜音：</b> Chat info &gt; <b>Mute notifications</b>。靜咗音嘅 chat 有人 @你 都照通知。</li><li><b>唔止訊息：</b> 有 task 派咗俾你、有人喺 task 或者 issue 度 @你、有 issue 派咗俾你或者你嘅 query 有人答、你嘅 task 就快到期，都會通知你。鈴入面嘅 <b>For you</b> 清單列出最近嘅（紅色數字係未睇嘅）；撳一項就打開，<b>Mark all read</b> 清咗個數字。<b>每項旁邊個格</b>可以剔做已讀、或者取消剔做返未讀，唔使打開。</li><li><b>裝 app：</b> 鈴 &gt; <b>Install the app</b>（Edge、Chrome），或者網址列右邊嘅安裝 icon。Android：選單 &gt; <b>Add to Home screen</b>。iPhone／iPad：Safari &gt; 分享 &gt; <b>加至主畫面</b>。App 會用自己嘅視窗打開，右撳 icon 有 Chat、Tasks、Calendar、Folders 同 Projects 捷徑。</li><li><b>冇開任何一版都收到（push）：</b> 鈴 &gt; <b>Turn on for this device</b>。要用 viewer 嘅 <b>https</b> 地址開先得（問你嘅 admin）。之後就算 app 閂咗，部手機或者電腦都會收到訊息。</li><li><b>iPhone／iPad：</b> 先喺 Safari &gt; 分享 &gt; <b>加至主畫面</b>，再由主畫面個 icon 打開；然後喺鈴度開通知、撳 <b>Turn on for this device</b>，再撳 <b>Send a test</b>。收唔到嘅話，會講埋原因（例如 server 連唔到 Apple）。Server 更新之後，請關一次再開一次 push。</li></ul>"},{"id":"s19","ch":"外觀、連結同新功能","h":"外觀、連結同新功能","lv":2,"html":"<figure class=\"shot\"><img src=\"help-img/profile-menu.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><ol><li>你嘅頭像：打開呢個選單</li><li>離線工作：將呢個 project 存喺呢部機</li><li>Admin：人同 project 成員</li><li>Account：你嘅密碼</li><li>Help (F1)</li><li>主題：淺色、深色、自動</li><li>登出</li></ol></figure><p>幾樣小嘢，等你喺 viewer 入面易啲搵路，又易啲同人分享。</p><ul><li><b>深色模式（Dark mode）：</b> 鈴 &gt; <b>Look</b> &gt; <b>Dark</b>。<b>Auto</b> 跟你部電腦或者手機（佢設咗夜晚轉深色就跟住轉）；<b>Light</b> 係平時嘅樣。每部電腦、每部手機各自記住。圖則、PDF、文件預覽同白板會保持白色（當係紙）；3D 背景會變深灰，除非你喺 Display 揀咗自己嘅顏色。</li><li><b>新功能（What's new）：</b> 每次更新之後會彈一張小卡，講有咩改咗，只出一次。撳 <b>Got it</b> 收埋；隨時都可以喺鈴 &gt; <b>What's new in the viewer</b> 睇晒成個列表。</li><li><b>複製連結（Copy link，🔗 掣）：</b> 複製一個網址，可以貼落 chat 或者 email。只有 project 入面嘅人先開到。</li><li><b>一張 sheet：</b> sheet 工具列嘅 🔗。<b>一個 issue：</b> issue 頂部嘅 🔗（2D 或 3D）。<b>一個 project：</b> Projects 版 project panel 嘅 🔗。<b>一個 3D 視角：</b> 3D 頂部 <b>BCF</b> 隔籬嘅 🔗，會複製返一模一樣嘅視角 - 鏡頭、section box 或 plane、樓層、顯示模式同隱藏咗嘅元件 - 開嘅人會見到一樣嘢。</li><li><b>可以摺埋嘅部分：</b> 喺 project panel（Projects 版）、Admin 版或者 3D 左邊 panel，撳個標題就摺埋或者打開。viewer 會記住你摺埋咗邊啲。</li><li><b>列表記住你去到邊：</b> Folders 會重新打開你之前喺樹度開咗嘅 folder；sheet 列表同 chat 列表會將你而家嗰個保持喺眼前。</li><li><b>列表載入緊嘅時候</b> 會見到灰色嘅佔位行，話你知內容會喺邊度出。</li></ul>"},{"id":"s20","ch":"還原（Undo）","h":"還原（Undo）","lv":2,"html":"<ul><li><b>Ctrl+Z</b>（Mac 係 Cmd+Z）還原上一個改動；<b>Ctrl+Y</b>（或者 Ctrl+Shift+Z）重做。底部會顯示還原咗乜嘢，有 <b>Redo</b> 掣。</li><li><b>Tasks：</b> 改欄、Kanban 搬卡、List 拖行、Gantt 改日期、開新 task，同刪除 task（連埋佢嘅 sub-task）。</li><li><b>Messenger：</b> 刪咗嘅訊息（自己嘅，一日之內）、修改、pin 同 reaction。</li><li><b>Folders：</b> 刪除、改名、搬、上載同開新 folder。</li><li>喺輸入框打緊字嘅時候，Ctrl+Z 照舊還原打字。Sheets 同 3D 版嘅 markup 有自己嘅 undo。</li></ul>"},{"id":"s21","ch":"Folders 檔案夾","h":"Folders 檔案夾","lv":2,"html":"<figure class=\"shot\"><img src=\"help-img/folders.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><ol><li>釘選、星號、最近、最近刪除</li><li>資料夾（拖檔案嚟搬）</li><li>隱藏或顯示資料夾</li><li>而家喺邊</li><li>搜尋呢個 project 嘅檔案</li><li>+ 資料夾</li><li>上載</li><li>將檔案拖到呢度上載入呢個資料夾（或者撳）</li><li>撳欄頭排序</li><li>鎖住嘅 00 BIM：由 Revit 嚟嘅圖則同 model</li><li>更多：改名、搬、版本、釘選、星號、刪除</li></ol></figure><p>喺左邊 folder 樹右撳一個 folder（或者用 folder 嘅 ⋯），可以 <b>New folder here</b>（喺度開新 folder）、改名、<b>Move to ...</b>、加星、Pin、copy 連結同刪除。</p><p><b>唔使下載都睇到：</b> 撳 PDF、相、片、文字檔，或者 <b>Word、Excel、PowerPoint</b>，就會喺清單隔籬打開。Server 裝咗 LibreOffice（問你嘅 admin）嘅話，Office 檔案會同喺 Office 入面一模一樣；未裝就用簡單啲嘅方式顯示 Word 同 Excel，PowerPoint 要下載。</p><ul><li><b>俾文件多啲位：</b> 清單左上角嘅 <b>☰</b> 收埋／打開左邊 folder 欄（會記住）。預覽入面嘅 <b>⤢</b> 連 folder 同檔案清單都收埋，文件用晒成個闊度；再撳一次或者 <b>Esc</b> 就返嚟。拖預覽嘅左邊邊位可以拉闊。</li><li><b>成版睇晒：</b> 喺網頁度顯示嘅 Word 同 Excel 一開就係 <b>Fit</b>：最闊嗰版（橫向都得）啱啱好放得落預覽闊度，電腦同手機都係。<b>−</b>、<b>+</b> 縮放；<b>Fit</b> 返原。PDF 一打開就係頁闊。</li><li><b>手機同平板</b>（打直或者打橫）：文件會全屏打開，PDF 同轉換咗嘅 Office 檔案一頁接一頁，可以向下碌晒全部頁；兩隻手指 pinch 或者用 <b>−</b> / <b>+</b> 縮放。<b>☰</b> 打開 folder 欄，撳旁邊空位就收返。</li><li><b>Admin 用 - 喺 server 裝 LibreOffice</b>（Ubuntu）：`sudo apt-get install -y --no-install-recommends libreoffice-writer libreoffice-calc libreoffice-impress fonts-noto-cjk fonts-liberation fonts-crosextra-carlito fonts-crosextra-caladea`，然後重開 viewer service。Writer、Calc、Impress 三個都要裝：淨係得 libreoffice-core 嘅話，網頁會話「cannot read this kind of file」。大文件第一次要等一陣，之後有 cache，即刻開到。</li></ul><p><b>Folders</b> 將每個 project 嘅檔案放喺 server 上面一個 folder，好似 ACC Docs 或者共用 drive 咁。喺左上角揀 project。</p><p><b>00 BIM</b>（🔒，永遠排第一）放住 viewer 已有嘅嘢，自動更新：<b>2D Sheets</b>（由 Revit 出嘅 sheet，用編號同名稱命名，同埋喺 Sheets 頁上載嘅 PDF set）同 <b>3D Models</b>（喺 3D 頁打開；IFC 檔案 - IFC project 同顧問 model - 可以下載）。Project 入面所有人都可以打開同下載，但冇人可以加、改名、搬或者刪。有幾個部分嘅 project，每部分一個 folder。</p><p><b>匯出存入 Folders：</b> 任何匯出下載完（碰撞或淨高 spreadsheet、Dashboard spreadsheet、BCF、加咗 markup 嘅 PDF、board 圖片或備份），底部會有條 bar 提供 <b>Save to Folders</b>；報告（碰撞、淨高、issue report）喺 Print 旁邊有 <b>Save to Folders (PDF)</b> - 由 server 整 PDF。佢哋存喺 <b>00 BIM &gt; Exports &gt; Clash / Headroom / Issues / BCF / Markups / Board</b>，每週報告存喺 <b>00 BIM &gt; Weekly dashboard</b>，記低係邊個存。同 00 BIM 其他嘢一樣，喺嗰度唔可以改名或者刪除（要改就下載一份）。同名嘅檔案會加「(2)」。</p><ul><li><b>瀏覽：</b> 左邊嘅 folder 樹、頂部嘅路徑，或者 <b>Search this project's files</b> 搜尋。雙擊 folder 打開；撳 PDF、相或者片就預覽。</li><li><b>上載：</b> 將檔案，甚至成個 folder 拖落版面（或者拖落清單入面某個 folder），或者撳 <b>Upload</b>。<b>+ Folder</b> 開新 folder。</li><li><b>檔案嘅 ⋯</b>（或者右撳）：預覽、下載、<b>Add to the Sheets page</b>（PDF）、<b>Star</b>（加星）、<b>Pin for everyone</b>（project admin）、copy 連結、改名、<b>Move to ...</b> 同刪除。揀咗檔案可以用 <b>Delete</b> 同 <b>F2</b>。</li><li><b>拖放，好似 OneDrive 咁：</b> 將清單入面嘅檔案或者 folder - 或者左邊 folder 樹嘅一個 folder - 拖落清單、folder 樹或者頂部路徑入面任何一個 folder。喺樹入面停喺一個未打開嘅 folder 上面一陣，佢就會打開，等你放得入深層；拖到樹嘅頂或者底會自動捲動。指標旁邊會講會發生乜事。放手時㩒住 <b>Ctrl</b> 就係<b>複製</b>，唔係搬。<b>Ctrl+Z</b> 可以還原。</li><li><b>版本（Versions）：</b> 上載一個 folder 入面已經有同名嘅檔案，頁面會問：<b>New version</b>（同名同位置；原本嗰個保留做上一個版本）或者 <b>Keep both</b>（「name (2)」）。可以寫低改咗乜（例如 <i>Rev B - layout revised</i>）。有版本嘅檔案名旁邊會顯示 <b>v2</b>、<b>v3</b> ...。<b>⋯ &gt; Versions</b>（或者預覽入面嘅 <b>Versions</b>）列出晒所有版本 - 邊個、幾時、改咗乜 - 可以 <b>Open</b>（喺預覽顯示，並註明係舊版本）、<b>⬇</b> 下載同 <b>Make current</b>，將舊版本攞返做最新版本（乜都唔會冇咗）。Project admin 可以用 <b>✕</b> 刪走舊版本。搬、改名、刪除同還原檔案，佢嘅版本都會跟住。</li><li><b>Pinned</b> 係 project admin 幫大家 pin 嘅重要文件；<b>Starred</b> 係你自己加星嘅。<b>Recent</b> 列出最新嘅檔案。</li><li><b>刪除：</b> 上載嗰個人，或者 project admin。刪咗嘅嘢會去 <b>Recently deleted</b>，可以放返原位；<b>Ctrl+Z</b> 都可以即刻攞返。</li><li><b>排序同欄位：</b> 撳 <b>Name</b>、<b>Modified</b>、<b>Size</b> 或者 <b>Uploaded by</b> 排序（▲、▼，再撳還原；資料夾排先）。拖資料夾樹或者預覽嘅邊可以調闊窄。</li><li><b>Folder 範本（project admin）：</b> 右上 ⋯ &gt; <b>Save these folders as a template</b>，將呢個 project 嘅 folder 結構（唔包檔案）用個名儲起。喺另一個 project 用 <b>Lay out folders from a template</b>，就會開返佢未有嘅 folder；乜都唔會刪。</li><li><b>放去 Sheets 版：</b> PDF 嘅 ⋯ &gt; <b>Add to the Sheets page</b>，每一頁變成一張 sheet，放喺自己一個 set（揀 set 名同 sheet 編號），即刻可以 markup 同開 issue。</li><li>用其他方法（例如 Windows Explorer）放入 server 上面嗰個 folder 嘅檔案，呢度都會見到。</li></ul>"},{"id":"s22","ch":"Sheets：2D 圖則","h":"Sheets：2D 圖則","lv":2,"html":"<figure class=\"shot\"><img src=\"help-img/sheets.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><ol><li>圖則清單 - 撳一張打開</li><li>搜尋圖號、圖名同圖上嘅字</li><li>Set：顯示邊組圖則（Revit 嘅，或者上載嘅 PDF 組）；改名、封存、刪除一組</li><li>Mark-up 工具，按類分組（下一張圖）</li><li>Comment / + Issue：畫嘅嘢變成 comment 定 issue</li><li>Files：下載 PDF、匯入 PDF / CAD、BCF、匯出</li><li>+ Task：將呢張圖放落一個 task</li><li>View：分割、比較兩個版本、同步、圖則之間嘅連結</li><li>復原 / 重做</li><li>縮放：100% 即係張圖啱啱夠闊；旋轉、縮小 / 放大、Fit</li><li>圖則，連 issue 同 comment - 撳一個打開</li><li>全部 / Issues / Comments</li><li>顯示或隱藏圖上嘅 mark-up</li><li>隱藏已關閉嘅 issue</li><li>按圖則、狀態、人 ... 分組</li><li>搜尋 issue 同 comment</li><li>按類型同狀態篩選；排序</li><li>一個 issue：編號、標題、邊個、幾時、狀態 - 撳一下打開</li><li>複製呢張圖嘅連結</li></ol></figure><p>Sheets 版顯示每張 publish 咗嘅 sheet，係真正嘅 PDF，搜尋得到，即刻可以 markup；markup 自己會儲存，冇 Save 掣。</p>"},{"id":"s23","ch":"Sheets：2D 圖則","h":"搵 sheet","lv":3,"html":"<ul><li>左邊嘅 <b>Sheets</b> 清單顯示 sheet 編號同名。「x/y mapped」即係張 sheet 上面有幾多個 view 連咗去 3D model。</li><li>撳一張 sheet 就打開。Viewer 會記住你上次打開嘅 sheet。</li><li><b>Search all sheets</b> 搵 sheet 編號、名，同埋圖上面印住嘅任何字（房名、note、grid 編號）。搵到嘅會喺 sheet 上面 highlight。一個 project 第一次搜尋可能要等一陣，因為要讀晒啲圖。</li><li><b>Page Down / Page Up</b> 去下一張或者上一張 sheet。</li><li>要加外面嘅 PDF（顧問嘅圖、草圖），用 <b>PDF</b> upload 掣，再改個 <b>set</b> 名（例如「Uploaded PDFs」或者「Consultant 2026-10」）。每個 set 喺 sheet 清單頂部嘅 <b>Set:</b> 入面自己一項，同「Revit sheets」分開。佢啲 sheet 會顯示「Imported 2D only」，撳 <b>✕</b> 就可以移除。</li><li><b>分組同隱藏 sheet：</b> sheet 清單可以分<b>組</b>（主題 - 平面、立面、剖面 ...）：Sheets 標題嘅 ☰ &gt; <b>New group</b>，再 ☰ &gt; <b>Move / hide sheets</b>：剔選 sheet，用清單頂嗰條一直固定喺頂嘅工具列嘅 <b>Move to ▾</b> 或者 <b>Hide</b>（或者右撳任何一張已剔嘅 sheet - 所有已剔嘅都會一齊搬）。每次搬完，揀選會清除，可以再揀下一批；撳 <b>Esc</b> 或者 <b>Done</b> 完成- project 成員整嘅組大家都見到。撳組嘅標題可以收埋；佢嘅 ⋯ 有 <b>Show only this group</b> 同 <b>Show all groups</b>（收埋邊組只係你自己嘅設定）。<b>Admin</b> 可以喺 viewer <b>隱藏</b> sheet：右撳 &gt; <b>Hide ... from the viewer</b>（或者揀幾張 &gt; <b>Hide</b>）。隱藏咗嘅 sheet 下次由 Revit 發佈之後都仍然隱藏；admin 仍然見到（淡色），喺 <b>Hidden from the viewer</b> 入面，可以再顯示。想永久唔要某啲 sheet，就喺 Revit 發佈時只揀要嘅 sheet，並剔走 <b>Keep sheets published before</b>。</li><li><b>排 sheet 次序：</b> 拖一張 sheet（或者已剔嘅幾張）去另一張上面 - 會放喺佢前面或者後面，入埋嗰張 sheet 嘅組；放喺組嘅標題上就會放到嗰組最尾。或者右撳 sheet &gt; <b>Move up</b> / <b>Move down</b>。每組有自己嘅次序，未分組嘅 sheet 亦一樣，所有人都睇到同一個次序。<b>Hidden 就係回收筒</b>（管理員）：右撳隱藏咗嘅 sheet &gt; <b>Delete from the server ...</b>，或者 Hidden 標題嘅 ⋯ &gt; <b>Delete all ...</b> - sheet 同佢嘅 PDF 會永久刪除，下次由 Revit 發佈都唔會返嚟；佢嘅標記同 issue 會保留。</li><li>將 sheet 搬入群組或者隱藏，會即刻顯示，之後喺背後儲存 - 唔使再讀成個 sheet 清單，所以就算大型項目都可以好快整理，唔會拖慢其他人用伺服器。如果改動儲存唔到，狀態列會講明，清單會按伺服器上嘅樣子再顯示。</li><li>匯入 PDF 會開一個視窗：<b>sheet 編號</b>（多頁 PDF 就係前綴）、<b>set</b>，同 <b>Keep the PDF in Folders</b> - 預設放喺 <b>00 BIM &gt; Import &gt; PDF &gt;（set 名）</b>；<b>Change folder ...</b> 揀第二個 project 或者 folder（或者 <b>+ New folder</b>）；<b>Don't keep a copy</b> 唔留。每個 project 會記住你嘅選擇。Model 要喺一個 Folders project 入面（Projects 頁）先得。</li><li><b>Set ▾</b>（sheet 清單旁邊，揀咗一個匯入 PDF 嘅 set 時）：<b>Select sheets</b> - 剔幾張（shift-click 揀一連串）一次過 <b>Delete</b>；<b>Rename set</b> 改名；<b>Archive set</b> 封存 - 喺 Sheets 頁同 Folders 收埋，乜都唔會刪，<b>Set ▾ &gt; Archived sets &gt; Bring back</b> 攞返出嚟；<b>Delete set</b> 刪除 - 連佢啲 sheet 同 PDF；會開一個視窗列出呢個 set <b>放咗喺 Folders 嘅檔案</b>，問你：<b>Delete the set, keep the files</b>（留低啲檔）或者 <b>Delete the set and its files</b>（一齊刪，會放入 Folders 嘅回收筒，可以還原）。刪咗嘅 sheet 上面嘅 markup 同 issue 會留喺 project。選單入面嘅動作係掣，<b>Delete set</b> 係紅色嗰個。</li><li>每個瀏覽器分頁會記住自己嘅 project（網址入面見到），所以可以兩個 project 並排開，每個 issue 都會存入自己嗰個 project。</li><li>張圖啱啱夠闊（<b>Fit</b>）嗰陣縮放顯示 <b>100%</b>；200% 即係大一倍。仲未有 markup 或者 issue 嘅時候，issue 清單會收埋喺邊（撳邊上個 tab 就返嚟，之後會保持打開）。 底部灰色嗰條會先寫<b>你睇緊邊個版本</b>：<i>Output 21 Oct 2026, 14:05 · Rev C (15/10/2026)</i> - 張 sheet 由 Revit 輸出嘅時間同佢而家嘅 revision - 上載嘅 PDF 就係 <i>Uploaded ... by ...</i>（之前發佈嘅 sheet 會顯示 <i>Published ...</i>，即係發佈嘅時間）。</li><li><b>檔案由邊度嚟：</b> <b>Files &gt; A PDF drawing</b> 或者 <b>A CAD drawing</b> 會先問：<b>Files on this PC ...</b>（平時嘅揀檔視窗）、CAD 仲有 <b>A folder on this PC ...</b>，或者 <b>From Folders ...</b> - 揀 project Folders 入面已經有嘅檔（例如 01 Incoming）：行到嗰個 folder 剔一個或者幾個。由 Folders 攞嘅檔會留喺原位（唔會再存多份）。</li><li><b>CAD 圖則：</b> <b>Files &gt; A CAD drawing (DWG / DXF)</b> - 揀圖則，或者成個 folder（或者一個 .zip）。剔要變做 sheet 嘅圖則（叫 Xref 之類嘅 folder 入面嘅檔唔會剔）；改 set 名；揀黑色線（好似出圖咁）或者圖則本身嘅顏色；同 CAD 檔放喺 Folders 邊度（預設 <b>00 BIM &gt; Import &gt; CAD &gt;（set 名）</b>，或者 <b>Change folder ...</b>，或者 <b>Don't keep a copy</b>）。<b>每個 layout 變一張 sheet</b>：圖框、圖標，同每個 viewport 按比例顯示嘅 model，連 xref，喺嗰個 viewport freeze 咗嘅 layer 唔會出。Sheet 編號用 layout 名（A-101 ...）。<b>Xref 會自己搵：</b> 系統會先讀圖則，佢用到嘅每個 xref（連 xref 自己嘅 xref）會喺你喺電腦揀咗嘅檔或者 folder 入面搵 - 只送需要嗰啲 - 搵唔到就喺 project <b>Folders</b> 任何位置搵（用最新嗰份）。仲係搵唔到先會問你：<b>Choose files ...</b>、<b>Choose a folder ...</b> 或者 <b>Make the sheets without them</b>（之後會列出邊啲搵唔到）。唔使 bind xref。好長嘅檔名、有 &amp; 或者括號嘅檔名都得。字體用標準字體，複雜線型用普通虛線；3D view、圖片同 OLE 唔會畫 - 要完全一樣，就喺 AutoCAD 出 PDF 再 import。DWG 要 server 裝咗 <b>ODA File Converter</b>（server 管理員裝一次）；DXF 唔使。</li></ul>"},{"id":"s24","ch":"Sheets：2D 圖則","h":"喺 sheet 上面移動","lv":3,"html":"<table><tr><th>動作</th><th>滑鼠</th><th>iPad / 觸控</th></tr><tr><td>Zoom</td><td>碌滑鼠轆（圍住游標 zoom）</td><td>兩隻手指捏</td></tr><tr><td>Pan</td><td>㩒住中間掣，或者用 <b>Pan</b> 工具（H）</td><td>兩隻手指；用過 Apple Pencil 之後，一隻手指就 pan</td></tr><tr><td>成張 sheet</td><td><b>Fit</b></td><td><b>Fit</b></td></tr><tr><td>轉張紙</td><td>工具列嘅 Rotate 掣</td><td>一樣</td></tr><tr><td>選單</td><td>撳右鍵</td><td>㩒住</td></tr><tr><td>Undo / redo</td><td>Ctrl+Z / Ctrl+Y</td><td>兩隻手指 tap / 三隻手指 tap</td></tr></table>"},{"id":"s25","ch":"Sheets：2D 圖則","h":"Sheet 有用嘅工具","lv":3,"html":"<figure class=\"shot\"><img src=\"help-img/sheet-view-menu.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><ol><li>View：下面嘅選單</li><li>Split：喺旁邊開第二張圖</li><li>Compare：同較早版本比較 - 紅色係刪咗，綠色係加咗</li><li>2D + 3D：model 喺圖則旁邊，一齊郁</li><li>Links：剖面符號同索引會打開相關嘅圖</li></ol></figure><p><b>Split</b>、<b>Compare</b>、<b>2D + 3D</b> 同 <b>Links</b> 喺 sheet 工具列嘅 <b>View ▾</b> 入面（View 上面有粒點即係 Split、Compare 或者 2D + 3D 開緊）。Markup 屬性列（layer、線、填色、文字、字型）只會喺揀咗畫圖工具或者揀咗 markup 嗰陣出現，<b>1:</b> 比例只會喺 Measure、Dimension、Area 同 Angle 出現 - 其餘時間將位留俾張圖。<b>👁 Markups</b> 同 <b>Hide closed</b> 喺右邊 issue 清單頂部，同 3D 版一樣。</p><ul><li><b>Split</b> 喺隔籬打開第二張 sheet，有自己嘅 zoom。</li><li><b>Links</b> 將 section 標記、callout 同 elevation 標記變成連去佢哋 sheet 嘅連結；<b>← back</b> 返去。</li><li><b>Compare</b> 顯示同一張 sheet 之前 upload 嘅版本、另一張 sheet，或者你電腦入面一個 PDF 有乜唔同：紅色 = 刪咗，綠色 = 加咗。<b>N / Shift+N</b> 喺改動之間跳。</li><li><b>2D + 3D</b> 喺 sheet 隔籬打開 3D model。揀 <b>Stand there</b> 或者 <b>Look at</b>，然後撳 plan：3D 視圖就會去嗰個位。Plan 上面有個「你喺度」標記跟住 3D 鏡頭；剔 <b>Follow</b> 就會一直睇住佢，你喺唔同樓層之間行嘅時候會自動轉 plan。只有 plan view 有用，section 同 elevation 唔得。</li></ul><figure class=\"shot\"><img src=\"help-img/sheet-split.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><ol><li>View &gt; Split</li><li>你打開嘅圖則</li><li>第二張圖：揀 project 入面任何一張</li><li>獨立縮放第二張圖：-、+、Fit</li><li>第二張圖</li><li>關閉分割</li></ol></figure><figure class=\"shot\"><img src=\"help-img/sheet-compare.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><ol><li>比較對象：呢張圖較早上載嘅版本、另一張圖，或者一個 PDF</li><li>顯示改動、較早版本或者現時版本</li><li>紅色：刪咗；綠色：加咗；灰色：冇改</li><li>逐個改動位置睇</li><li>Outline：每個改動位置加框</li><li>同邊個版本比較</li><li>張圖，按改動上色</li><li>關閉 Compare</li></ol></figure><figure class=\"shot\"><img src=\"help-img/sheet-2d3d.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><ol><li>You：你企喺邊、望緊邊個方向</li><li>Stand there：撳平面圖就企去嗰點</li><li>Look at：撳平面圖就轉身望去嗰點</li><li>喺 model 入面行</li><li>Follow：你郁嘅時候平面圖跟住你</li><li>Issue：喺 3D 某一點開 issue</li><li>Issues：顯示 issue 釘；Depth：深度陰影</li><li>而家模式嘅說明（行：W A S D，拖動嚟望）</li><li>打開完整 3D 頁；關閉</li><li>Models：顯示邊啲 model</li><li>Model，同平面圖同步</li><li>Walking：撳 Stop 停止行</li></ol></figure>"},{"id":"s26","ch":"Sheets：2D 圖則","h":"Markup 工具","lv":3,"html":"<figure class=\"shot\"><img src=\"help-img/markup-tools.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><ol><li>揀選 (V)：揀、搬同改 mark-up</li><li>移動 (H)：拖動張圖</li><li>形狀：長方形、圓形、直線、箭咀、多段線、多邊形 - 旁邊個箭咀列出全部</li><li>雲線：最常用嚟標 issue，或者自由形</li><li>筆同螢光筆</li><li>文字、文字框、引線標註</li><li>印章：Approved、Rejected ...</li><li>量度、尺寸線、面積、角度 - 按圖則比例</li><li>截圖、揀選文字、擦膠、複製格式</li><li>快捷鍵：每個工具一個鍵</li></ol></figure><table><tr><th>類別</th><th>工具</th></tr><tr><td>形狀</td><td>Rect、Circle、Line、Arrow、Cloud、Polyline、Polygon</td></tr><tr><td>手寫</td><td>Pen（一筆畫完之後停定唔郁，就會變成直線、圓或者長方形）、Highlighter</td></tr><tr><td>文字</td><td>Text、Text box、Callout</td></tr><tr><td>印章</td><td>APPROVED、APPROVED AS NOTED、REVISE &amp; RESUBMIT、REJECTED、REVIEWED、FOR INFORMATION、VOID（會簽上你個名同時間）</td></tr><tr><td>量度</td><td>Measure、Dimension、Area、Angle（用 <b>1:</b> 格入面嘅比例；空白就用 view 自己嘅比例）</td></tr><tr><td>其他</td><td>Snip（將一個範圍 copy 做圖片；亦可以貼圖入嚟）、Select text、Eraser、Match properties、Select、Pan</td></tr></table><ul><li><b>Polyline / Polygon：</b> 撳啲點，然後按 Enter、double-click 或者 <b>✓ Finish</b>。Backspace 刪最後一點。</li><li><b>Style bar：</b> Layer、線／填色／文字顏色、Opacity、Weight（紙上 mm）、線 Type、Font、Size（字高 mm）、Align。</li><li><b>改 markup：</b> 揀一個 markup 就可以搬、改大細或者改樣式；R / Shift+R 轉 90°；Ctrl+C / Ctrl+V copy 同貼（貼去另一張 sheet 會喺同一個位置）；Delete 刪除。</li><li><b>Comment 定 Issue：</b> 圖則工具列嘅 <b>Comment / + Issue</b> 掣決定畫完 markup 之後做乜。喺 <b>Issue</b> 模式會即刻彈出 <b>Raise issue</b> 視窗。Comment 之後都可以用 <b>Issue</b> 或者右鍵 <b>Raise issue</b> 變做 issue。</li><li><b>Layer：</b> markup 放喺 layer 上面（預設「General」）。Admin 可以鎖 layer 或者唔俾某啲人睇到。issue 清單頂部嘅 <b>👁 Markups</b> 會隱藏所有 markup。</li></ul>"},{"id":"s27","ch":"Sheets：2D 圖則","h":"Export","lv":3,"html":"<ul><li><b>PDF</b>（download）export 呢張 sheet、所有有 markup 嘅 sheet，或者全部 sheet；markup 可以係 <b>Editable</b>（Bluebeam、Acrobat 或 PDF-XChange 用嘅真 PDF comment）或者 <b>Flattened</b>，100、150 或 200 dpi，可以喺最尾加 issue 報告。</li><li><b>JSON</b>（download / upload）儲存或者載入所有 comment 同 issue，用嚟 backup 或者搬去另一個 project。</li><li><b>BCF</b> export sheet 嘅 issue 俾 Revit 或 Navisworks（睇「Issue 同 BCF」）。</li></ul>"},{"id":"s28","ch":"3D：四圍睇","h":"3D：四圍睇","lv":2,"html":"<figure class=\"shot\"><img src=\"help-img/model.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><ol><li>樓層：喺某層切開 model，當平面睇</li><li>透視或者平行投影</li><li>Issue 釘：顯示或隱藏 model 上嘅 issue</li><li>平面疊圖：將圖則疊喺 model 上</li><li>更多：複製視圖連結、BCF、設定正面 / 世界座標、+ Task</li><li>轉動：轉、移、縮放 model</li><li>以眼睛高度行入去睇</li><li>Fit：成個 model</li><li>開關剖切盒</li><li>量度（會鎖點）</li><li>+ Add issue：撳 model 放一個</li><li>Project 嘅 model - 剔選顯示</li><li>構件：顯示或隱藏每個類別</li><li>視圖方塊：撳一面；Home 返總覽</li><li>Selection：撳中構件嘅屬性（未揀之前得一行）</li><li>3D 入面嘅 issue：清單同篩選</li></ol></figure><p>3D 版嘅滑鼠用法同大部分 BIM viewer 一樣：右掣轉、中間掣 pan、轆 zoom、左掣揀。</p>"},{"id":"s29","ch":"3D：四圍睇","h":"滑鼠、觸控同鍵盤","lv":3,"html":"<table><tr><th>動作</th><th>滑鼠</th><th>iPad / iPhone</th></tr><tr><td>Orbit（轉）</td><td>㩒住右掣拖</td><td>一隻手指</td></tr><tr><td>Pan</td><td>㩒住中間掣（轆）拖</td><td>兩隻手指</td></tr><tr><td>Zoom</td><td>碌滑鼠轆（向住游標）</td><td>兩隻手指捏</td></tr><tr><td>對準一個面</td><td>Double-click 佢</td><td>Double tap</td></tr><tr><td>揀一個元件</td><td>左掣撳</td><td>Tap</td></tr><tr><td>設定轉嘅中心</td><td>右鍵撳唔好拖，或者右鍵選單 <b>Set orbit centre here</b></td><td>-</td></tr><tr><td>動作選單</td><td>撳右鍵</td><td>-</td></tr><tr><td>喺一個位開新 issue</td><td><b>Add issue</b>，然後撳</td><td>㩒住（0.6 秒）</td></tr><tr><td>上一層／下一層</td><td>Page Up / Page Down</td><td>Floor plan 清單</td></tr><tr><td>取消量度或者行</td><td>Esc</td><td>Stop 掣</td></tr></table><p>用滑鼠嘅話，你一放手畫面就停喺嗰度；用手指會滑多少少，同其他平板 app 一樣。</p>"},{"id":"s30","ch":"3D：四圍睇","h":"右鍵選單","lv":3,"html":"<p>喺元件上面：<b>Set orbit centre here</b>、<b>Zoom to this element</b>、<b>Isolate</b>、<b>Hide</b>、<b>Show all</b>、<b>Walk from here</b>、<b>Add issue here</b>、<b>Section box around this element</b>、<b>See-through</b>（呢個元件、佢個 type 或者成個 category）、<b>Make all solid again</b>、<b>Section on this face</b>、<b>Square section box to this face</b>、<b>Turn section on/off</b>、<b>Measure</b>、<b>Save view...</b>、<b>Fit model</b>。喺空位：Show all、Turn section on/off、Measure、Save view...、Fit model。</p>"},{"id":"s31","ch":"3D：四圍睇","h":"View cube 同鏡頭","lv":3,"html":"<ul><li>撳 cube 嘅一個<b>面</b>睇嗰個方向，撳一條<b>邊</b>睇兩個面之間，撳一個<b>角</b>睇 isometric。拖個 cube 可以轉。下面個圈顯示北面。</li><li>屋仔掣返去 3D 全景。Cube 下面有 <b>Walk</b>（睇「喺 model 入面行」）同 <b>Fit</b>，將所有載入咗嘅 model 放晒入畫面 - 開咗 section box 就只係放 box 入面嘅嘢。</li><li><b>Perspective / Parallel</b> 轉投影方式（plan 永遠係 parallel）。</li><li><b>Set front：</b> 撳一幅牆話俾 cube 知呢棟樓邊面係「Front」；<b>World</b> 返去世界軸。</li></ul>"},{"id":"s32","ch":"3D：四圍睇","h":"樓層","lv":3,"html":"<ul><li><b>Floor plan</b> 下拉選單（喺 3D 頁頂，同 <b>Navigate / Add issue / Measure</b>、<b>Plan overlay</b>、視圖連結同 <b>BCF</b> 一齊 - 闊嘅視窗全部排一行，窄啲就排喺第二行）列出 <b>Whole building</b> 同由上至下每一層。<b>Search</b>、鈴同 <b>+ Task</b> 喺右上角，同其他頁一樣。</li><li>揀一層就會由嗰層樓面以下 0.5 m 切到以上 1.2 m，再由上面直望落去，好似 Revit 嘅 plan 咁。</li><li><b>Page Up / Page Down</b> 上落一層；<b>Whole building</b> 返去成個 3D model。</li><li><b>Plan overlay</b>（樓層清單旁邊）將嗰層嘅 plan sheet 鋪喺 model 上面，等你對比圖同 model。</li></ul><figure class=\"shot\"><img src=\"help-img/model-floorplan.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><ol><li>Floor plan：喺某一層切開 model</li><li>Plan overlay：將嗰層嘅圖則疊喺切面上</li><li>用邊張圖</li><li>疊喺切面上嘅圖，連註釋同尺寸</li><li>而家顯示緊邊張圖</li></ol></figure>"},{"id":"s33","ch":"3D：四圍睇","h":"Models panel","lv":3,"html":"<ul><li>每個 model（主 model 同每個 link）一個剔格。唔剔就會隱藏個 model，慳返記憶體；<b>All on / All off</b> 一齊開關，視圖唔會變。</li><li>Model 隔籬嘅 <b>▸</b> 顯示佢嘅大細同副本數目，仲有 <b>Compare with previous export</b>，睇上次 publish 之後加咗、改咗或者刪咗乜。</li><li><b>Apply link transforms</b>（開咗）會將 link 放喺 Revit 入面嘅位置。</li><li><b>Light mode (phones, tablets)</b> 只會喺你望緊嘅附近載入重複嘅標準層。手機同平板預設開咗。</li><li><b>分階段載入：</b> 主 model 一載入完就顯示，你即刻可以開工；其他 model 喺後面繼續載入，近你視角嘅先載（「Main model ready - N more model(s) loading behind it」）。</li><li><b>Open with the main model only</b>（喺 list 下面，呢部機會記住）：打開時只載入主 model；其他 model 要你剔佢或者行近佢先會載入。網絡慢或者電腦記憶體少嘅時候好有用。</li><li>每個 panel 嘅標題（Models、Section、Measure 等等）撳一下就收埋，下次都會保持收埋。</li></ul><p>左邊 panel 分做三組，每組一隻顏色，容易搵：</p><table><tr><th>組</th><th>顏色</th><th>部分</th></tr><tr><td><b>Model</b></td><td>藍</td><td>Models、Elements、Model browser - 載入咗乜、入面有乜</td></tr><tr><td><b>Tools</b></td><td>青綠</td><td>Section、Measure、Checks - 處理 model 嘅工具</td></tr><tr><td><b>View</b></td><td>琥珀</td><td>Display、Saved views - 點樣顯示</td></tr></table><p>喺 model 上面：<b>底部嘅工具列</b>有 <b>Orbit</b>、<b>Walk</b>、<b>Fit</b>、<b>Section box</b>、<b>Measure</b> 同 <b>+ Add issue</b>；<b>左上角嘅 chip</b> 係 <b>Floor</b>（喺某層切開 model）、<b>Perspective</b>、<b>Issue pins</b>（顯示或隱藏）、<b>Plan overlay</b> 同 <b>⋯</b>（複製視圖連結、BCF、Set front／World、+ Task）。View cube 保留 <b>Home</b>。<b>Shaded / White / X-ray</b> 同 <b>Depth</b> 喺 <b>Display</b> 頂部；<b>Hide closed</b> 喺右邊 <b>Issues in 3D</b> 頂部。未揀元件之前 Selection 只得一行。平板上兩邊 panel 由左上角個掣滑出嚟；手機就由下面升上嚟。</p>"},{"id":"s34","ch":"3D：揀、搵同顯示","h":"3D：揀、搵同顯示","lv":2,"html":"<p>撳任何元件就睇到佢係乜；用 Model browser 可以按名、type、樓層或者 property 搵元件。</p>"},{"id":"s35","ch":"3D：揀、搵同顯示","h":"Selection panel","lv":3,"html":"<p>撳一下會顯示元件嘅 <b>Model</b>、<b>Category</b>、<b>Family / type</b>、<b>Level</b>、<b>Revit id</b>（ElementId）、<b>UniqueId</b>、<b>IFC GUID</b>、撳中嘅 <b>Point</b>（x、y、z，單位米）同 <b>Shared E,N,Z</b>（測量座標），跟住係佢所有 Revit parameter，分組可以收埋。</p><ul><li><b>Copy Revit ID</b> copy ElementId；喺 Revit 用 <b>Manage &gt; Select by ID</b> 貼上，就會揀中同一個元件。<b>Show in Revit</b> 叫 LWK add-in 喺 Revit 揀佢（睇「Revit 元件」）。<b>+ Task</b> 將個元件放落一個 task。</li><li><b>Isolate</b> 只顯示揀咗嘅元件。<b>Hide</b> 隱藏佢哋。<b>Show all</b> 全部返嚟。有個數字顯示隱藏咗幾多個。</li><li>Hide 同 isolate 只會改你自己嘅視圖，乜都冇刪到。</li></ul>"},{"id":"s36","ch":"3D：揀、搵同顯示","h":"Elements panel","lv":3,"html":"<p>每個 category 一個剔格（Walls、Floors and slabs、Columns、Windows、Doors、Furniture、Railings...），有數目。唔剔一個 category 就隱藏佢；<b>Show all</b> 全部開返。你揀咗乜會記住。</p>"},{"id":"s37","ch":"3D：揀、搵同顯示","h":"Model browser","lv":3,"html":"<ul><li>一個樹狀清單：<b>model › category › family / type › 元件</b>。撳一行打開佢同揀成組；撳一個元件會 highlight 同 zoom 埋去。</li><li><b>Search names, types, levels, properties</b>：普通字會對 name、category、family、type 同 level。用 <b>property:value</b> 對一個 parameter，例如 Fire Rating:2 hr 或者 Mark:D101。</li><li><b>Select</b> 將搵到嘅上色，<b>Isolate</b> 只顯示佢哋，<b>Zoom</b> 放晒入畫面。<b>Select</b> 之後，頂部嘅 <b>+ Task</b> 會將所有揀咗嘅元件放落 task 做「Elements to change」，<b>Copy Revit ID</b> 會 copy 晒佢哋嘅 id。</li><li>Browser 用喺 fast 3D 格式 publish 嘅 model（即係正常 Publish to Viewer 出嚟嘅）。</li></ul>"},{"id":"s38","ch":"3D：揀、搵同顯示","h":"Display","lv":3,"html":"<figure class=\"shot\"><img src=\"help-img/model-display.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><ol><li>Shaded、White 或者 X-ray</li><li>Depth：深度陰影</li><li>背景顏色</li><li>地面同佢嘅顏色</li><li>格網</li><li>深度陰影：陰影同邊線，同佢哋嘅顏色</li><li>還原深度陰影</li><li>Saved views：Save 會記住鏡頭、剖面同顯示嘅嘢</li></ol></figure><table><tr><th>模式</th><th>用嚟</th></tr><tr><td><b>Shaded</b></td><td>正常睇，用 model 自己嘅顏色</td></tr><tr><td><b>White</b></td><td>乾淨、冇顏色，啱 review 同截圖</td></tr><tr><td><b>X-ray</b></td><td>透過牆同樓板睇到入面</td></tr></table><p>呢三個掣同 <b>Depth</b>（角落柔和陰影同邊線）喺 <b>Display</b> panel 頂部；呢個 panel 仲可以設定背景顏色、地面（開關同顏色）、grid 同深度陰影。</p>"},{"id":"s39","ch":"3D：揀、搵同顯示","h":"Saved views","lv":3,"html":"<ul><li><b>Save</b>（或者右鍵 <b>Save view...</b>）會連名同縮圖儲存鏡頭、section 同隱藏咗嘅元件。Saved view 成個 project 都睇到。</li><li>撳一個 saved view 返去嗰度；<b>✕</b> 刪除。</li><li>由 3D 去 Sheets 再返嚟，你上次嘅 3D 視圖會原封不動咁返嚟。</li></ul>"},{"id":"s40","ch":"Section box、section plane 同 floor plan","h":"Section box、section plane 同 floor plan","lv":2,"html":"<p>用 section box 將棟樓一部分切開，用 section plane 沿住任何一個面切；切到嘅實體會顯示橙色 hatch，好似圖則咁。</p>"},{"id":"s41","ch":"Section box、section plane 同 floor plan","h":"Section 工具","lv":3,"html":"<figure class=\"shot\"><img src=\"help-img/model-tools.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><ol><li>Box：model 嘅剖面盒 - 拖橙色箭咀</li><li>Plane：撳一個面就喺嗰度切</li><li>Align、Flip、Reset 切面</li><li>切面實心填色；平面圖用平面樣式</li><li>量度：距離、角度、面積</li><li>Straight：只沿 X、Y 或 Z 量</li><li>Undo、Clear；Keep 將量度留低做尺寸</li><li>顯示留低嘅尺寸</li><li>檢查：Clash、Headroom、SBD</li><li>要行嘅 clash 規則</li><li>+ 新規則；✎ 修改；✕ 刪除</li><li>範圍：成個 model、某幾層，或者剖面盒入面</li><li>執行</li></ol></figure><table><tr><th>掣</th><th>做乜</th></tr><tr><td><b>Box</b>（剔）</td><td>開 section box，圍住成個 project</td></tr><tr><td><b>Plane</b></td><td>撳一個面：model 就喺嗰個面切開</td></tr><tr><td><b>Align</b></td><td>撳一幅牆：個 box 會轉到同嗰幅牆對正</td></tr><tr><td><b>Flip</b></td><td>留 section plane 另一邊</td></tr><tr><td><b>Reset</b></td><td>移除所有切面</td></tr><tr><td><b>Solid fill on the cut</b></td><td>切到嘅牆、樓板同柱會顯示橙色 hatch（預設開）</td></tr><tr><td><b>Plan look for floor plans</b></td><td>喺 floor plan 入面，表面淡啲，下面嘅樓層會淡出（預設開）</td></tr></table><p>Floor plan 下拉選單（睇「3D：四圍睇」）就係一層樓現成嘅 section box。</p>"},{"id":"s42","ch":"Section box、section plane 同 floor plan","h":"移動切面","lv":3,"html":"<ul><li>Box 每個面都有一粒<b>有短柄嘅彩色點</b>：紅色 X、綠色 Y、藍色高度。單一 section plane 係橙色點。</li><li><b>滑鼠：</b> 移到一粒點上面，或者切面嘅邊（個面會變橙色），然後拖。切面只會沿住自己嘅方向郁。</li><li><b>iPad / iPhone：</b> 一隻手指拖粒點。兩隻手指永遠係郁視圖、唔會郁切面，所以開住 section 都可以隨便捏同轉。</li><li>喺電腦上面，切面停定之後會有啡色線描出切口嘅邊。手機同平板只顯示 hatch。</li></ul>"},{"id":"s43","ch":"Section box、section plane 同 floor plan","h":"方便嘅快捷","lv":3,"html":"<ul><li>右鍵撳一幅牆或者樓板：<b>Section on this face</b> 就喺嗰度切；<b>Square section box to this face</b> 將個 box 對正佢。</li><li>右鍵撳空位：<b>Turn section on/off</b>。</li><li><b>Section box 圍住一個元件：</b> 撳佢，再撳 Selection panel 嘅 <b>Section box</b>；或者右鍵 &gt; <b>Section box around this element</b>。個 box 會圍住嗰個元件、四邊留少少位，視圖會飛過去。喺 <b>Model browser</b> 揀一組（category、type、樓層）再撳 <b>Section box</b>，就圍住成組。</li></ul>"},{"id":"s44","ch":"Section box、section plane 同 floor plan","h":"半透明（See-through）元件","lv":3,"html":"<p>想睇穿牆、樓板或者天花又唔想收埋佢哋，就將佢哋變半透明：佢哋留喺原位、好似一塊淡色網，撳落去會穿過去揀後面嘅嘢。</p><ul><li><b>一個元件：</b> 撳佢，再撳 Selection panel 嘅 <b>See-through</b>；或者右鍵 &gt; <b>See-through: this element</b>。</li><li><b>佢個 type 或者成個 category：</b> 右鍵 &gt; <b>See-through: its type (n)</b> 或者 <b>See-through: all Walls (n)</b>（即係佢個 category 名）。</li><li><b>自己揀一組：</b> 喺 <b>Model browser</b> 搜尋或者揀 category、type、樓層，再撳 <b>See-through</b>。</li><li>Selection panel 會數住有幾多個（<b>5 see-through</b>）。撳 <b>Show all</b>，或者右鍵 &gt; <b>Make all solid again</b>，就變返實心。</li></ul>"},{"id":"s45","ch":"喺 3D 量度","h":"喺 3D 量度","lv":2,"html":"<p>每個量度點都會 snap 去真實嘅角、邊或者中點，個 label 會話你知係邊種，你就知個數信唔信得過。</p>"},{"id":"s46","ch":"喺 3D 量度","h":"點樣量","lv":3,"html":"<ol><li>撳底部工具列嘅 <b>Measure</b>（或者右鍵 <b>Measure</b>），揀 <b>Distance</b>、<b>Angle</b> 或者 <b>Area</b>。</li><li>將游標移過 model。彩色點同 label 會顯示下面 snap 到乜。</li><li>撳第一點，再撳下一點。距離會跟住你郁即時更新，仲有佢嘅 <b>plan</b> 同 <b>height</b> 部分。</li><li>按 <b>Esc</b> 放棄一個唔小心開始咗嘅量度。</li></ol><table><tr><th>模式</th><th>點數</th><th>結果</th></tr><tr><td><b>Distance</b></td><td>2</td><td>長度（1 m 以下用 mm，否則用 m），仲有 plan 同 height 部分</td></tr><tr><td><b>Angle</b></td><td>3</td><td>中間嗰點嘅角度</td></tr><tr><td><b>Area</b></td><td>3 至 64</td><td>多邊形面積（m²）</td></tr></table>"},{"id":"s47","ch":"喺 3D 量度","h":"Snap","lv":3,"html":"<table><tr><th>顏色</th><th>Snap</th><th>意思</th></tr><tr><td>紅色</td><td>corner</td><td>元件嘅一個頂點，或者 section 入面切口嘅角</td></tr><tr><td>紫色</td><td>midpoint</td><td>一條邊嘅中間</td></tr><tr><td>綠色</td><td>perpendicular</td><td>由你上一點到一條邊嘅垂直線落腳點</td></tr><tr><td>藍色</td><td>edge</td><td>一條邊上面任何一點</td></tr><tr><td>灰色</td><td>surface</td><td>附近冇特徵：面上面嘅點（冇咁準）</td></tr></table><ul><li>每次 snap 到新嘢都會有個圈散開（手機會震），等你知捉到咗。</li><li>喺 floor plan 或者 section 入面，snap 會跟住切口輪廓，所以喺 plan 可以量牆到牆。</li><li>曲面係由好多細平面組成，所以暫時未有切線或者弧心 snap。</li></ul>"},{"id":"s48","ch":"喺 3D 量度","h":"Straight 同其他掣","lv":3,"html":"<ul><li><b>Straight</b> 令下一點同上一點沿 X、Y 或者高度成一直線，量真正正交嘅距離。㩒住 <b>Shift</b> 就只係下一點轉換。</li><li><b>Undo</b> 刪最後一點，<b>Clear</b> 刪晒所有量度。</li><li><b>Keep</b> 將量好嘅距離儲存做 dimension，project 所有人都睇到。<b>Dimensions</b> 剔格顯示或者隱藏 keep 咗嘅 dimension，每個都可以撳 <b>✕</b> 刪除。</li></ul>"},{"id":"s49","ch":"碰撞同淨高檢查","h":"碰撞同淨高檢查","lv":2,"html":"<p>3D 版左邊 panel 嘅 <b>Checks</b> 會搵出撞埋一齊嘅元件，同埋淨高唔夠嘅地方 - 喺 project 自己嘅 model 入面，亦可以同一齊 load 咗嘅顧問 model 比。佢檢查嘅係 viewer 畫出嚟嘅嘢（Revit medium detail、IFC 轉換後嘅樣）：用嚟日常快速協調，唔係正式嘅 clash report。</p>"},{"id":"s50","ch":"碰撞同淨高檢查","h":"碰撞（Clash）：一條規則，然後 Run","lv":3,"html":"<figure class=\"shot\"><img src=\"help-img/clash-rule.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><ol><li>規則名稱</li><li>Set A：一邊嘅 model 同類別</li><li>Set B：同 A 比較嘅（A 同 B 可以係同一個 model）</li><li>已儲存嘅 model 同類別組合；Save as set</li><li>Model：我哋同顧問嘅</li><li>類別（All / None）</li><li>名稱包含 / 唔包含：只揀部分構件</li><li>幾多重疊先計；A 周圍嘅淨空距離</li><li>唔計門窗喺佢哋嘅牆入面</li><li>唔計 Revit 自動清理嘅接駁位</li><li>開放面互相交叉</li><li>儲存規則（同成個 project 共用）</li></ol></figure><ol><li>喺 Models panel load 你要嘅 model（顧問嘅 IFC、疊加另一個 project）。</li><li>Checks &gt; <b>Clash</b> &gt; <b>+</b>。俾條規則一個名，揀 <b>Set A</b> 同 <b>Set B</b>：每邊剔一個或者多個 model（或者 <b>All models</b>，之後先 load 嘅 link 都會計埋）同要檢查嘅類別 - 例如建築 model 嘅 <i>Ceilings</i> 對結構 model 嘅 <i>Beams</i>，或者所有建築 link 嘅 <i>Walls</i> 對所有機電 link 嘅 <i>Ducts</i> 同 <i>Pipes</i>。A 同 B 可以係同一啲 model：即係檢查佢哋自己入面嘅碰撞。model 上面嘅 <b>All</b> / <b>None</b> 一次過剔晒或者唔剔晒。<b>Name has</b> / <b>Name has not</b> 只保留名、type 或者 family 有（或者冇）呢啲字嘅元件 - 例如 <i>Name has not: Finish</i>（幾個字之間用逗號：任何一個都算）。</li><li><b>Selection sets</b>（好似 Navisworks）：<b>Save as set</b> 將一邊嘅 model、類別同名稱篩選用一個名儲存，project 所有人共用。任何規則都可以喺嗰邊頂部嘅列表揀返。跟住 set 嘅規則會用 set 而家嘅樣，所以改 set（揀佢、改剔、用同一個名再 <b>Save as set</b>）就會改晒所有用佢嘅規則。<b>Delete set</b> 刪除；用過佢嘅規則會保留佢嘅揀選。</li><li><b>Overlap that counts</b>（預設 10 mm）：重疊少過呢個數只算掂到，唔算撞。<b>Clearance</b>：未掂到但近過呢個距離都報（0 = 唔檢查）。</li><li>揀範圍：<b>Whole model</b>、<b>Floors</b>（由某一層到某一層），或者 <b>Inside the section box</b>（大 model 快啲），然後撳 <b>Run</b>。如果太多元件掂住（多過 30,000 對），panel 會講有幾多對、大約要幾耐，俾你揀 <b>Check them all</b>（有進度條；<b>Stop</b> 會保留已經搵到嘅）或者 <b>Choose floors instead</b>。</li></ol><p>規則底部三個選項：</p><table><tr><th>選項</th><th>作用</th></tr><tr><td><b>Leave out doors and windows in their walls, floors and roofs</b></td><td>門窗一定喺佢所在嘅牆入面；唔剔嘅話，每一度門窗都會同自己幅牆報一次。</td></tr><tr><td><b>Leave out joins between walls, floors, roofs, columns, beams and stairs</b></td><td>呢啲元件交接嘅位（牆企喺樓板上、面層喺牆底、平台入咗牆）Revit 會整乾淨，但匯出時每個元件都係完整嘅，所以會重疊。剔咗：只有一個大部分喺另一個入面（重複、埋咗喺入面）先算。機電、傢俬同天花唔受影響。唔剔：每個交接都會列出 - 通常幾百個。</td></tr><tr><td><b>Report open surfaces crossing each other</b></td><td>有啲元件只係面，唔係封閉實體（某啲 IFC 匯出、冇封口嘅喉管）；佢哋冇「入面」，計唔到穿過幾深。唔剔：面只係插入實體先算。剔咗：兩個面單純交叉都會報 - 更齊，但更多雜音。</td></tr></table><p>規則係共用嘅：project 入面所有人都喺規則列表見到、可以 run、可以改，亦見到上次嘅結果（只可以睇嘅人可以 run，但結果唔會儲存）。顧問 model 係用佢個名同公司認，所以佢哋送嚟下一版之後條規則照用得。</p><table><tr><th>顯示</th><th>意思</th></tr><tr><td><b>Overlap 120 mm</b></td><td>兩個實體重疊；個數係最薄嗰個方向重疊幾深</td></tr><tr><td><b>Inside</b></td><td>一個元件成個埋咗喺另一個入面（例如喉管喺牆入面）</td></tr><tr><td><b>Too close 30 mm apart</b></td><td>冇掂到，但近過 clearance</td></tr><tr><td><b>Crossing</b></td><td>兩個唔係封閉實體嘅面互相穿過（計唔到深度）- 只係條規則剔咗 <b>Report open surfaces crossing each other</b> 先會報</td></tr></table><ul><li>唔會報：牆頂牆、牆企喺樓板上、多層嘅牆同樓板掂住（相差一兩毫米都當掂住），同埋（預設剔咗）喺牆、樓板、屋頂入面嘅門窗。唔封閉嘅面對住實體，會量佢插入幾深。</li><li><b>Leave out joins</b>（預設剔咗）：匯出嘅 model 入面，牆、樓板、屋頂、柱、樑同樓梯喺交接位會重疊 - 牆穿過樓板、地台面層或者防水層喺牆底、平台入咗牆、樑入牆或者入柱。呢啲唔會報。重複嘅元件、兩幅牆並排重疊，或者任何嘢穿過天花，就照報。</li><li>列表顯示上面揀咗嘅範圍入面嘅碰撞：成個 model、揀咗嘅樓層，或者 section box 入面，連埋上次喺嗰度檢查嘅時間（未檢查過會寫「Not checked on L2 yet」）。之前喺其他地方搵到嘅碰撞會保留：「<i>N</i> more elsewhere」- 撳 <b>Show</b> 一齊列出。</li><li>列表上面嘅 <b>Hide under ... mm</b> 唔使再 run 就可以收埋淺過呢個數嘅重疊（每條規則喺呢部電腦記住）；<b>Deepest first</b> 按深度排。</li><li>擺埋一齊又共用同一個元件嘅碰撞會歸做一組（「5 clashes around Beam 12」）。</li><li>撳一個碰撞：會用幾米闊嘅 section box 喺嗰度切開嗰層，兩個元件會上色（A 橙、B 藍 - 可以用列表上面 <b>A</b> 同 <b>B</b> 兩個顏色格揀自己嘅顏色，記喺呢部電腦），一粒紅點標住位置。3D 畫面左下角有個圖例講明邊個係 A、邊個係 B。如果兩個都喺同一個 Revit model 入面，會共用 A 嘅顏色（每個 model 只有一種 highlight 顏色），圖例會註明。<b>Section off</b> 放返成個 model；<b>Only these</b> 會收埋其他嘢（<b>Show all</b> 放返出嚟）。</li><li><b>Make issue</b> 會打開填好晒嘅 issue 表格：標題 <b>Clash issue 007 - Ducts x Beams (L2)</b>（project 內順序編號），描述寫明兩個元件（model、類別、名、類型、id）、碰撞種類同深度、樓層同 project 座標位置，限期係 <b>3 個工作天</b>之後（星期一至五，唔計香港公眾假期）。揀人跟進再 Save；可以用 BCF 送去 Revit 或 Navisworks。</li><li>列表上面嘅 <b>Raise issues for all <i>N</b></i> 會為每個列出、未處理、唔係 <i>Not an issue</i> 又未有 issue 嘅碰撞，逐個顯示、影相再開一個咁樣嘅 issue（<b>Stop</b> 停）。想全部交俾同一個人，先喺 <b>Assign to</b> 打個名。</li><li><b>Save view：</b> 轉好角度、較好 section box 或者收埋啲元件，令個碰撞睇得清楚，然後撳嗰個碰撞嘅 <b>Save view</b>。之後所有人打開都係呢個視圖（旁邊有 📷 <i>view</i>），佢嘅 issue（逐個開或者 Raise issues for all）都用呢個視圖，儲存咗嘅結果都會記住。<b>Clear view</b> 取消。</li><li><b>Not an issue</b> 之後每次 run 同埋儲存咗嘅結果都唔會再列呢對元件（可以喺 <b>Not an issue</b> 搵返；<b>Count again</b> 取消）。</li><li><b>Save result</b>（喺結果列表旁邊）將而家顯示嘅結果用一個名儲存，project 所有人都睇到 - 幾多份都得（例如 design freeze 前後、顧問每次交 model）。喺碰撞上面個列表揀返一份就可以再睇；<b>Latest run</b> 返去最新一次。儲存嘅人或者 project admin 可以 <b>Delete</b>。</li><li><b>顧問 IFC model：</b> 規則表格會列出 project 嘅顧問 model，就算頁面未載入都會列（<i>consultant IFC - not loaded</i>），剔咗就會載入。<b>All consultant models</b> 揀晒全部顧問 model，<b>All LWK BIM models</b> 揀晒我哋自己嘅 model；<b>Our models x consultant models</b> 一撳就填好「我哋嘅 model 對全部顧問 model、所有類別」嘅規則。Run 嗰陣，規則用到但未載入嘅顧問 model 會先載入。</li><li><b>Export the list</b>：<b>Spreadsheet</b> 將列出嘅碰撞儲存做 CSV 檔俾 Excel 用（狀態、種類、深度、樓層、兩個元件同佢哋嘅 id、project 座標位置、issue）。<b>Report</b> 喺新分頁開一份報告 - <b>With pictures</b> 會逐個顯示並影低每個碰撞（每個大約一秒；<b>Stop</b> 停），<b>Without</b> 即刻出 - 然後 <b>Print / Save as PDF</b>，或者 <b>Save to Folders (PDF)</b> 存入 project 嘅 Folders。如果瀏覽器擋咗個分頁，請容許呢個網站彈出視窗。</li><li>publish 咗新版或者顧問送咗新 model 之後<b>再 Run</b>：每個碰撞會標 <b>New</b>、仍然存在，或者 <b>Gone</b>。已經冇咗嘅碰撞仍然會顯示佢個 issue，方便關閉。</li></ul><figure class=\"shot\"><img src=\"help-img/clash-results.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><ol><li>由邊層到邊層</li><li>最新結果，或者已儲存嘅結果</li><li>Save result：保存呢次結果</li><li>Set A 同 B，同佢哋喺 model 嘅顏色</li><li>隱藏細過呢個數嘅 clash</li><li>清單分組：按樓層、類別 ...</li><li>未處理、上次之後新增、已消失、唔係問題</li><li>全部開 issue</li><li>匯出清單：試算表、報告</li><li>一個 clash：inside 或 overlap、深度、樓層；Make issue、Only these、Section off、Save view、Not an issue</li><li>Model 入面嘅 clash，周圍切開咗</li><li>顏色代表乜</li><li>而家顯示緊乜；Section off 顯示成個 model</li></ol></figure>"},{"id":"s51","ch":"碰撞同淨高檢查","h":"淨高（Headroom）","lv":3,"html":"<figure class=\"shot\"><img src=\"help-img/headroom.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><ol><li>檢查 &gt; Headroom</li><li>Probe：撳地台或者梯級，睇到上面嘅高度</li><li>地台上面、樓梯同斜道上面嘅最少高度</li><li>唔理低過呢個高度嘅嘢（枱、窗台）</li><li>計算嘅 model</li><li>Stood on：你企喺上面嘅嘢</li><li>Overhead：頭頂上計算嘅嘢</li><li>常用類別</li><li>範圍：成個 model、某幾層，或者剖面盒入面</li><li>掃描</li></ol></figure><ul><li><b>Probe：</b> Checks &gt; <b>Headroom</b> &gt; <b>Probe</b>，然後撳一塊樓板、一級梯級或者平台。會有條線垂直向上去到上面第一樣嘢，顯示高度 - 低過樓梯限制係紅色，低過樓面限制係橙色，夠高係綠色。<b>Keep</b> 會儲存做所有人睇到嘅尺寸。<b>Esc</b> 停。</li><li><b>Scan：</b> 設定限制（<b>Floors</b> 預設 2.30 m；<b>Stairs, ramps</b> 預設 2.00 m；<b>Ignore lower than</b> 預設 1.5 m - 矮過呢個嘅空間唔係人用嘅：坐廁或者長櫈下面、管道或者天花槽入面、樓梯伸入上一層樓板底嘅位置），揀樓層（由 ... 到 ...）或者 section box 入面，然後撳 <b>Scan</b>。樓面、樓梯、平台同斜道會以 0.25 m 網格量度（樓梯 0.2 m，窄嘅風喉、喉管同樑下面更密），量到上面嘅嘢：樓板、天花、樑、上面嘅樓梯、風喉、喉管、線槽、機電設備。</li><li><b>Models counted</b> 揀計邊啲 model - 剔埋顧問嘅機電同結構 model 就睇到佢哋嘅影響。<b>What counts</b> 列出 <b>Stood on</b>（企喺上面）同 <b>Overhead</b>（頭頂）嘅類別；傢俬、坐廁同洗手盆、櫃同 generic models 唔剔就唔算頭頂。<b>Usual categories</b> 還原預設。呢啲設定係 project 所有人共用。</li><li>低過限制嘅地方會喺地面顯示紅色方格（橙色：高過限制 100 mm 以內），每個地方都會列出最低高度、頭頂係咩同面積。<b>Look</b> 會喺嗰度切開嗰層、將頭頂嘅嘢上色，喺最矮嗰點畫出高度（<b>Keep</b> 儲存做尺寸）；<b>Make issue</b> 開 issue。<b>Clear</b> 清走啲方格。<i>under the limit</i> 旁邊個顏色格可以揀顏色（記喺呢部電腦）；3D 畫面有圖例講明頭頂係咩。</li><li><b>Export</b>：<b>Spreadsheet</b>（每個地方：樓層、企喺咩上面、最低高度、限制、面積、頭頂係咩、位置）或者 <b>Report</b>，可以連或者唔連每個地方嘅相，列印或者儲存做 PDF，或者 <b>Save to Folders (PDF)</b>。</li><li><b>Make issue</b>、<b>Raise issues for all</b>、<b>Not an issue</b> 同 <b>Save result</b> 同碰撞一樣：issue 標題係 <b>Headroom issue 001 - 2.05 m under Ducts (L1)</b>，限期 3 個工作天；標咗 <i>Not an issue</i> 嘅地方每次 scan 都會保持（用兩個元件同位置認，準確到半米）；儲存咗嘅結果列喺地方列表上面，所有人睇到。<b>Save view</b> 同碰撞一樣可以為每個地方記住視圖。淨高 issue 仲會記住條高度尺寸線，每次打開個 issue 嘅視圖都會再畫出嚟。</li><li><b>Include consultant models</b>（喺 Models counted 入面，預設開）：顧問嘅 IFC model 都會計，頁面未載入嘅會喺 scan 嗰陣載入。</li><li>鋪喺樓板上面嘅地台面層、企喺樓面上嘅樓梯，唔會當做頭頂嘅嘢。高度係由人企嘅位置垂直量（樓梯就由梯級量）。</li></ul><figure class=\"shot\"><img src=\"help-img/headroom-results.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><ol><li>掃描成個 model 或者揀咗嘅樓層</li><li>Probe 結果：量到嘅高度；Keep 留低做尺寸</li><li>今次掃描，或者已儲存嘅結果；Save result</li><li>紅色：低過限制；橙色：只係高過 100 mm 以內</li><li>未處理、唔係問題</li><li>全部開 issue</li><li>匯出：試算表、報告</li><li>一個低位：高度、限制、樓層、上面係乜；Look、Make issue、Save view、Not an issue</li><li>紅色係低過限制嘅範圍，連高度</li><li>顏色代表乜</li></ol></figure>"},{"id":"s52","ch":"碰撞同淨高檢查","h":"SBD：點樣準備 model 同送去 viewer","lv":3,"html":"<p>Checks &gt; <b>SBD</b> 需要 Revit 提供乜，同埋將 mass 送去 viewer 嘅步驟。全部由 model 讀出嚟 - 唔使每個區人手畫嘢。</p><p><b>要求</b></p><ul><li><b>建築用 Mass：</b> 每座建築（平台、每座塔樓）用 <b>Mass</b>（Massing &amp; Site &gt; In-Place Mass，或者 Mass family），建到真實高度同形狀。穿過建築嘅空位（例如塔樓下面嘅平台花園）建成空位 - 會變成 PE。唔使樓板、牆或者房間。</li><li><b>Mass 企喺地面：</b> 最低嗰個 mass 由高度區嘅地面（平均街道水平）開始；塔樓可以由平台開始。Model 喺錯嘅高度會令所有區移位 - Checks &gt; SBD 會提你。</li><li><b>地盤界線：</b> Property Line，或者喺 10 mm 內閉合嘅線。</li><li><b>街道：</b> 每條對住地盤嘅街用一塊 <b>Floor</b>，類型名有 <b>Street</b>、<b>Road</b>、<b>Lane</b> 或者 <b>Path</b>，由街邊畫到街邊，喺街道嘅高度；佢嘅<b>類型名</b>就係圖上嘅街名（例如類型 <i>Yeung Fan Lane North Street</i>）。路口唔係長條形 - 改為揀佢嘅中線同對面界線嘅線。 一條街可以係幾塊同類型嘅 Floor，或者一塊斜嘅、改過形狀嘅 Floor：同類型又相連嘅板會合併做一條街。</li><li><b>隔籬建築</b>（可以唔要）：地盤界線外面嘅 mass 用斜線顯示，唔計。</li></ul><p><b>步驟</b></p><ol><li>喺 Revit 打開 model，檢查 mass、Property Line 同街道樓板（3D 視圖：mass 企喺街道水平）。</li><li><b>LWK &gt; Viewer tools &gt; SBD Export。</b> 揀地盤界線；剔走唔係對住地盤嘅街；揀 <b>viewer 嘅 project</b> - 每次都會問（一次 export 會取代嗰個 project 嘅 SBD model），上次同呢個 Revit 檔用過嘅 project 排第一。唔會再問地面：Level 0 係同地盤相鄰最低嗰條街嘅平均水平（每條街用自己樓板嘅高度）；冇街就用 mass 嘅底。</li><li>Mass 會送去 viewer 即刻計算；Revit 視窗會顯示 P、要求 P 同每條街。Mass 亦會出現喺 project 嘅 3D，叫 <b>SBD masses - (model)</b>。</li><li>喺 viewer 打開 model 嘅 <b>3D</b> 頁 &gt; <b>Checks &gt; SBD</b>。<b>Run</b> 再計（plane 自動搵）；<b>Plan ...</b> 顯示每個區嘅平面同立面連計算；<b>Save</b>、<b>Make issue</b> 同 <b>Report</b> 保存結果。</li><li>改咗設計之後，再做一次 <b>SBD Export</b> - 會取代 mass 同結果（儲存咗嘅結果會留低）。</li></ol><p><b>如果有嘢唔啱</b></p><ul><li><b>「The lowest mass starts ... above the zones' ground」：</b> 地面或者 mass 喺錯嘅高度 - 再 export，揀啱嘅地面。</li><li><b>冇街：</b> Low 區嘅 Plane X 會改用地盤主方向；請建街道樓板。</li><li><b>Mass 嘅 model 喺 3D 位置唔啱：</b> 喺 Models 列表移動佢（佢放喺 export 嗰個 model 嘅 internal origin）。</li></ul>"},{"id":"s53","ch":"碰撞同淨高檢查","h":"冇 Revit 都做到 SBD：用 CAD 畫 model","lv":3,"html":"<p>冇 Revit model？用 AutoCAD（或者 SketchUp、Rhino，任何可以 save DXF 嘅軟件）喺 <b>CAD template</b> 嘅 layer 上面畫 SBD model，再 import：佢會變成 project 嘅 SBD model，計法同由 Revit 送嚟嘅完全一樣，啲 mass 亦會出現喺 3D。</p><p><b>要求</b></p><ul><li><b>單位：</b> 米（毫米同厘米會跟圖則嘅單位自動換算）。Block 要 explode - 唔會讀 block。</li><li><b>SBD-SITE：</b> 地盤界線，<b>一條閉合 polyline</b>。</li><li><b>SBD-STREET-&lt;街名&gt;：</b> 每條街嘅路面，用閉合 polyline 由地盤界線畫到街嘅對面（對面地盤界線），<b>Elevation = 嗰條街嘅平均街道水平</b>。一條街一個 layer - <i>SBD-STREET-TLO Street</i>、<i>SBD-STREET-Second Street</i> - dash 後面就係街名；一條街有兩個高度可以喺同一個 layer 畫兩塊。Level 0 係同地盤相鄰最低嗰條街。</li><li><b>SBD-MASS</b>（或者 <i>SBD-MASS-&lt;名&gt;</i>）：建築用閉合 polyline 加 <b>Elevation</b>（底）同 <b>Thickness</b>（高度）- 平台同塔樓疊起嚟 - 或者用 3D face、polyface mesh 或 MESH。AutoCAD 嘅實體（3DSOLID）讀唔到：先用 <b>CONVTOMESH</b> 轉做 mesh。SketchUp 同 Rhino 會 save 做 mesh。</li></ul><p><b>步驟</b></p><ol><li>喺 3D 頁 &gt; <b>Checks &gt; SBD</b>，撳 <b>CAD template</b>（No Revit?），打開個 DXF：有齊 layer 同規則 - 如果 project 已經有 SBD model（由 Revit 送過一次），就會有 project <b>自己嘅地盤界線同街道</b>；如果 project 嘅 3D（Revit export）有 shared coordinates，就用 <b>shared（測量）座標同 mPD 水平</b>；否則係一個例子（一個地盤、兩條街、一個平台同一座塔）。請保留圖入面 <b>LWK-SBD-FRAME: SHARED</b> 呢句：import 嗰陣會將張圖搬返去 Revit model 嘅原點，啲 mass 喺 3D 先會對得啱。</li><li>喺嗰啲 layer 畫你嘅地盤、街同 mass（刪走例子），用地盤本身嘅坐標，save 做 DXF（或者 DWG）。</li><li>撳 <b>Import CAD model ...</b> 揀個檔案。會即刻讀、即刻計，顯示做 <i>CAD: (檔名)</i>；讀唔到嘅嘢（block、實體、冇 thickness 嘅 polyline、唔係長條嘅街）會逐項列出。</li><li>改咗之後再 import 一次 - 會取代 model 同結果（儲存咗嘅結果會留低）。</li></ol>"},{"id":"s54","ch":"碰撞同淨高檢查","h":"SBD（PNAP APP-152）","lv":3,"html":"<figure class=\"shot\"><img src=\"help-img/model-sbd.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><ol><li>Checks &gt; SBD（旁邊有 Clash 同 Headroom）</li><li>再計一次</li><li>每個區嘅平面高度（全部，或者某一個高度）</li><li>最新結果，或者已儲存嘅；Save 保存呢個</li><li>透風度：P 對比要求 - PASS 或 FAIL</li><li>設計要求 (1)：Lp 對比 5U</li><li>每個區 Plane X 同 Y 嘅 P - 紅色：唔符合，綠色：符合</li><li>顏色嘅意思</li><li>Plan ...：每個區嘅平面、立面同街道峽谷</li><li>3D：喺 model 顯示或隱藏 SBD mass 同高度區界線</li><li>Make issue：為唔合格嘅地方開 issue</li><li>Report：每個區嘅平面同計算，可以列印</li><li>CAD ...：所有圖輸出 DXF 或 DWG</li><li>刪除 mass 同結果</li><li>CAD template：用 CAD 畫 model（冇 Revit 都得）</li><li>Import CAD model：張圖變成 SBD model</li></ol></figure><figure class=\"shot\"><img src=\"help-img/sbd-plan.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><ol><li>平面 / 立面 / 街道峽谷</li><li>投影面 X 或 Y</li><li>各高度區，連 P</li><li>呢張圖輸出 DXF 或 DWG</li><li>關閉</li><li>圖：S1、S2 ... 空隙加陰影、投影面、尺寸</li><li>計算：每個空隙嘅面積、深度同 S</li><li>放大 / 縮小、Fit</li></ol></figure><p>Checks &gt; <b>SBD</b> 會由 Revit model 嘅建築 <b>mass</b> 計算設計要求 (2) - 通風度 <b>P</b> 同分隔距離 <b>S1 / S2 / S3</b> - 同設計要求 (1) 街道峽谷 <b>U</b>。唔使畫 Filled Region，亦唔使每個區揀嘢：每個高度區都係由 mass 切出嚟。</p><ul><li><b>喺 Revit 要建乜：</b> 每座建築（平台、塔樓）用 <b>Mass</b>（Massing &amp; Site &gt; In-Place Mass，或者 Mass family）；<b>地盤界線</b>用 Property Line（或者喺 10 mm 內閉合嘅線）；每條<b>街用一塊 Floor</b>，類型名有 <b>Street</b>、<b>Road</b>、<b>Lane</b> 或者 <b>Path</b>（例如 <i>SBD Street</i>），由街道界線畫到街道界線，喺街道嘅高度（佢嘅<b>類型名</b>會做街名）。唔使開晒啲樓層 - 高度由 mass 嚟。</li><li><b>由街道樓板讀乜：</b> 佢嘅<b>中線</b>（兩條長邊嘅正中，轉彎都跟）、佢嘅<b>遠邊</b> = 對面地盤嘅界線（Case 1 U 用）同佢嘅<b>高度</b>。Axis 1（Projection Plane X）沿住同地盤相接最長嗰條街。高度區由<b>街道水平</b>量起 = 地盤附近街道樓板嘅平均頂面高度（按面積）；都可以改揀一個 Level。唔係長條形嘅樓板（路口）會唔計 - 改為揀佢嘅中線同對面界線嘅線。</li><li><b>LWK &gt; Viewer tools &gt; SBD Export：</b> 揀地盤界線，剔走唔係對住地盤嘅街，揀 viewer 嘅 project，mass 就會送去 viewer 即刻計算；Revit 視窗都會顯示結果，連每條街嘅長度、闊度同高度。 Model 會即刻送出，viewer 喺背後計算（進度條會等結果，最多 5 分鐘）；計好之前 Checks &gt; SBD 會顯示 <i>Assessing ...</i>。唔係長條形嘅街板只會報一次，仲可以即刻揀佢嘅中線同對面界線。</li><li><b>高度區：</b> <b>Low（0-20 m）、Middle（20-60 m）、High（60 m 以上）</b>。每個區嘅建築係 mass 喺嗰個區入面嘅高度嘅外框，所以平台 + 塔樓方案嘅 Middle 區係塔樓 - 唔係平台。冇建築嘅區唔會計。地盤界線外面嘅 mass（隔籬）會用斜線顯示，唔計。</li><li><b>表：</b> 每個區 Plane X 同 Plane Y 嘅 P（區立面上嘅 (IS + PE) / (W x H)，下面有 plane 嘅角度）、計到嘅空隙、<b>控制 P</b>（最低嗰個）對 Table 1 嘅<b>要求 P</b>（由地盤面積同 Lp），同 PASS / FAIL。Lp 係所有建築投影喺 Axis 1 嘅長度；如果 SBD panel 嘅 Lp（一座建築嘅短邊）會得出另一個要求 P，兩個都會顯示。<b>Case 1：</b> 每條街 U = 峽谷面積 / 沿中線長度（由中線 30 m 內嘅外牆到對面界線）、Lp 同 5U。</li><li><b>Run</b> 再計（投影 plane 自動搵 - 見下面）。<b>Save</b> 儲存結果俾所有人睇；列表顯示儲存咗嘅結果（打開嚟比較，✕ 刪除）。</li><li><b>Plan ...</b> 打開每個區嘅平面（Axis 1 或 2）：地盤、嗰個區嘅建築、每條空隙係橫過地盤嘅一條帶 - <b>綠色</b>＝計，<b>紅色</b>＝唔計（太窄或者被擋）- 連類別同闊度、S2 最窄位、15 m 或以上嘅<b>風道</b>（藍色虛線）同軸。</li><li><b>3D</b> 會喺 model 上面畫出 mass 同地盤喺地面、20 m 同 60 m（LWK Publish 發佈嘅 model）。<b>Make issue</b> 開一個 issue 寫低結果同唔計嘅嘢；<b>Report</b> 整一份有表同每個區每條軸平面嘅報告，可以列印或者 <b>Save to Folders (PDF)</b>（00 BIM &gt; Exports &gt; SBD）。</li><li>計算用 SBD panel 自己嘅引擎（Check &amp; Comply &gt; Shared.scripts，27/08），每個區用自己嘅外框：<b>S1</b> 係每邊側面區域嘅平均闊度 <b>面積 / 深度</b>（邊線跟住建築外角，最多 15°）- Plan 會列出計算，例如 <i>S1 (left side) = A / D = 706.9 m² / 70.83 m = 9.98 m</i>；<b>S2</b> 風道可以轉最多 15° 再轉返；斜邊界用 <b>S3</b> = A / D。每個區嘅 <b>Plane Y</b> 會喺 Plane X 嘅 <b>75-105°</b> 之間揀最好嘅角度；<b>Middle 同 High</b> 區嘅 <b>Plane X</b> 仲會轉去令 P 最大嘅角度（先 15° 一步，再準到 1°，最好嘅幾個用完整規則再確認）；Low 區 Plane X 沿住街。表入面每個區嘅 P 下面會顯示角度。</li><li><b>3D 入面嘅 SBD mass：</b> 每次 SBD Export 都會將啲 mass 放入 project 嘅 3D 做一個 model（Models 列表入面嘅 <b>SBD masses - (model)</b>：可以開關、透明度、移動，同顧問 model 一樣；放喺 export 嗰個 model 嘅 internal origin）。Checks &gt; SBD 嘅 <b>Remove ...</b> 會刪走 mass、最新結果同嗰個 model（儲存咗嘅結果會留低）。</li><li><b>高度：</b> 高度區由 Level 0 量起（同地盤相鄰最低嗰條街；冇街就用 mass 嘅底）。如果最低嗰個 mass 唔係由嗰度開始，Checks &gt; SBD 會提你（否則 10 m 高嘅平台會計咗入 Middle 區）。</li><li><b>立面（Plan ... &gt; Elevation）：</b> 每個區喺佢自己嘅 Plane X 同 Plane Y 上面嘅立面投影（Fig B10 / B11），由 mass 畫出：建築、<b>IS</b>（綠點：平面計到嘅空隙，至少有區高度嘅 2/3，同埋矮啲嘅建築上面向天開放嘅位 - 例如平台天台 - 連旁邊嘅 IS 闊 7.5 m 或以上先計）、<b>PE</b>（藍格：穿過建築、闊同高都至少 3 m 嘅空位）同區嘅框（紅色虛線）。計算跟 BD 樣本個案咁列：區面積 W x H、IS 面積、IS 嘅 P、PE 面積、PE 嘅 P，同 P = IS + PE。PE 最多計要求 P 嘅 1/3，IS 自己要達到要求 P 嘅 2/3。表入面嘅 P 就係呢個 P（平面嘅 IS / W 寫喺計算下面）。</li><li><b>Low 區豁免：</b> Low 區 1/3 H（6.67 m）或以下嘅部分唔計 - 喺立面用斜線顯示，唔當 IS，亦唔計入嗰個區嘅外框同 Lp（6 m 高嘅平台邊唔會封住後移位）。Table 1 嘅 Lp（使唔使計 P）仍然用 Low 區所有建築。</li><li><b>每個區嘅 Case 1：</b> U = 峽谷面積 / 沿中線長度，Lp = 外牆投影喺街上嘅長度；Low 區係平台（1/3 H 以上），Middle 同 High 區係塔樓；Lp 唔可以超過 5U（BD 樣本：U = 15 m，5U = 75 m，Lp = 80 - 7.5 x 2 = 65 m；塔樓 U = 15 + 4 = 19 m，5U = 95 m，Lp = 32 m）。<b>Plane Y：</b> 少過 2 公頃嘅地盤只查 Plane X；Plane Y 顯示做參考（灰色）。2 公頃或以上，Plane X 要 20 %，Plane Y 要 25 %（有建築高過 60 m 就要 33.3 %）。</li><li><b>變形立面（跟 SBD panel）：</b> 每個區喺 Plane X 同 Plane Y 嘅立面，由平面沿住地盤最近 plane 嗰條邊（街嗰邊）排出嚟：每條<b>空隙用佢嘅 S 值</b>（S1 = 側面區域嘅 A / D，S2 = 風道闊度 - 即係平面上面嘅數字），每組<b>建築用佢喺嗰條邊上面嘅闊度</b>（夾喺兩邊空隙之間，所以風道轉幾度會令旁邊嘅陰影闊啲或者窄啲）。所以 <b>W = 各 S 值 + 各陰影</b>，P = (IS + PE) / (W x H)。唔計嘅空隙（例如 S2 少過 15 m）用紅色斜線畫，唔當 IS。兩張圖都有同一條尺寸鏈：平面沿住近邊（每條空隙嘅投影闊度、佢嘅 S 同陰影），立面喺下面。</li><li><b>Plane 自動搵：</b> Low 區 Plane X 沿街（跟 BD 樣本）；Middle 同 High 區會完整計幾對 plane，用令 P（立面上報告嘅 P）最大嗰對 - Plan 會列出試過嘅組合。每個區嘅 Plane Y 喺 X 嘅 75-105° 之間揀最好嘅角度。唔使揀軸。</li><li><b>平面圖：</b> 每條風道同側面區域都畫到地盤界線（佢嘅帶，用地盤裁切）；標籤有轉角（0 至 15° 之間任何角度，例如 <i>S2 16.9 m · 7.6°</i>）；建築叫 B1、B2 ...，同立面一樣。</li><li><b>街道峽谷（Plan ... &gt; Street canyon）：</b> 設計要求 (1) 做一項獨立檢查，逐個區：每座對住街嘅建築，佢嘅峽谷（由中線 30 m 內嘅外牆到對面地盤界線）用斜線顯示，入面寫住 U，沿街畫出 Lp；旁邊有計算 - U = 峽谷面積 / 長度、Lp、5U 同結果。摘要有自己嘅判斷（Street canyon: Lp ≤ 5U · PASS / FAIL，連唔過嘅建築），Report 同 Make issue 都會包括。</li><li><b>設計要求 (1) - 臨街建築嘅 Lp（跟 GB081）：</b> 一座建築或者一組建築只要<b>任何部分</b>喺街道中線 30 m 內，就算臨街。佢嘅峽谷沿住建築喺嗰條街上嘅整段投影長度，由外牆到對面地盤界線：<b>U = 街道峽谷面積 / 長度</b>。有兩條街就用較細嘅 U（UB1 &lt; UB2）。<b>Max Lp = 5 x U</b>，實際 Lp（外牆投影喺街上嘅長度）唔可以超過。Street canyon 視圖畫出每個峽谷（STREET CANYON AREA A = ... m²）、ACTUAL Lp、LENGTH 同一個典型闊度，旁邊有計算；冇建築喺 30 m 內就會寫明唔適用。報告每個區都有一頁設計要求 (1)。</li><li><b>圖：</b> 空隙沿 plane 編號 <b>S1、S2、S3 ...</b>（平面、近邊尺寸鏈、立面同計算都用同一個號）；每個側面區域顯示面積 <b>A1</b> 同深度 <b>L1</b>（S1 = A1 / L1）；每條轉咗角嘅邊有角度符號同數值；Axis 1 (X) 同 Axis 2 (Y) 連佢哋之間嘅角度；比例尺（0 - 一半 - 全長）；街道中線標 <b>℄</b> 同街名。立面會標出建築輪廓每一級嘅闊度同高度，IS 編號（IS1、IS2 ...），高度另外用括號寫 model 嘅水平。所有數字都用 3 個小數位。</li><li><b>街道同 Plane X（報告 3）：</b> 會轉彎嘅街（圍住地盤轉角嘅 L 形街）逐段計：Low 區嘅 Plane X 沿住對住地盤最長嗰段，設計要求 (1) 每段當一條街計，例如 <i>TLO Street (leg 2)</i>；兩條喺唔同邊界嘅街各自計，用較細嘅 U。側面區域嘅邊<b>只轉一次</b>：先垂直於 plane，之後最多 15° 一直去到尾。未達 S 嘅空隙（S1 少過 7.5 m、S2 少過 15 m）但闊度有 3 m 或以上，喺立面當 <b>PE</b> 計（PE 最多計要求 P 嘅 1/3）；少過 3 m 就唔計。斜面切出嚟嘅細級會合併成一個 IS（或 PE）面積，用三角形（½ x 闊 x 高）或者階梯面積表示，輪廓尺寸亦合併做一級斜面。平面沿街寫街名，中線尾有 <b>℄</b>，同埋<b>平均街道水平</b>（評估嘅 Level 0）；Street canyon 視圖加上每座建築嘅 <b>Lp 長方形</b>（虛線 - 距離超過 30 m 嘅建築都會計出 Lp）、離中線 <b>30 m 嘅線</b>同街闊。報告入面嘅圖會裁切到地盤，印大啲。</li><li><b>Report 4 嘅規則：</b> <b>Level 0</b> 係同地盤相鄰最低嗰條街嘅平均水平；平面上每條街顯示自己嘅平均街道水平。<b>貼住街</b>（唔係共用界線）嘅側面區域會一直去到<b>街嘅中線</b>（S = A / L 會大咗）。兩邊嘅側面區域都由<b>同一個 projection plane</b> 量 - plane 喺地盤其中一邊（街嗰邊，或者計到最多嗰邊），邊線由佢垂直出發，再向外轉一次。每條風道兩條邊都去到界線。<b>IS 同 PE 橫向計：</b> 每個高度，未夠 S 嘅空隙連埋旁邊較矮建築上面向天開放嘅空間，加埋夠嗰條空隙嘅 S 闊就係 IS；空隙其餘部分係 PE（≥ 3 m 闊）。<b>設計要求 (1)：</b> 只計建築喺中線 30 m 以內嘅部分（Lp、峽谷同長方框都停喺 30 m 線）；<b>相距少過 15 m</b> 嘅建築當一組計 Lp（會標出距離）；每條街有自己嘅 U，最細嗰個控制。圖則寫 <b>Projection Plane X</b> 同 <b>Projection Plane Y</b>，所有字唔會重疊，plane 符號同比例尺會放喺圖則空位。</li><li><b>Report 5 嘅規則：</b> <b>側面區域</b>而家準確咁計：內邊由 plane 垂直出發，轉一次（最多 15°）；用<b>最近 plane</b> 嗰一塊；角位一定喺地盤界線上；貼住街嘅話，只係對住街嗰段界線先延伸到中線，兩邊用經過嗰段界線兩個角、<b>平行 plane</b> 嘅線封住。<b>風道</b>由頭到尾闊度一樣 - 轉角位嘅外邊垂直轉咗嘅邊去 offset，唔係橫向。唔再畫淡色投影帶。<b>設計要求 (1)：</b> 外牆中間退後超過 30 m 嘅話，峽谷會分開幾塊 - <i>A1(a) + A1(b)</i> - <b>U = (A(a) + A(b)) / (L(a) + L(b))</b>，Lp 係幾段投影加埋（Fig B7）；同一組建築之間嘅外牆當連續計。唔貼街嘅建築 <b>Lp = 最細外框矩形嘅短邊</b>，圖上有標註。每條街中線 30 m 嘅 offset 用虛線畫；街名、水平同闊度會放喺避開峽谷嘅位置。</li><li><b>Report 6 嘅規則：</b> 側面區域嘅內邊一定由 plane <b>垂直出發</b>，只會喺建築角位先轉（唔會一開始就斜），所以角位一定喺界線上。延伸入街嗰部分由界線旁邊嘅<b>街道樓板</b>判斷（唔再用中線距離），所以條街叫乜名、或者樓板同界線差少少，都照樣延伸 - 只會橫過條街，唔會沿住條街。<b>風道係一條直嘅帶</b>，由頭到尾闊度一樣，角度最多 15°。<b>設計要求 (1)：</b> 只有射線打中 30 m 內真正嘅外牆先計 - 兩翼之間退後超過 30 m 嘅外牆會變成<b>兩個峽谷 A(a) + A(b)</b>，條街唔係完全直都一樣。</li><li><b>Report 7 嘅規則：</b> 側面區域收窄到地盤界線上一點（內邊碰到界線）嗰段都計埋 - hatch 會<b>準確收喺界線嘅角</b>，唔會喺未到之前切平。向住街嘅界線如果有一段短過 3 m 嘅級位，或者界線同街道樓板之間有一條窄縫，都唔會將延伸入街嗰部分切開：一個延伸直到中線。風道兩端亦準確喺界線上。</li><li><b>Report 8 嘅規則：</b> 轉咗角嘅內邊由地盤遠端界線出咗地盤，而地盤喺佢後面仲轉角延續，側面區域會連嗰個角一齊計 - 內邊線外面嘅所有地盤，一直去到界線嘅角。平面有分叉嘅塔（Y 形或者 U 形）一定會畫喺立面（每個切面用佢裏面嘅一點對返所屬嘅建築），立面上每座建築都標 <b>B1、B2 ...</b>。<b>Lp（設計要求 (1)）</b> 係包住建築（或者一組建築，相距少過 15 m 當一組）嘅<b>概念矩形嘅長邊</b>；矩形貼住建築，揀令 Lp <b>最細</b>嘅方向（Fig B3：「L2 &gt; L1，Lp = L1」）- 所有建築都係咁，無論係咪對住街（取代 report 5 嘅短邊同峽谷分段嘅投影）。街道峽谷照樣計 U = (A(a) + A(b)) / (L(a) + L(b))，Max Lp = 5U。</li><li><b>TMTL496 嘅規則（L 形街、斜路、路口）：</b> <b>每條街用一個 Floor 類型</b>（類型名就係街名）；L 形或者彎嘅街都係一個類型 - 一塊或者幾塊 Floor 都得，唔使切開，viewer 會自己逐段計 - 路口屬於主路。同一條街嘅板如果重疊或者留咗少少空隙（斜路旁邊平嘅一段、改過形狀嘅斜路）會頭尾接駁，Revit 會列出每條街用咗幾多塊 Floor 同頂面。街尾畫成兩條邊嘅，中線唔會再喺尾打斜。貼街嘅側面區域會沿地盤嘅圓角或者斜角轉向路口，一直計到街道中線；佢喺街上嘅部分去到內邊同地盤界線相交嗰點為止，平行投影面切斷。平面上重疊嘅通風廊只當<b>一條</b>：保留計數嗰條（15 m 或以上）- 兩條都唔計就保留轉角最細嗰條；並排嘅就當一個開口，唔並排嘅另一條空隙就<b>略去</b>（打交叉、當阻擋、冇 IS）。直投影睇唔到、轉咗角（最多 15°）嘅開口會顯示為<b>斜向空隙</b>（A1 ...）；15 m 或以上會標示要檢查。兩條唔同名嘅街就係兩塊 Floor（兩個類型）：主路包路口，另一條街喺主路嘅路邊線收尾。Checks &gt; SBD 嘅 <b>Model (JSON)</b> 可以下載送出嘅 model，傳俾我哋檢查。每條街只有<b>一條 30 m 線</b>（成條中線向內偏移 30 m），而每兩組分開嘅建築都會標尺寸（15 m 或以上，分開）。</li><li><b>TMTL496 第三次審閱：</b> 側面區域喺街上嘅部分，啱啱好喺內邊同地盤界線相交嘅兩點之間，兩頭都<b>平行投影面</b>切斷。過咗最後一個建築角，內邊亦可以向離開投影面嘅方向轉 15°，冇建築擋住嘅地方就計多啲面積。開口會<b>逐層</b>搵：喺某個高度以上先通嘅開口（例如兩座塔中間有座矮樓）會當<b>由嗰個高度起嘅通風廊（S2）</b>，立面上嗰個高度以下當阻擋，以上當 IS（矮樓旁邊少過 3 m 嘅窄縫算佢嘅一部分；嗰度有較闊嘅空隙就照原樣保留，矮樓上面嘅空間橫向計）。轉角嘅開口夠 15 m 或以上，而家都會當通風廊計。每條通風廊會用經同一個開口、轉最多 15° 嘅<b>最闊</b>帶量度；咁樣夠 15 m 就計數。喺平面將滑鼠放喺建築名上面，會顯示佢頂部離 Level 0 幾高 - 如果喺高過佢頂部嘅平面層仍然見到佢，即係 Level 0 比你預期低（Level 0 係貼地盤最低嗰條街）。</li><li><b>檢查進行中：</b> 每次 SBD 檢查都喺伺服器上獨立嘅程序度行，優先次序較低，所以期間 viewer 同由 Revit 發佈都照常運作。大嘅 model 可能要幾分鐘 - 面板會顯示進行中。超過 20 分鐘嘅檢查會停止並顯示訊息：請將 model（Model (JSON)）傳俾我哋睇睇。</li><li>撳 <b>Run</b> 會喺伺服器開始檢查，面板會顯示進行中；完成後結果會自動顯示（由 2026-12-09 起，有好多級塔樓嘅大 model 都唔使一分鐘）。結果下面嘅 <b>took ...</b> 會寫檢查用咗幾耐，同埋每一步用咗幾耐（plane search、elevations、Case 1 等）。你可以離開面板再返嚟 - 期間 viewer 其他部分照常運作。</li><li><b>街道峽谷闊度</b>會垂直於該段街道（佢嘅整體方向）量度，覆蓋建築或建築組嘅整個臨街面，只要外牆喺中線 30 m 範圍內 - 街道由幾塊 Floor 接駁而令中線有少少彎位，都唔會令峽谷變斜。</li><li><b>立面上</b>，建築兩端如果某部分全部喺唔計嘅 1/3 H 以內，佢上面嘅空間（同埋旁邊較矮一級上面嘅空間）就係側面退縮旁邊嘅空間：會橫向併入嗰個退縮嘅 IS（如果個退縮本身唔計，兩者加埋夠 7.5 m 都會計）。建築輪廓每一級都寫上闊度，窄嘅會放喺唔撞嘅位置。Checks &gt; SBD 嘅 <b>3D</b> 剔格會一齊顯示或者隱藏 3D 入面所有 SBD 嘅嘢 - 外框、高度區界線，同每次 export 加入嘅 <b>SBD masses</b> model。</li><li><b>面板上：</b> 符合要求嘅 P 或 Lp 用綠色底，唔符合嘅用實心紅色，表下面有圖例講明（灰色：只供參考）；所有動作（Plan、3D、Make issue、Report、CAD、Remove、CAD template、Import CAD model）都係掣。</li><li><b>Plan level：</b> 每個區都有 <b>Plan level</b> 選單：預設 <i>All levels (worst)</i> 計晒區內所有高度；揀一個高度，嗰個區嘅平面（空隙、側面區域、風道）就用 mass 喺嗰個高度切出嚟嘅形狀。立面一定係真 3D，所以喺其他高度擋住嘅照計擋住。表、平面、立面同報告都會寫明每個區用咗邊個高度（<i>all levels</i> 或者 <i>plan at +x</i>）。</li><li><b>CAD 輸出：</b> <b>CAD ...</b> &gt; <b>DXF</b>（或者 <b>DWG</b>，由 server 嘅 ODA File Converter 整）會 save 晒所有平面、立面同街道峽谷，每個區一行，每張有標題；Plan 視窗嘅 <b>DXF / DWG</b> 只 save 而家見到嗰張，平面用 model 本身嘅坐標（可以疊落地盤圖）。一種嘢一個 layer - SBD-SITE、SBD-STREET、SBD-BLDG、SBD-IS、SBD-PE、SBD-NOT、SBD-CANYON、SBD-LP、SBD-DIM、SBD-TEXT ... - 單位係米。</li><li><b>縮放：</b> 喺 Plan、Elevation 同 Street canyon 視圖，用滑鼠轆（或者兩指）喺指標位置縮放，拖動移動，右下角有 <b>+</b>、<b>-</b> 同 <b>Fit</b>（或者雙擊）。</li></ul><figure class=\"shot\"><img src=\"help-img/sbd-report.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><ol><li>列印 / 儲存做 PDF</li><li>Save to Folders (PDF)：存入 project 嘅資料夾</li><li>有幾多張高度區圖</li><li>結果：P 對比要求、Lp 對比 5U、地盤、投影面、Level 0</li><li>每個高度區：平面高度、Plane X 同 Y 嘅 P、Case 1</li><li>每個高度區嘅平面同立面，連計算</li></ol></figure>"},{"id":"s55","ch":"碰撞同淨高檢查","h":"採光同通風（窗面積檢查）","lv":3,"html":"<p>Revit 嘅 <b>Light &amp; Vent</b> 檢查會逐個房計算所需嘅採光面積（房面積 x 1/10）同可開啟面積（x 1/16），同佢嘅窗同幕牆板提供嘅面積比較。結果可以喺 viewer <b>嘅平面圖 sheet</b> 上面審閱 - 就算檢查係喺一個 model 做（<b>Calculation Master Model</b>，房面積最準），而平面圖 sheet 係由另一個 model 發佈（<b>Layout Master Model</b>）都得。兩個 model 只要用<b>同一套 shared coordinates</b>。</p><p><b>喺 Revit</b></p><ul><li><b>Calculation model：</b> 照舊做 <b>Light &amp; Vent</b>，之後喺 <i>Send the result to the viewer?</i> 揀 <b>Yes</b>，再揀 viewer project。每個房會連埋佢嘅輪廓、窗同結果一齊送出；diagrams PDF（如果有整）都會一齊送，亦會存喺 Folders &gt; 00 BIM &gt; Exports &gt; Light &amp; Ventilation。</li><li><b>Layout model：</b> 用<b>更新咗嘅 add-in</b>（2026-12-10 或之後）<b>再發佈一次</b>平面圖 sheet。之後每張平面圖都會記住佢喺 shared coordinates 嘅位置。未再發佈之前，有房間表嘅平面圖 sheet 會用<b>房號同房名</b>對應佢自己嘅房去顯示；圖例會講明邊啲平面圖仲要再發佈。</li><li><b>房</b>一律只取 Calculation model 自己嘅房（2026-12-11 起）；窗同幕牆板仍然可以來自佢嘅 link model。Link model 將同一層叫第二個名（例如 4/F 叫 5/F）唔會再加入佢嘅房。</li><li><b>完整報告：</b> 如果呢部電腦整唔到 diagrams PDF（要有 Python 同 reportlab），diagrams 會送去 server 由 server 整 PDF；如果未整 diagrams，Light &amp; Vent 會問你要唔要為 viewer 整。</li></ul><p><b>喺 sheet 上面</b></p><ul><li><b>View &gt; Light &amp; Vent</b> 會喺<b>同一層</b>嘅平面圖上將每個已檢查嘅房上色：綠色 <b>OK</b>、紅色 <b>NOT OK</b> / <b>NO WINDOW</b>、橙色 <b>NEEDS DATA</b>（有窗類型要確認）。同另一個房一齊計嘅房（例如廚房同客廳：<i>WITH 131</i>）會用嗰個房嘅顏色畫虛線。啲圓點係佢嘅窗同幕牆板。</li><li>左下角嘅圖例會顯示數量、model 同檢查時間，仲有一個開關：<b>Filled</b>（房間上色 - 圖則嘅線穿過顏色仍然清楚）、<b>Outline</b>（只有每個房嘅輪廓同一個結果顏色嘅圓點，圖則完全睇得清楚）或者 <b>Off</b>。呢部機會記住你嘅選擇。</li><li><b>顏色下面冇圖則？</b> 如果發佈平面圖嗰陣有 link model（例如塔樓單位）未載入或者佢嘅 workset 關咗，sheet 嗰部分就冇圖：圖例同狀態列會列出嗰個 link。請喺載入晒 link、打開晒 workset 嘅情況下打開 Layout model，再發佈嗰張 sheet。</li><li><b>撳一個房</b>（Select 工具）：卡片會顯示面積、所需同提供嘅採光及可開啟面積（實量玻璃，旁邊係 闊 x 高 x 70 %）、每個窗（標記、類型、尺寸、開法、所佔比例）同備註。<b>Show in 3D</b> 會喺 model 顯示佢啲窗；<b>Make issue</b> 會喺房外面畫雲線並打開已填好嘅 issue 表格。<b>Esc</b> 清除。</li></ul><p><b>表格同 Dashboard</b></p><ul><li><b>3D &gt; Checks &gt; Light &amp; Vent：</b> 最頂嘅 <b>Show on sheets</b> 會打開顯示最多所揀房間（樓層、座數、單位）嘅平面圖 sheet 並上色。表格有 <b>Tower</b> 一欄；列出所有房，可以按樓層、座數、單位同結果篩選（先睇要處理嘅房）。撳一行會顯示卡片：<b>Show in 3D</b> 會喺同一頁揀中並放大佢啲窗（唔會重新載入）；<b>Make issue (3D)</b> 會喺度打開已填好嘅 3D issue 表格（如果佢啲窗唔喺顯示緊嘅 model 入面，就會喺房嘅位置）；<b>Show on plan ...</b> 會打開嗰張 sheet 並顯示嗰個房。冇平面圖顯示到佢嘅時候，卡片會講原因（平面圖未再發佈，或者冇嗰層嘅平面圖）。</li><li><b>Full report</b>（3D 分頁、sheet 上面嘅圖例、Dashboard）：按樓層同單位列出每個房嘅表，再列每個房嘅窗 - <b>Print / Save as PDF</b>，或者 <b>Save to Folders</b>（Light &amp; Ventilation，存做 PDF）。<b>Table (CSV)</b> 同 <b>Diagrams (PDF)</b> 可以下載表格同 diagrams。</li><li><b>Dashboard：</b> 有一張 Light &amp; Ventilation 卡，顯示數量同上次檢查日期。</li><li>如果房喺平面圖上嘅位置唔啱，即係兩個 model 唔係用同一套 shared coordinates：請同 BIM team 檢查（Revit 嘅 Manage &gt; Coordinates）。</li></ul>"},{"id":"s56","ch":"喺 model 入面行","h":"喺 model 入面行","lv":2,"html":"<p>Walk 模式將你放喺棟樓入面眼睛嘅高度，跟住樓板、樓梯同斜路行。</p><p><b>開始：</b> 撳 <b>Walk</b>，然後撳一塊樓板（撳牆會將你放喺牆前面嘅樓板）。或者右鍵撳一個位揀 <b>Walk from here</b>。開始行會熄 floor plan 同 section box。</p><table><tr><th>動作</th><th>鍵盤／滑鼠</th><th>iPad / iPhone</th></tr><tr><td>向前／向後</td><td>W / S 或者 ↑ / ↓</td><td>畫面上嘅控制板</td></tr><tr><td>打側行</td><td>A / D</td><td>畫面上嘅控制板</td></tr><tr><td>轉身</td><td>← / →，或者用滑鼠拖</td><td>用手指拖，或者控制板</td></tr><tr><td>望上望落</td><td>用滑鼠拖</td><td>用手指拖</td></tr><tr><td>快啲</td><td>㩒住 Shift（3 倍速）</td><td>-</td></tr><tr><td>向前或者向後一步</td><td>碌滑鼠轆</td><td>-</td></tr><tr><td>上一層／下一層</td><td>Page Up / Page Down</td><td>-</td></tr><tr><td>升／降（Gravity 熄咗）</td><td>E / Q</td><td>-</td></tr><tr><td>停</td><td>Esc 或者 <b>Stop</b></td><td><b>Stop</b></td></tr></table><p><b>Walking panel 設定</b>（會記住）：</p><ul><li><b>Eye</b> 眼睛高度，0.8 至 3 m（預設 1.6 m）。</li><li><b>Speed</b> 速度，0.5 至 8 m/s（預設 1.5 m/s）。</li><li><b>Gravity</b>（開）：企喺樓板上面，行得上樓梯同斜路，唔理檯咁高嘅級。</li><li><b>Walls block</b>（熄）：唔俾你穿牆。Model 入面啲門係閂住嘅，所以開咗呢個連門口都會擋住。</li></ul><p>喺 Sheets 版用 <b>2D + 3D</b> 加 <b>Walk</b>，就可以喺 3D 行，隔籬嘅 plan 會顯示你喺邊。</p>"},{"id":"s57","ch":"顧問嘅 model（IFC）","h":"顧問嘅 model（IFC）","lv":2,"html":"<p>其他公司（結構、MEP、室內、幕牆）嘅 model 可以同 project 自己嘅一齊睇。叫佢哋俾 <b>IFC</b>（IFC 2x3 或者 IFC4）：SketchUp、Revit、Tekla、ArchiCAD 同 Rhino 全部都出得，而且保留晒元件、屬性同真實座標。（「WebGL」係瀏覽器畫圖嘅方法，唔係用嚟交換嘅檔案格式。）</p><table><tr><th>用法</th><th>點做</th></tr><tr><td>加入呢個 project 嘅 3D</td><td><b>Models</b> panel &gt; <b>+ Consultant model (IFC)</b>：揀 .ifc，填名、公司同專業，撳 <b>Upload and convert</b>。Server 會轉換（有進度條），完成後就喺 <b>Consultant models</b> 出現</td></tr><tr><td>疊另一個 project 嘅 model</td><td><b>+ Overlay another project</b>：揀一個你開得嘅 project 同佢其中一個 model。會用兩個 project 共用嘅 shared coordinates 擺位</td></tr><tr><td>自己一版 3D</td><td>Admin 用 <b>New 3D project from IFC</b>（Admin 版）開。座標同乜都對唔上嘅 model 用：做一個獨立參考，之後一樣可以疊落其他 project</td></tr></table><ul><li>每個顧問 model 有剔格（你自己開／關）同一條可以調透明嘅 slider。</li><li><b>整體上色，方便比較：</b> 顧問 model 隔籬（同 <b>Models</b> 清單每個 model 隔籬）嘅小圓圈，可以將成個 model 變一隻顏色 - 紅、橙、黃、綠、青、藍、紫、灰或者任揀 - 例如自己 project 灰色、結構紅色。<b>↺ Original colour</b>（顏色選單入面，或者上咗色嘅 model 隔籬個 <b>↺</b>）變返原色；Models panel 頂部嘅 <b>↺ Reset colours</b> 一次過將所有 model 變返原色。會記喺呢部機，可以同透明 slider 一齊用，<b>White</b> 模式都保留顏色。</li><li>用 <b>No coordinates: set in the middle</b> 擺位嘅 model，位置會為所有人記住，手機都一樣 - 手機載入嘅 link model 少啲，以前會因此計錯位置。</li><li><b>Place</b>（加佢嗰個人或者 project admin）幫所有人設定擺喺邊：<b>Shared coordinates</b>（有協調座標嘅顧問就係呢個）、<b>This model's origin</b>，或者 <b>No coordinates: set in the middle</b>；再用 <b>East / North / Up</b>（mm）同 <b>Turn</b>（°）一路睇一路手動移。<b>Save for everyone</b> 儲存；<b>Cancel</b> 放返原位。</li><li>佢嘅元件一樣撳得，一樣可以開 issue。</li><li><b>×</b> 由 project 移除（加佢嗰個人或者 project admin）。</li></ul>"},{"id":"s58","ch":"Issue 同 BCF","h":"Issue 同 BCF","lv":2,"html":"<p>Issue 係一個 markup 或者 3D 嘅一點，有標題、類型、負責人、到期日同對話；server 會幫佢編號（#N），同一個 issue 會喺 Sheets、3D、Dashboard 同 Revit 出現。</p>"},{"id":"s59","ch":"Issue 同 BCF","h":"開 issue","lv":3,"html":"<figure class=\"shot\"><img src=\"help-img/issue-new.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><ol><li>Template：用已儲存嘅範本填 issue</li><li>Save as template：將呢個儲存做 project 範本</li><li>標題</li><li>描述</li><li>類型：General、Design、Coordination、Clash ...</li><li>指派：名或者 email</li><li>到期日</li><li>狀態</li><li>優先</li><li>位置：圖則、視圖同 model 入面嗰點</li><li>Save issue（Cancel 取消）</li></ol></figure><table><tr><th>喺邊</th><th>點做</th></tr><tr><td>喺 sheet 上面</td><td>將頂部轉做 <b>Issue</b> 再畫 markup；或者揀一個 markup 撳 <b>Issue</b>；或者右鍵撳佢揀 <b>Raise issue</b>。會自動夾一張清晰嘅圖則截圖：直接由 PDF 用大約 200 dpi 畫出嚟，唔受你放大幾多或者電腦嘅速度設定影響。</td></tr><tr><td>喺 3D</td><td>撳 <b>Add issue</b>，然後撳個位（iPad：㩒住）。鏡頭、section 同隱藏咗嘅元件會一齊儲存，仲會夾一張截圖。<b>Mark up snapshot</b> 俾你喺張相上面畫嘢（cloud、箭咀、文字等等）。</td></tr></table><p>填好 issue 視窗，然後撳 <b>Save issue</b>：</p><table><tr><th>欄</th><th>備註</th></tr><tr><td><b>Title</b></td><td>一定要填，最多 120 個字。寫清楚咩問題、喺邊，例如「L12 corridor: fire door swing clashes with riser」</td></tr><tr><td><b>Type</b></td><td>General、Design、Coordination、Clash、Fire safety、Statutory / BD、Structure、MEP、Facade、Drawing error、Query / RFI</td></tr><tr><td><b>Description</b></td><td>咩問題、你預期係點、有咩參考</td></tr><tr><td><b>Assign to</b></td><td>揀一個 project 成員（或者打個名）</td></tr><tr><td><b>Due</b></td><td>幾時要有答覆</td></tr><tr><td><b>Status</b></td><td>Open、In progress、Resolved、Closed</td></tr><tr><td><b>Priority</b></td><td>Low、Normal（預設）、High、Critical</td></tr><tr><td><b>Template</b></td><td>載入一套儲存咗嘅欄位；<b>Save as template</b> 將而家嘅分享俾成個 project</td></tr></table><figure class=\"shot\"><img src=\"help-img/issue-3d.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><ol><li>範本；Save as template</li><li>標題（由檢查自動填）</li><li>類型</li><li>描述（由檢查自動填）</li><li>指派；到期日</li><li>狀態同優先</li><li>喺 model 嘅位置</li><li>視圖截圖</li><li>喺截圖上畫：雲線、箭咀、文字 ...</li><li>Save issue</li></ol></figure>"},{"id":"s60","ch":"Issue 同 BCF","h":"跟進 issue","lv":3,"html":"<ul><li>喺清單撳一個 issue（或者 3D 入面佢支 pin）打開佢。喺 3D，視圖會返去開 issue 嗰個人見到嘅樣：同一個眼位同方向、section box 連佢嘅角度（或者 section plane）、隱藏咗嘅元件、平行定透視，同 floor plan。<b>Show in view</b> 同 issue 連結都一樣。</li><li><b>喺 Revit</b>（LWK Issues &gt; <b>Go to</b>）：用 viewer 普通鏡頭、或者行緊（walk）時開嘅 issue，會喺一個透視鏡頭視圖 <b>LWK Issue - &lt;你&gt; (camera)</b> 由同一個眼位打開，連埋同一個 section box，唔再係由外面睇成棟樓。</li><li>喺 issue 視窗：改標題同欄位、<b>Add photo</b>（地盤相，可以一次加幾張），喺 <b>Discussion</b> 寫低再撳 <b>Post</b>。打 <b>@</b> 可以 mention project 成員。</li><li><b>討論入面加相</b>（Sheets 同 3D 一樣）：Post 旁邊嘅 <b>📷 Photo</b> 揀相 - 用手機或者 iPad 可以即刻影 - 或者喺訊息格 <b>Ctrl+V</b> 貼截圖，或者將相片檔拖入去。相會喺格下面等住（✕ 拎走一張），撳 <b>Post</b> 就同訊息一齊出；淨係相冇字都得。大張相會先縮細（1920 px）。喺討論撳一張相可以睇大圖（← → 下一張，<b>Esc</b> 關）。Issue report 會喺訊息下面顯示呢啲相。</li><li><b>Show in view</b> 返去嗰個位；<b>Show in 3D</b> 喺嗰度打開 3D 版。</li><li><b>Not an issue</b> 會連一個人人睇到嘅原因閂咗佢；同一個掣可以重開。</li><li><b>Delete</b> 會幫所有人刪除。Member 只可以刪自己嘅 issue；project admin 刪得任何一個。</li><li><b>Revit element</b>（3D issue）：開 issue 嗰個元件，有 <b>Copy Revit IDs</b>、<b>Show in 3D</b> 同 <b>Show in Revit</b>。</li><li><b>Tasks：</b> 連住呢個 issue 嘅 task，有負責人同到期日。<b>+ New task from this issue</b> 開一個（睇「Issue 同 task 連埋一齊」）；<b>Send to chat</b> 將 issue 貼去一個 chat。</li><li>將狀態改做 <b>Resolved</b> 或者 <b>Closed</b> 再撳 <b>Save</b>：如果 issue 嘅 task 仲未完成，viewer 會問你要唔要順手剔佢哋做完成。</li></ul>"},{"id":"s61","ch":"Issue 同 BCF","h":"狀態：邊個做乜（團隊做法）","lv":3,"html":"<table><tr><th>狀態</th><th>邊個改</th><th>意思</th></tr><tr><td>Open</td><td>開 issue 嘅人</td><td>開咗，等負責人跟</td></tr><tr><td>In progress</td><td>負責人</td><td>做緊</td></tr><tr><td>Resolved</td><td>負責人</td><td>改好或者答咗；等開 issue 嘅人檢查</td></tr><tr><td>Closed</td><td>開 issue 嘅人或者 project admin</td><td>檢查過，搞掂</td></tr></table>"},{"id":"s62","ch":"Issue 同 BCF","h":"搵 issue","lv":3,"html":"<ul><li><b>Sheets：</b> 右邊 panel 列出 <b>All / Issues / Comments</b>，可以按 Sheet、Status、Assigned to、Raised by、View、Issue type 或者 Markup type 分組，有 <b>Search</b> 格。右鍵撳一項可以打開、喺 sheet 或者 3D 顯示，或者改狀態。</li><li><b>3D：</b> <b>Issues in 3D</b> 按 Status、Floor、Issue type、Assigned to、Raised by 或者 Model 分組。<b>Sheet issues</b> 會將喺 sheet 開嘅 issue 用菱形顯示喺 model 入面。<b>Hide issues</b>（panel 頂部）隱藏啲 pin，<b>Hide closed</b> 隱藏已解決同已關閉嘅（乜都冇刪）- 喺 sheet 上面，連同同嗰個 issue group 埋一齊嘅所有 markup。</li><li><b>Dashboard：</b> 篩選、過咗期清單同責任表（睇「Dashboard 同 project」）。</li></ul>"},{"id":"s63","ch":"Issue 同 BCF","h":"BCF：同 Revit、Navisworks 等等交換 issue","lv":3,"html":"<ul><li><b>Export BCF</b>（3D 版）同 <b>BCF</b>（Sheets 版）會下載一個 BCF 2.1 檔，入面有每個 issue 嘅標題、狀態、優先次序、日期、作者、負責人、描述、鏡頭、揀咗嘅元件同截圖。冇 issue 嘅普通 comment 唔會包括，issue 類型、comment 對話同加咗嘅相都唔會包括。</li><li>揀咗嘅元件會連佢嘅 IFC GUID <b>同 Revit ElementId</b>（AuthoringToolId）一齊寫入，所以 Autodesk BCF Manager、BCFier 同 Revizto 呢啲 Revit BCF 工具會喺 Revit 揀中佢。</li><li><b>Import BCF</b>（只限 3D 版）讀 Revit、Navisworks、Solibri 或者 ACC 嘅 BCF 2.0、2.1 同 3.0。佢會先問個檔用邊套座標：除非你知，否則揀 <b>Work it out (recommended)</b>。已經 import 過（同一個 ID）嘅 issue 會跳過。</li></ul>"},{"id":"s64","ch":"Issue 同 task 連埋一齊","h":"Issue 同 task 連埋一齊","lv":2,"html":"<p>Issue 講咩出咗問題；task 講邊個幾時之前改好。兩樣連埋一齊，每一邊都會問你要唔要順手閂埋另一邊。</p><ul><li><b>由 issue 開 task：</b> 喺 issue 視窗撳 <b>+ New task from this issue</b>。呢個 project 嘅 task list 同 group 會排先，負責人係 issue 嘅 <b>Assigned to</b>，到期日同 issue 一樣。Issue、佢嘅檔案同 Revit 元件都會放落個 task。剔 <b>Open the task when made</b> 就會開完即刻去個 task。</li><li><b>Task 完成 → issue：</b> 當你 <b>Mark complete</b> 一個 task，而佢連住嘅 issue 仲未閂，Tasks 會問 <b>Resolve its issues too?</b> 剔要改嘅，揀 Resolved 或者 Closed。改法同你喺 viewer 自己改一樣：有歷史、email、chat 卡片，同一條寫明係邊個 task 嘅 comment。</li><li><b>Issue 解決 → task：</b> 將 issue 改做 Resolved 或者 Closed 再 <b>Save</b>；如果佢嘅 task 仲未完成，viewer 會問你要唔要剔佢哋做完成。啲 task 嘅 activity 都會多一行記錄。</li><li>Task 視窗會顯示每個相連 issue 而家嘅狀態；task 清單會顯示 <b>#n open</b> 或者 <b>#✓</b>。</li></ul>"},{"id":"s65","ch":"Revit 元件","h":"Revit 元件","lv":2,"html":"<p>3D issue 會記住開 issue 嗰個 Revit 元件：<b>ElementId</b>、<b>UniqueId</b>、IFC GUID、category、family / type 同樓層。由 LWK add-in publish 嘅 model 全部都知；舊啲嘅 model 只有 IFC GUID。</p><table><tr><th>想</th><th>咁做</th></tr><tr><td>而家喺 Revit 揀中佢</td><td><b>Copy Revit ID</b>（或者 <b>Copy Revit IDs</b>），然後喺 Revit 用 <b>Manage &gt; Select by ID</b> 貼上。今日已經用得，唔使改 add-in</td></tr><tr><td>喺 3D 睇佢</td><td><b>Show in 3D</b>：3D 版會揀出嗰啲元件再 zoom 埋去</td></tr><tr><td>叫 Revit 揀佢</td><td><b>Show in Revit</b> 叫 LWK add-in 喺 Revit 揀中佢。Add-in 未支援之前，會改為 copy 啲 id 俾你用 Select by ID</td></tr><tr><td>交俾同事</td><td>喺 3D 版揀元件再撳 <b>+ Task</b>：佢哋會放落 task 做 <b>Elements to change</b>，有同樣嘅掣</td></tr><tr><td>傳去其他軟件</td><td><b>Export BCF</b>：Revit 嘅 BCF 工具會用 ElementId 揀中個元件</td></tr></table>"},{"id":"s66","ch":"搜尋","h":"搜尋","lv":2,"html":"<p>一個格搵晒所有嘢：喺任何一版按 <b>Ctrl+K</b> 或者 <b>/</b>，或者撳頂部個放大鏡。</p><ul><li>佢會搵 <b>project</b>、<b>task</b>（標題、描述、T-12）、<b>issue</b>（#12、標題、描述、sheet、負責人、Revit 元件同 id）、<b>sheet</b>、儲存咗嘅 <b>3D 視圖</b>、<b>訊息</b>，同 task 同 issue 上面嘅<b>檔案同連結</b>。</li><li>打一個或者幾個字；每個字都要對到。結果按種類分組；↑ ↓ 同 <b>Enter</b> 打開，<b>Esc</b> 閂。</li><li>你只會見到你有權打開嘅嘢。個格空白嗰陣會列出你最近搜尋過嘅。</li></ul>"},{"id":"s67","ch":"離線工作","h":"離線工作","lv":2,"html":"<p>喺地盤冇訊號嘅時候，下載咗落部機嘅 project 照樣用得：sheet、3D model、issue 同 markup。</p><ol><li>有網絡嗰陣，打開個 project，喺右上角個人選單揀 <b>Work offline ...</b>，再撳 <b>Download for offline</b>。下載會顯示進度，斷咗可以繼續。</li><li>冇網絡嗰陣，頂部會寫 <b>Offline - copy of &lt;日期&gt;</b>。可以睇 sheet 同 model、開同回覆 issue、畫 markup。</li><li>離線做嘅改動會喺部機度等（<b>N changes waiting</b>），網絡返嚟就會自己 upload（<b>All changes uploaded</b>）。</li></ol><ul><li>Dashboard、Admin、Board、Tasks、Messenger、同舊版本比較同加 PDF 都要有網絡。</li><li>喺 iPad 同 iPhone，先 <b>Add to Home Screen</b>：Safari 可能會清走幾個禮拜冇開過嘅網站，但 Home Screen 嘅 app 會保留。</li></ul>"},{"id":"s68","ch":"手機同平板","h":"手機同平板","lv":2,"html":"<p>同一個網址喺 iPad 同 iPhone 嘅 Safari 都用得；viewer 會認出部機，載入輕啲嘅 3D model，等部機記憶體夠用。</p><p><b>手機或者平板有乜唔同</b></p><ul><li>側邊 panel 變成抽屜：左邊 <b>☰ Models</b> / <b>☰ Sheets</b>，右邊 <b>ⓘ Details</b> / <b>Issues</b>。撳抽屜外面就閂。Details 上面有粒點即係揀咗嘢。</li><li>3D 會載入每個 model 嘅手機版，每次 publish 之後 server 會整。大 project 嘅幾何會跟住你望邊度一嚿嚿攞（「streaming」），先粗後幼。</li><li><b>Light mode</b> 開咗：重複嘅標準層只會喺你望緊嘅附近載入。</li><li>傢俬呢啲細嘢只會喺鏡頭附近畫，遠嘅部分用簡化咗嘅形狀。</li><li>切到嘅實體有橙色 hatch，但冇啡色輪廓線。</li><li>頂部可以打橫碌：掃一掃就見到 Board、Tasks、Chat 同 Dashboard。</li><li><b>Search</b> 會佔滿成個畫面。喺 <b>Messenger</b>，撳一下訊息就出佢嘅掣；Enter 係換行，撳圓形掣先發送。</li></ul><p><b>手勢</b></p><table><tr><th>手勢</th><th>3D</th><th>Sheets</th></tr><tr><td>一隻手指</td><td>轉</td><td>用而家嘅工具畫（用過 Apple Pencil 之後就係 pan）</td></tr><tr><td>兩隻手指</td><td>捏 zoom，拖 pan</td><td>捏 zoom，拖 pan</td></tr><tr><td>Double tap</td><td>對準嗰個面</td><td>-</td></tr><tr><td>㩒住</td><td>喺嗰點開新 issue</td><td>右鍵選單</td></tr><tr><td>兩隻／三隻手指 tap</td><td>-</td><td>Undo / redo</td></tr></table><p><b>貼士</b></p><ul><li>iPad 打橫用，畫圖嘅位最多。</li><li>如果個 model 啱啱幾分鐘前先 publish，手機版可能仲整緊；版面會問你要唔要整，等幾分鐘再試。</li><li>如果 Safari 自己 reload 個版，即係部機記憶體唔夠：喺 <b>Models</b> 唔剔你唔使用嘅 model，留喺一層，再報告（睇「解決問題同常見問題」）。</li></ul>"},{"id":"s69","ch":"Performance panel 同設定","h":"Performance panel 同設定","lv":2,"html":"<p>3D 版右下角嘅 <b>Performance</b> 連結會打開載入時間、frame rate 同記憶體，仲有幾個設定；<b>Copy</b> 會將成份報告放入 clipboard，報告問題嗰陣可以貼落 email 或者 Teams。</p><table><tr><th>設定</th><th>選擇</th><th>做乜</th></tr><tr><td><b>Streaming</b></td><td>automatic / on / off</td><td>大 model 跟住視圖需要一嚿嚿攞（automatic = 手機同平板開）</td></tr><tr><td><b>Memory budget</b></td><td>automatic / 150 至 1500 MB</td><td>部機留幾多幾何先放走睇唔到嘅部分</td></tr><tr><td><b>Drawing with</b></td><td>WebGL（標準）/ WebGPU（試驗）</td><td>繪圖方法；轉嘅時候會 reload。除非叫你試，否則用 WebGL</td></tr><tr><td><b>While moving</b></td><td>follow the frame rate / always full quality</td><td>郁嘅時候 frame rate 跌，就畫輕啲嘅郁動畫面；停定嘅畫面永遠係全質素</td></tr></table><p>Streaming 同 memory budget 要 reload 個版先生效。狀態列亦會顯示即時 frame rate、畫咗幾多三角形同顯示卡記憶體；「moving step 1 to 4」即係用緊輕啲嘅郁動畫面。</p><p><b>載入速度</b></p><ul><li>Viewer 嘅檔案會壓縮咗先傳（3D library 由 4.8 MB 變 0.7 MB），而且你個瀏覽器會留低：由第二次開始，版面喺你自己部電腦打開，只有資料由 server 嚟。</li><li>每一版載入嗰陣會一次過攞晒佢要嘅資料。Messenger 同 Projects 版仲會即刻顯示上次見到嘅嘢，然後先更新。</li><li>Viewer 更新之後，改咗嘅檔案會自己重新攞；唔會新舊混埋。</li></ul>"},{"id":"s70","ch":"俾 BIM coordinator：由 Revit publish","h":"俾 BIM coordinator：由 Revit publish","lv":2,"html":"<p>一個掣 <b>Publish to Viewer</b> 就會 export sheet 同 3D model 再 upload；其他掣係俾你逐步自己做，或者夜晚自動做。</p>"},{"id":"s71","ch":"俾 BIM coordinator：由 Revit publish","h":"設定（每部電腦一次）","lv":3,"html":"<ul><li>安裝 LWK pyRevit extension。佢會加一個 <b>LWK</b> tab，有 <b>Viewer &amp; Issues</b> panel：<b>Publish to Viewer</b>、<b>LWK Issues</b> 同 <b>Viewer tools</b> 下拉選單。</li><li>Sign in 一次（喺 <b>LWK Issues</b> 或者 <b>Publish</b>）。登入會保留一年，夜晚 upload 都照做得。</li><li>Upload 去現有 project 你要係佢嘅 <b>project admin</b>；新 project 名要 <b>site admin</b>。</li></ul>"},{"id":"s72","ch":"俾 BIM coordinator：由 Revit publish","h":"Publish to Viewer","lv":3,"html":"<ol><li>喺 Revit 打開 model，撳 <b>Publish to Viewer</b>。</li><li><b>Where：</b> 揀 <b>Viewer project</b>（或者打個新名：英文字母、數字、- 同 _），檢查 <b>Server</b> 顯示「signed in」，同埋 <b>Export folder</b>。</li><li><b>What：</b> 剔 <b>3D model (fast format, with its linked models)</b>，揀細節：<b>Coarse (lightest)</b>、<b>Medium (recommended)</b> 或者 <b>Fine (most detail)</b>。剔 <b>Sheets</b>，揀 <b>All sheets</b>、<b>A Revit sheet set</b> 或者 <b>These sheets</b>。<b>Keep sheets published before</b> 會保留之前 publish 過、但唔喺今次選擇入面嘅 sheet。</li><li><b>Then：</b> <b>Send to the viewer server (only what changed)</b>、<b>Open it in the browser when done</b>，可以揀 <b>Publish this model again every night at</b> 01:00（想嘅話只限星期一至五；只限 ACC model）。</li><li>撳 <b>Publish</b>。你揀嘅嘢會為呢個 model 記住。Revit model 唔會被改或者儲存。</li></ol><p>Upload 完之後 server 要幾分鐘整手機版同讀 sheet 嘅字。Server 會保留每張 sheet PDF 最近 12 個版本（俾 <b>Compare</b> 用），同每個 3D model 最近 2 個（俾 <b>Compare with previous export</b> 用）。</p>"},{"id":"s73","ch":"俾 BIM coordinator：由 Revit publish","h":"Viewer tools 下拉選單","lv":3,"html":"<table><tr><th>掣</th><th>用嚟</th></tr><tr><td><b>Fast 3D Export</b></td><td>只 export 3D model（同 link），用 fast 格式；sheet 保留</td></tr><tr><td><b>Export Viewer</b></td><td>自己 export sheet 同 manifest（舊 IFC 方法）</td></tr><tr><td><b>Upload Now</b></td><td>再將上次 export 傳去 server</td></tr><tr><td><b>Add Model</b></td><td>登記一個 ACC model 做自動 export：sheet、IFC schema、唔要嘅 category、標準層組</td></tr><tr><td><b>Run Export</b></td><td>即刻 export 同 upload 所有登記咗嘅 model（Shift-click：只做打開緊嗰個）</td></tr><tr><td><b>Night Export</b></td><td>排每晚或者平日夜晚做、取消排程，或者睇狀態同 log</td></tr><tr><td><b>Export Link</b></td><td>Export 一個自動 export 開唔到嘅 link（例如舊版本嘅 cloud model）</td></tr><tr><td><b>Link Places</b></td><td>將每個 link instance 嘅位置寫入 export folder</td></tr><tr><td><b>Test Links</b></td><td>快速檢查放咗多過一次嘅 link</td></tr></table><p><b>夜晚 export 需要：</b> 部電腦開住同登入咗（鎖咗 screen 冇問題）、排咗嘅時間 Revit 要閂咗、Revit 登入咗 Autodesk。每個 model 預大約 15 分鐘。Log 喺 %APPDATA%\\LWK\\nightly。</p><ul><li>Model 嘅每個 workset 都會逐個名打開，冇 load 嘅 link 會 load 返。如果仲有 workset 閂住，或者 3D model 出咗嚟係空嘅，viewer 會<b>保留上次好嘅 3D model</b>（sheet 照傳），log 最尾寫 <b>result FAILED</b> 同原因。</li><li>已知嘅對話框會自動答，唔會令夜晚 export 停住：DWG 嘅 paper space 冇嘢（Yes）、DWG <b>extents greater than 1E9</b>（OK：照樣 import，只係切走好遠嗰部分）、DWG import 嘅通知例如 <b>Elements Lost on Import</b>（Close）、<b>External Tools - Add-in Assembly Not Found</b> 同其他 add-in 嘅 <b>搵唔到 xxx.dll</b> 訊息（Close），同埋所有得一個掣嘅訊息。LWK 工具未載入之前、或者開 model 期間彈出嘅對話框，由 launcher 嘅 watcher 處理，佢會搵晒嗰個 Revit 嘅所有視窗。每個對話框都會寫入 nightly\\dialogs.log。更新之後，下次你自己開 Revit 時，launcher 同 watcher 會自動更新。最好係喺嗰部電腦修好或者移除壞咗嘅 add-in。</li><li><b>Revit 2023-2026（watcher 2026-11-31）：</b> launcher 嘅 watcher 而家亦會睇到新式嘅 WPF 視窗，並按掣上嘅字去撳：未簽署嘅 add-in 撳 <b>Load Once</b>、缺少連結撳 <b>Ignore and continue opening the project</b>、缺少第三方 updater 撳 <b>Continue working with the file</b>，What's New 之類嘅通知就 Close。佢永遠唔會撳 <b>Cancel</b>、<b>Do Not Load</b> 或者 <b>Always Load</b> - 得一個 Cancel 掣嘅進度視窗會由佢，所以開緊嘅 model 唔會被停。佢唔認識嘅對話框會寫入 nightly\\dialogs.log，相片放喺 nightly\\dialogs\\ - 兩樣都傳俾我哋，就可以加規則。更新之後，請喺每部電腦開 <b>Auto-export</b>，<b>儲存一次排程</b>：咁先會寫入新嘅 launcher 同 watcher。</li><li><b>只上載有改動嘅檔案（2026-12-08 更新）：</b> 冇改過嘅 3D model 會出同上一晚一模一樣嘅檔案；圖紙冇改過嘅 sheet PDF（Revit 每次都會寫入新日期）亦會認得係同一張——兩樣都唔會再上載。Log 會寫例如「upload: sending 6 of 108 file(s), 12.4 MB - the rest unchanged (40 sheet PDF(s) exported again with only their dates changed)」。要喺部 PC 更新 add-in（LWK.extension）；更新後第一晚仍然會全部上載一次。</li><li><b>夜晚只發佈有改動嘅 model：</b> 開咗 model 之後，夜晚 run 會讀 model 同每個 link model 嘅版本（Revit 每次儲存都有編號）。如果上次發佈之後一個都冇再儲存過、job 設定又一樣，就唔會 export，夜晚 log 會寫 <b>UNCHANGED</b>。Test run、自己撳 Run Export、改咗設定或者更新咗工具，都一定會發佈。仍然要先開 model 先讀到版本。</li><li><b>時間：</b> 每個 Revit 版本最多可以行 3 個鐘（nightly_schedule.json 嘅 limit_hours）；版本會一個跟一個咁行（2023、2024、2025），嗰部電腦已經開咗嘅 Revit 版本，當晚會跳過。夜晚 run 最好早啲開始（例如 01:00），等所有版本喺朝早有人開 Revit 之前做完。</li></ul>"},{"id":"s74","ch":"俾 BIM coordinator：由 Revit publish","h":"Revit 入面嘅 LWK Issues 視窗","lv":3,"html":"<ul><li>列出一個 project 喺 viewer 嘅 issue：<b>Show</b> 未完成同做緊、派俾我嘅，或者全部；可以搜尋；欄有 #、Title、Type、Status、Priority、Assigned to、Due、Where。</li><li><b>Go to issue</b>（或者 double-click）會打開一個私人 3D 視圖「LWK Issue - 你個名」，有 section box 圍住個 issue，或者 zoom 去 sheet。隔籬有 <b>Open its plan view</b> 同 <b>Open in web viewer</b>。</li><li><b>Place pins for the list</b> / <b>Remove pins</b> 喺 workset「LWK Issues」加「LWK #n」標記。<b>Clouds on sheets</b> 喺 revision「LWK Viewer issues」下面加 revision cloud。</li><li>揀個狀態及／或打個 comment，然後 <b>Send to viewer</b>：會用你個名出現喺網上 viewer。</li></ul>"},{"id":"s75","ch":"俾 BIM coordinator：由 Revit publish","h":"Revit 元件同 LWK add-in","lv":3,"html":"<ul><li>喺 publish 咗嘅 model 3D 入面開嘅每個 issue 都帶住元件嘅 ElementId 同 UniqueId。Review 嘅人可以 copy 啲 id 用 <b>Manage &gt; Select by ID</b>，BCF export 會當 AuthoringToolId 帶埋佢哋。</li><li>Viewer 入面嘅 <b>Show in Revit</b> 會喺 server 留低一個要求俾 add-in 攞；add-in 亦可以將 Revit 入面揀咗嘅嘢傳去 viewer。Add-in 要做乜寫咗喺 <b>server/REVIT_ADDIN_API.md</b>，俾負責維護佢嘅人睇。</li></ul>"},{"id":"s76","ch":"俾 admin 嘅","h":"俾 admin 嘅","lv":2,"html":"<p>Project admin 喺 <b>Admin</b> 版管理自己 project 嘅人同設定；site admin 仲管理 account、所有 project、回收站同裝置報告。</p>"},{"id":"s77","ch":"俾 admin 嘅","h":"角色","lv":3,"html":"<table><tr><th>角色</th><th>可以</th></tr><tr><td><b>Viewer</b></td><td>乜都睇得；唔可以加或者改 issue 同 comment</td></tr><tr><td><b>Member</b></td><td>開同改 issue 同 comment；只可以刪自己嘅</td></tr><tr><td><b>Publisher</b></td><td>Member 做得嘅全部，加上由 Revit publish sheet 同 3D model（LWK tab &gt; <b>Publish to Viewer</b>）</td></tr><tr><td><b>Project admin</b></td><td>Publisher 做得嘅全部，加上管理 project 成員、改或者刪任何嘢、無視 layer 鎖、upload model</td></tr><tr><td><b>Site admin</b></td><td>所有 project；加、停用同 reset account；開、刪同還原 project</td></tr></table><p>每個 project 一定要留最少一個 project admin。</p>"},{"id":"s78","ch":"俾 admin 嘅","h":"Project 同成員","lv":3,"html":"<ul><li><b>Add people to this project：</b> 搜尋，用 <b>team</b>、<b>office</b> 或者 <b>company</b> 篩選，剔幾個人（或者 <b>Select all shown</b>），揀 Role 再撳 <b>Add N people</b>；或者填 <b>Someone without an account yet</b>（Email、Name、Office、Company、Role）再撳 <b>Create and add</b>。臨時密碼只會顯示<b>一次</b>。</li><li>用 <b>Email invitation</b>（打開你自己嘅 Outlook）或者 <b>Copy invitation</b> 傳俾佢。佢第一次 sign in 要揀自己嘅密碼。</li><li>喺成員表改角色，或者 <b>Remove</b> 一個人（佢嘅 issue 同 comment 會留低）。</li><li><b>Teams channel：</b> 貼 Teams Workflow webhook 網址，<b>Save</b>，<b>Send a test</b>，再揀每週總結嘅日子同鐘數（香港時間）。</li><li><b>Markup layers：</b> 每個 layer 設定邊個改得（所有成員、只限 project admin，或者指定嘅人）、邊個睇得到，同埋開頭係咪隱藏。</li><li><b>Phones and tablets：</b> 如果手機話冇手機版，<b>Prepare this project now</b> 會重新整；<b>Show progress</b>（site admin）顯示 server 背後做緊嘅嘢。</li></ul>"},{"id":"s79","ch":"俾 admin 嘅","h":"Projects（Admin > Projects and members）","lv":3,"html":"<ul><li><b>+ New project</b>：<b>Project name</b>（例如 HKA-P-01681-ARC - SKW；code 會由佢攞）、<b>Code</b>、<b>Status</b>、<b>Group / team</b>、<b>Owners</b>，同 <b>Folders and files</b>（OneDrive、SharePoint 或者 ACC 連結）。<b>Import</b> 讀由 Lark Base 或者 Excel export 嘅 project 表。</li><li><b>Models and sheets：</b> 顯示呢個 job 嘅 viewer project（export folder）。一個 job 有幾個 Revit model 同 sheet set（例如 Site 1 同 Site 2），就 Ctrl+click 揀幾個。揀一個其他地方用緊嘅會搬嚟呢度；server 單獨為佢整嘅項目會移除，佢嘅 task group 會跟住搬過嚟。</li><li>成員屬於每一個部分（係佢哋令人可以打開嗰個 model）。有幾個部分嘅話，成員表上面會出 <b>Part</b> 選擇。</li><li><b>Remove from Projects</b> 將一個 job 拎走出 Projects 版；佢嘅 task、issue、model 同檔案都會留低。</li></ul>"},{"id":"s80","ch":"俾 admin 嘅","h":"只限 site admin","lv":3,"html":"<ul><li><b>People：</b> 加 account、<b>Reset password</b>、<b>Make / Remove site admin</b>、<b>Deactivate / Reactivate</b>（會喺所有地方 sign out 嗰個人）、<b>Edit</b>、<b>Delete</b>（整錯咗嘅 account 用）。</li><li><b>Delete project ...：</b> 打個 project 名確認。Model、sheet、issue、markup 同成員會搬去 server 嘅回收站；喺回收站清單撳 <b>Restore</b> 會全部放返，只要個名未被再用。</li><li><b>Devices：</b> 3D 版由每部裝置傳嚟嘅報告：載入咗乜、最高記憶體、frame rate、卡頓同 crash。篩選 crash 或者手機同平板，就知 viewer 喺邊度辛苦。</li><li><b>Speed（網站管理員）：</b> 伺服器回應有幾快、用家要等幾耐，一直都喺度量度。<b>Days</b>：回應數量、一般同最慢嘅時間，同 <b>stalls（停頓）</b> - 伺服器停咗回應所有人嘅時刻（好似 viewer 顯示 Offline 嗰陣）。每次停頓都會講伺服器當時忙緊乜：傳俾我哋就可以修正嗰部分。<b>Pages, as people waited</b>：每個版喺用家自己部機上要幾耐先用得（第一張圖紙或者模型顯示咗），同佢最慢嘅資料。<b>Server answers</b> 同 <b>Slow answers</b>（超過 2 秒）顯示邊部分用咗時間。Chat 等緊新訊息嘅請求會計數，但唔當慢。</li><li><b>Server：</b> email 要 server 設定好 LWK_SMTP_。如果 server 前面嘅 proxy 處理唔到壓縮咗、瀏覽器保留嘅檔案，用 --plain-assets 開 server（或者喺 run.bat 設 PLAIN_ASSETS=1）。</li></ul>"},{"id":"s81","ch":"解決問題同常見問題","h":"解決問題同常見問題","lv":2,"html":"<p>大部分問題都係舊嘅 cache 版面、網絡慢或者部機記憶體唔夠；下面個表寫咗第一樣要試嘅嘢。</p><table><tr><th>問題</th><th>試吓咁</th></tr><tr><td>啲嘢好似舊咗，或者冇咗新功能</td><td>睇左上角「LWK Viewer」隔籬嘅版本；按 Ctrl+F5（Windows）或者 Cmd+Shift+R（Mac）。iPad 就閂咗個 tab 再開過</td></tr><tr><td>「Wrong email or password」</td><td>檢查 email；叫 admin <b>Reset password</b>。試咗 10 次之後要等 15 分鐘</td></tr><tr><td>「You are not a member of this project」</td><td>叫 project admin 加你</td></tr><tr><td>我加唔到或者改唔到 issue</td><td>你喺呢個 project 係 <b>Viewer</b>；叫 project admin 俾你做 Member</td></tr><tr><td>Publish to Viewer 話「You need to be a Publisher or project admin」</td><td>你喺嗰個 project 係 <b>Member</b>（或者 Viewer）。叫 project admin 開 <b>Admin</b>、揀個 project，喺成員表將你嘅角色改做 <b>Publisher</b></td></tr><tr><td>「N waiting to save」</td><td>你個網絡斷咗。留住個版唔好閂；網絡返嚟就會儲存</td></tr><tr><td>Header 顯示 <b>Offline</b>（或者 <b>Server busy</b>）</td><td>將滑鼠放上去睇原因。<b>The server did not answer：</b> 喺 server 嗰部電腦檢查 server 個視窗仲開住（再開 <b>server\\run.bat</b>，每次更新之後都要），喺公司外面用連結就要開住 <b>tunnel.bat</b>；喺 server 部電腦開 http://127.0.0.1:8713/api/ping 應該有回應。<b>Server busy：</b> server 開住但答得太慢，會自己好返；成日咁就叫 admin 睇 <b>Admin &gt; Performance</b></td></tr><tr><td>最新嘅 sheet 或者 model 唔見</td><td>Publish 可能仲做緊，或者 server 準備緊；等幾分鐘再 reload</td></tr><tr><td>電腦上面 3D 好慢或者一頓頓</td><td>唔剔唔使用嘅 model、用 floor plan、檢查 <b>While moving</b> 係「follow the frame rate」</td></tr><tr><td>iPad 或者 iPhone 自己 reload 個版</td><td>記憶體唔夠：開少啲 model、留喺一層、開住 <b>Light mode</b>；傳 Performance 報告</td></tr><tr><td>喺 section 入面撳唔到一個元件</td><td>只有切面睇得到嗰邊揀得；郁吓切面或者用 Model browser</td></tr><tr><td>量度 snap 錯嘢</td><td>Zoom 近啲；停定等 label 顯示 <b>corner</b>、<b>midpoint</b> 或者 <b>edge</b></td></tr><tr><td>Revit link 唔見咗或者放錯位</td><td>檢查 <b>Apply link transforms</b> 開咗；話俾 BIM coordinator 知</td></tr><tr><td>轉咗 WebGPU 之後版面唔同咗</td><td>喺 Performance 撳 <b>Drawing with</b> 轉返 WebGL（或者喺網址加一次 &amp;gpu=webgl）</td></tr><tr><td>經 VPN 或者喺屋企開版面好慢</td><td>第二次會快好多（啲檔案會留喺你個瀏覽器）。如果第一次開一直都慢，叫 IT 喺 server 嘅 proxy 開 HTTP/2</td></tr><tr><td>搜尋乜都搵唔到</td><td>最少打 2 個字；每個字都要對到。你只會見到你係成員嘅 project、list 同 chat</td></tr><tr><td>「Revit's LWK add-in is not listening」</td><td>已經改為 copy 咗啲 id：喺 Revit 用 <b>Manage &gt; Select by ID</b> 貼上</td></tr><tr><td>WhatsApp import：「does not look like a WhatsApp chat export」</td><td>用 WhatsApp 嘅 <b>Export chat</b> 檔（.txt 或者 .zip），唔好用截圖或者轉發嘅訊息</td></tr><tr><td>Task 或者訊息連結打開唔到嘢</td><td>你可能唔係嗰個 list、chat 或者 project 嘅成員；問佢嘅 owner</td></tr><tr><td>訊息或者 chat 冇 Delete</td><td>訊息只有發嘅人刪得。Group 由佢嘅 admin 刪，project channel 同 topic 由 project 嘅 admin 刪</td></tr></table><p><b>報告問題嗰陣</b>請傳：project、版面（Sheets 定 3D）、你部機同瀏覽器、你做咗乜、截圖，3D 版就加埋 <b>Performance → Copy</b> 報告。</p><p><b>常見問題</b></p><ul><li><b>會唔會改到 Revit model？</b> 唔會。Publish 只係讀個 model。只有 LWK Issues 視窗會加 pin 或者 cloud，而且係你叫佢先會做。</li><li><b>邊個睇到我嘅 markup？</b> Project 所有人，除非個 markup 喺 admin 限制咗嘅 layer 上面。</li><li><b>會唔會發 email？</b> 會，只要 server 設定好 mail：派 task、@mention、你 follow 緊嘅 task 有 comment 同完成，仲有每日到期 task 清單。Teams 照舊會 post。</li><li><b>可唔可以離線用？</b> 可以，用下載咗落部機嘅 project（睇「離線工作」）。短暫斷線都冇問題：改動會等住，網絡返嚟就儲存。</li><li><b>Messenger 係咪取代 WhatsApp？</b> 佢係用嚟做 project 嘢，就喺圖則同 task 隔籬。訊息可以傳去 WhatsApp，亦可以由 WhatsApp 帶入嚟，但兩邊唔會自動同步。</li><li><b>顧問用唔用得？</b> 用得，用佢哋自己嘅 account，通常只係嗰個 project 嘅 <b>Viewer</b> 或者 <b>Member</b>。</li></ul>"},{"id":"s82","ch":"快捷鍵一覽","h":"快捷鍵一覽","lv":2,"html":"<p>印咗呢個表，或者頭一個禮拜放喺 screen 隔籬。</p><table><tr><th>喺邊</th><th>鍵或者掣</th><th>做乜</th></tr><tr><td>3D</td><td>右掣拖</td><td>轉</td></tr><tr><td>3D</td><td>中間掣拖</td><td>Pan</td></tr><tr><td>3D</td><td>滑鼠轆</td><td>向住游標 zoom</td></tr><tr><td>3D</td><td>Double-click</td><td>對準嗰個面</td></tr><tr><td>3D</td><td>右鍵撳（唔拖）</td><td>選單，同將轉嘅中心搬去嗰度</td></tr><tr><td>3D</td><td>Page Up / Page Down</td><td>上一層／下一層</td></tr><tr><td>3D</td><td>Esc</td><td>取消量度、停止行、閂選單</td></tr><tr><td>3D 量度</td><td>Shift</td><td>下一點開／熄 Straight</td></tr><tr><td>3D 行</td><td>W A S D、↑ ↓</td><td>行同打側行</td></tr><tr><td>3D 行</td><td>← →</td><td>轉身</td></tr><tr><td>3D 行</td><td>Shift / Q / E</td><td>快啲／降／升（Gravity 熄咗）</td></tr><tr><td>Sheets</td><td>滑鼠轆／中間掣拖</td><td>Zoom / pan</td></tr><tr><td>Sheets</td><td>Page Down / Page Up</td><td>下一張／上一張 sheet</td></tr><tr><td>Sheets</td><td>V / H</td><td>Select 工具／Pan 工具</td></tr><tr><td>Sheets</td><td>Enter、Esc、Backspace</td><td>Polyline 完成、結束，或者刪最後一點</td></tr><tr><td>Sheets</td><td>Delete</td><td>刪揀咗嘅 markup</td></tr><tr><td>Sheets</td><td>Ctrl+A</td><td>揀晒張 sheet 嘅 markup</td></tr><tr><td>Sheets</td><td>Ctrl+C / Ctrl+V</td><td>Copy／貼 markup（貼去另一張 sheet 都得）</td></tr><tr><td>Sheets</td><td>Ctrl+Z / Ctrl+Y</td><td>Undo / redo</td></tr><tr><td>Sheets</td><td>R / Shift+R</td><td>揀咗嘅順時針／逆時針轉 90°</td></tr><tr><td>Sheets compare</td><td>N / Shift+N</td><td>下一個／上一個改動</td></tr><tr><td>每一版</td><td>Ctrl+K 或者 /</td><td>搜尋所有嘢</td></tr><tr><td>搜尋</td><td>↑ ↓、Enter、Esc</td><td>移動、打開、閂</td></tr><tr><td>Tasks</td><td>K / J</td><td>上一個／下一個 task</td></tr><tr><td>Messenger</td><td>Enter / Ctrl+Enter</td><td>換行／發送</td></tr><tr><td>Messenger</td><td>@ # ! $ %</td><td>Mention 人／連結 task、issue、sheet、3D 視圖</td></tr><tr><td>Messenger</td><td>Ctrl+Enter / Esc（改緊訊息）</td><td>儲存／取消改訊息</td></tr><tr><td>Messenger</td><td>Ctrl+B / Ctrl+I / Ctrl+Shift+X</td><td>粗體／斜體／刪除線</td></tr></table>"},{"id":"s83","ch":"意見同先試乜","h":"意見同先試乜","lv":2,"html":"<p>呢個係試用版：請試吓下面啲嘢，話俾我哋知乜嘢好用、乜嘢搞唔清、仲欠乜。</p><ul><li>☐ Sign in 同改密碼</li><li>☐ 搜尋一個房名或者 note 搵一張 sheet</li><li>☐ 喺 sheet 上面畫一個 cloud 加文字，再變成 issue</li><li>☐ 喺 3D 打開同一個位置，切一個 floor plan</li><li>☐ 開住 <b>Straight</b>，喺 plan 量一間房牆到牆</li><li>☐ 喺 3D 開一個 issue，派俾同事，再用 @mention 寫 comment</li><li>☐ 試 <b>2D + 3D</b>，一路行走廊一路睇 plan</li><li>☐ 喺 iPad 或者 iPhone 打開 viewer 睇一層</li><li>☐ 由你嘅測試 issue 開一個 task，然後喺 Tasks 版完成佢同解決個 issue</li><li>☐ 喺你 project 嘅 channel 發一條有 # task 同 $ sheet 連結嘅訊息</li><li>☐ 喺你嘅 project channel 開一個 topic，pin 一條訊息，再發一個 poll 同一個 event</li><li>☐ 用 Ctrl+K 搵你嘅測試 issue</li><li>☐ 喺 3D 撳一個元件，撳 Copy Revit ID，再喺 Revit 用 Select by ID 揀中佢</li><li>☐ 試完刪咗你嘅測試 issue 同 task</li></ul><p>意見、問題同問題報告請傳去 [名 / Teams channel]。同速度或者 crash 有關嘅，請夾埋 Performance 報告。</p>"}]};
